  ('july-30-part-1', 'july-30-part-1-draft-speaking-4', 23, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-30-part-1-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"hope","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the hope meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “早く元気になるといいですね。”.","hintJa":"相手への現実的な願いにも hope を使います。","explanation":"Model: “I hope you feel better soon.” (早く元気になるといいですね。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I hope you feel better soon.」（早く元気になるといいですね。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I hope you feel better soon.","speakJa":"早く元気になるといいですね。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-1', 'july-30-part-1-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-30-part-1-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"wish now","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the wish now meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。”.","hintJa":"今の天気と反対の願いを表します。","explanation":"Model: “I wish the weather were cooler.” (もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I wish the weather were cooler.」（もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I wish the weather were cooler.","speakJa":"もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-1', 'july-30-part-1-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-30-part-1-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"hope","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the hope meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “早く元気になるといいですね。”.","hintJa":"相手への現実的な願いにも hope を使います。","explanation":"“I hope you feel better soon.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「I hope you feel better soon.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: I wish I hadn’t said that.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: あんなことを言わなければよかった。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I hope you feel better soon.","jp":"早く元気になるといいですね。"},{"id":"b","en":"I wish the weather were cooler.","jp":"もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。"},{"id":"c","en":"I hope everything goes well.","jp":"すべてうまくいくといいですね。"},{"id":"d","en":"I wish I had studied harder.","jp":"もっと一生懸命勉強しておけばよかった。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-1', 'july-30-part-1-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-30-part-1-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"wish now","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the wish now meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。”.","hintJa":"今の天気と反対の願いを表します。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “I wish the weather were cooler.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「I wish the weather were cooler.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"I wish the weather cooler.","accepted":["I wish the weather were cooler."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-1', 'july-30-part-1-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-1-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"hope","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the hope meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “また会えるといいですね。”.","hintJa":"可能性のある未来には hope + can が自然です。","explanation":"“I hope we can meet again.” directly expresses “また会えるといいですね。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「I hope we can meet again.」が「また会えるといいですね。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: また会えるといいですね。","promptJa":"「また会えるといいですね。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I hope we can meet again.","jp":"また会えるといいですね。"},{"id":"b","en":"I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.","jp":"来年マレーシアを訪れられるといいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I wish I had more free time.","jp":"もっと自由な時間があればいいのに。"},{"id":"d","en":"I wish I had called her earlier.","jp":"もっと早く彼女に電話すればよかった。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-1', 'july-30-part-1-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-1-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"hope","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Look for a realistic future travel hope, not regret about the past.","hintJa":"過去の後悔ではなく、実現できそうな未来の旅行への希望を見ましょう。","explanation":"“I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.” is correct. The future calendar, travel pictures and hopeful expression show a possible visit next year. “I hope everything goes well.” does not fit because that sentence means “すべてうまくいくといいですね。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I wish I had studied harder.” does not fit because that sentence means “もっと一生懸命勉強しておけばよかった。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I hope you feel better soon.” does not fit because that sentence means “早く元気になるといいですね。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.」（来年マレーシアを訪れられるといいです。）です。未来のカレンダー、旅行写真、希望に満ちた表情が来年の訪問を示しています。 「I hope everything goes well.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「すべてうまくいくといいですね。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I wish I had studied harder.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「もっと一生懸命勉強しておけばよかった。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I hope you feel better soon.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「早く元気になるといいですね。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.","jp":"来年マレーシアを訪れられるといいです。"},{"id":"b","en":"I hope everything goes well.","jp":"すべてうまくいくといいですね。"},{"id":"c","en":"I wish I had studied harder.","jp":"もっと一生懸命勉強しておけばよかった。"},{"id":"d","en":"I hope you feel better soon.","jp":"早く元気になるといいですね。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-30-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A learner happily imagines visiting Malaysia next year.","visualAssetId":"july-30-part-1-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-1', 'july-30-part-1-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-1-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"wish now","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Compare the person’s real location with the place in the thought bubble.","hintJa":"本人が実際にいる場所と、吹き出しの中で願っている場所を比べましょう。","explanation":"“I wish I were in Malaysia now.” is correct. The person is at home but imagines being in Malaysia at the present moment. “I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.” does not fit because that sentence means “来年マレーシアを訪れられるといいです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I wish I had gone with you.” does not fit because that sentence means “あなたと一緒に行けばよかった。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I hope we can meet again.” does not fit because that sentence means “また会えるといいですね。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I wish I were in Malaysia now.」（今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。）です。本人は自宅にいますが、今マレーシアにいる自分を想像しています。 「I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「来年マレーシアを訪れられるといいです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I wish I had gone with you.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「あなたと一緒に行けばよかった。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I hope we can meet again.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「また会えるといいですね。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I wish I were in Malaysia now.","jp":"今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。"},{"id":"b","en":"I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.","jp":"来年マレーシアを訪れられるといいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I wish I had gone with you.","jp":"あなたと一緒に行けばよかった。"},{"id":"d","en":"I hope we can meet again.","jp":"また会えるといいですね。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-30-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A person at home wishes they were in Malaysia now.","visualAssetId":"july-30-part-1-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-1', 'july-30-part-1-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-1-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"wish + could","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Notice the contrast between hesitant speech and the confident ability being wished for.","hintJa":"ためらって話す現実と、願っている自信ある話し方の対比に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I wish I could speak English more confidently.” is correct. The learner wants a speaking ability they do not yet feel they have. “I wish I were in Malaysia now.” does not fit because that sentence means “今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I wish I had called her earlier.” does not fit because that sentence means “もっと早く彼女に電話すればよかった。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I wish the weather were cooler.” does not fit because that sentence means “もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I wish I could speak English more confidently.」（もっと自信を持って英語を話せたらいいのに。）です。学習者は、まだ十分に持てていない英語を話す自信を願っています。 「I wish I were in Malaysia now.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I wish I had called her earlier.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「もっと早く彼女に電話すればよかった。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I wish the weather were cooler.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I wish I could speak English more confidently.","jp":"もっと自信を持って英語を話せたらいいのに。"},{"id":"b","en":"I wish I were in Malaysia now.","jp":"今マレーシアにいたらいいのに。"},{"id":"c","en":"I wish I had called her earlier.","jp":"もっと早く彼女に電話すればよかった。"},{"id":"d","en":"I wish the weather were cooler.","jp":"もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-30-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"An English learner wishes they could speak more confidently.","visualAssetId":"july-30-part-1-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-1', 'july-30-part-1-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-1-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"past regret","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The clock and unused phone show a missed action in the past.","hintJa":"時計と使われなかった電話から、過去にしなかった行動を考えましょう。","explanation":"“I wish I had called her earlier.” is correct. The late time and regretful look show that the earlier call was never made. “I hope everything goes well.” does not fit because that sentence means “すべてうまくいくといいですね。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I wish I could speak English more confidently.” does not fit because that sentence means “もっと自信を持って英語を話せたらいいのに。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I hope you feel better soon.” does not fit because that sentence means “早く元気になるといいですね。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I wish I had called her earlier.」（もっと早く彼女に電話すればよかった。）です。遅い時刻と後悔した表情が、もっと早い電話をしなかったことを示しています。 「I hope everything goes well.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「すべてうまくいくといいですね。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I wish I could speak English more confidently.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「もっと自信を持って英語を話せたらいいのに。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I hope you feel better soon.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「早く元気になるといいですね。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I wish I had called her earlier.","jp":"もっと早く彼女に電話すればよかった。"},{"id":"b","en":"I hope everything goes well.","jp":"すべてうまくいくといいですね。"},{"id":"c","en":"I wish I could speak English more confidently.","jp":"もっと自信を持って英語を話せたらいいのに。"},{"id":"d","en":"I hope you feel better soon.","jp":"早く元気になるといいですね。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-30-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"A person regrets not calling someone earlier.","visualAssetId":"july-30-part-1-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-1', 'july-30-part-1-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-1-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"wish now","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Look for a present weather condition the person wants to be different.","hintJa":"今の天気について、本人が違ってほしいと願っている状態を見ましょう。","explanation":"“I wish the weather were cooler.” is correct. The person is hot now and imagines cooler, more comfortable weather. “I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.” does not fit because that sentence means “来年マレーシアを訪れられるといいです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I wish I had more free time.” does not fit because that sentence means “もっと自由な時間があればいいのに。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I wish I hadn’t said that.” does not fit because that sentence means “あんなことを言わなければよかった。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I wish the weather were cooler.」（もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。）です。本人は今暑がっており、もっと涼しく快適な天気を想像しています。 「I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「来年マレーシアを訪れられるといいです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I wish I had more free time.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「もっと自由な時間があればいいのに。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I wish I hadn’t said that.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「あんなことを言わなければよかった。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I wish the weather were cooler.","jp":"もっと涼しい天気ならいいのに。"},{"id":"b","en":"I hope I can visit Malaysia next year.","jp":"来年マレーシアを訪れられるといいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I wish I had more free time.","jp":"もっと自由な時間があればいいのに。"},{"id":"d","en":"I wish I hadn’t said that.","jp":"あんなことを言わなければよかった。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-30-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A person wishes the hot weather were cooler.","visualAssetId":"july-30-part-1-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はもう朝食を食べました。”.","hintJa":"already は通常 have と過去分詞の間に置きます。","explanation":"“I have already eaten breakfast.” is the sentence that means “私はもう朝食を食べました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I have already eaten breakfast.」が「私はもう朝食を食べました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 私はもう朝食を食べました。","promptJa":"「私はもう朝食を食べました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I have already eaten breakfast.","jp":"私はもう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t eaten dinner yet.","jp":"私はまだ夕食を食べていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I had already eaten when you arrived.","jp":"あなたが着いた時には、私はもう食べ終えていました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I had been there before.","jp":"私は以前そこへ行ったことがありました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はまだ夕食を食べていません。”.","hintJa":"yet は否定文では通常、文末に置きます。","explanation":"“I haven’t eaten dinner yet.” is the sentence that means “私はまだ夕食を食べていません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I haven’t eaten dinner yet.」が「私はまだ夕食を食べていません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 私はまだ夕食を食べていません。","promptJa":"「私はまだ夕食を食べていません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I haven’t eaten dinner yet.","jp":"私はまだ夕食を食べていません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve just arrived home.","jp":"私はたった今家に着きました。"},{"id":"c","en":"She had left before I called.","jp":"私が電話する前に、彼女は出発していました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I wish I had been born there.","jp":"そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はたった今家に着きました。”.","hintJa":"just は have と過去分詞の間です。","explanation":"“I’ve just arrived home.” is the sentence that means “私はたった今家に着きました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I’ve just arrived home.」が「私はたった今家に着きました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 私はたった今家に着きました。","promptJa":"「私はたった今家に着きました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve just arrived home.","jp":"私はたった今家に着きました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I have lived here since 2016.","jp":"私は2016年からここに住んでいます。"},{"id":"c","en":"He had finished the report by noon.","jp":"彼は正午までにレポートを終えていました。"},{"id":"d","en":"She had been tired before the meeting started.","jp":"会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
