  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-speaking-4', 23, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"be born","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the be born meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。”.","hintJa":"be born の過去完了は had been born です。","explanation":"Model: “I wish I had been born there.” (そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I wish I had been born there.」（そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I wish I had been born there.","speakJa":"そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"had been","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the had been meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。”.","hintJa":"had been + 形容詞で、過去の基準時より前の状態を表せます。","explanation":"Model: “She had been tired before the meeting started.” (会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「She had been tired before the meeting started.」（会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"She had been tired before the meeting started.","speakJa":"会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"be born","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the be born meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。”.","hintJa":"be born の過去完了は had been born です。","explanation":"“I wish I had been born there.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「I wish I had been born there.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: I had been there before.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: 私は以前そこへ行ったことがありました。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I wish I had been born there.","jp":"そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。"},{"id":"b","en":"She had been tired before the meeting started.","jp":"会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I haven’t eaten dinner yet.","jp":"私はまだ夕食を食べていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"She had left before I called.","jp":"私が電話する前に、彼女は出発していました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"had been","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the had been meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。”.","hintJa":"had been + 形容詞で、過去の基準時より前の状態を表せます。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “She had been tired before the meeting started.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「She had been tired before the meeting started.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"She been tired before the meeting started.","accepted":["She had been tired before the meeting started."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もう仕事を終えましたか？”.","hintJa":"今の時点で終わったかを尋ねる現在完了の質問です。","explanation":"“Have you finished your work yet?” directly expresses “もう仕事を終えましたか？”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「Have you finished your work yet?」が「もう仕事を終えましたか？」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: もう仕事を終えましたか？","promptJa":"「もう仕事を終えましたか？」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Have you finished your work yet?","jp":"もう仕事を終えましたか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I have already eaten breakfast.","jp":"私はもう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I have lived here since 2016.","jp":"私は2016年からここに住んでいます。"},{"id":"d","en":"I had a car when I lived there.","jp":"そこに住んでいた時、私は車を持っていました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The empty plate shows the breakfast is already complete.","hintJa":"空になった皿から、朝食がすでに終わっていることを考えましょう。","explanation":"“I have already eaten breakfast.” is correct. The finished plate and satisfied expression show the meal was completed before now. “I haven’t eaten dinner yet.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はまだ夕食を食べていません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “She had left before I called.” does not fit because that sentence means “私が電話する前に、彼女は出発していました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I wish I had been born there.” does not fit because that sentence means “そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I have already eaten breakfast.」（私はもう朝食を食べました。）です。食べ終わった皿と満足した表情が、朝食がすでに完了したことを示しています。 「I haven’t eaten dinner yet.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はまだ夕食を食べていません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「She had left before I called.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私が電話する前に、彼女は出発していました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I wish I had been born there.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I have already eaten breakfast.","jp":"私はもう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t eaten dinner yet.","jp":"私はまだ夕食を食べていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"She had left before I called.","jp":"私が電話する前に、彼女は出発していました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I wish I had been born there.","jp":"そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-30-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A person has already finished breakfast.","visualAssetId":"july-30-part-2-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"present perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The person is crossing the doorway at this very moment.","hintJa":"本人がまさに今、玄関を入った瞬間に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I’ve just arrived home.” is correct. Keys, bag and the just-opened door show a very recent arrival home. “I have already eaten breakfast.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はもう朝食を食べました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “He had finished the report by noon.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼は正午までにレポートを終えていました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Have you finished your work yet?” does not fit because that sentence means “もう仕事を終えましたか？,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I’ve just arrived home.」（私はたった今家に着きました。）です。鍵、鞄、開いたばかりの玄関が、たった今の帰宅を示しています。 「I have already eaten breakfast.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はもう朝食を食べました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「He had finished the report by noon.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼は正午までにレポートを終えていました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Have you finished your work yet?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「もう仕事を終えましたか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve just arrived home.","jp":"私はたった今家に着きました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I have already eaten breakfast.","jp":"私はもう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"c","en":"He had finished the report by noon.","jp":"彼は正午までにレポートを終えていました。"},{"id":"d","en":"Have you finished your work yet?","jp":"もう仕事を終えましたか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-30-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A person has just arrived home.","visualAssetId":"july-30-part-2-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"past perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Identify which of the two past actions happened first.","hintJa":"二つの過去の出来事のうち、どちらが先だったかを見ましょう。","explanation":"“I had already eaten when you arrived.” is correct. The meal is finished before the guest reaches the door. “I’ve just arrived home.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はたった今家に着きました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I had a car when I lived there.” does not fit because that sentence means “そこに住んでいた時、私は車を持っていました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “She had been tired before the meeting started.” does not fit because that sentence means “会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I had already eaten when you arrived.」（あなたが着いた時には、私はもう食べ終えていました。）です。客が玄関に着く前に、食事が終わっている時間の流れです。 「I’ve just arrived home.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はたった今家に着きました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I had a car when I lived there.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「そこに住んでいた時、私は車を持っていました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「She had been tired before the meeting started.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I had already eaten when you arrived.","jp":"あなたが着いた時には、私はもう食べ終えていました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve just arrived home.","jp":"私はたった今家に着きました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I had a car when I lived there.","jp":"そこに住んでいた時、私は車を持っていました。"},{"id":"d","en":"She had been tired before the meeting started.","jp":"会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-30-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"A host had already eaten when a guest arrived.","visualAssetId":"july-30-part-2-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"had","isOriginal":false,"hint":"This is simple past possession during an earlier period of life.","hintJa":"以前の生活期間に持っていた物を表す単純過去に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I had a car when I lived there.” is correct. The memory shows the person possessing a car during the time they lived there. “I haven’t eaten dinner yet.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はまだ夕食を食べていません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I had already eaten when you arrived.” does not fit because that sentence means “あなたが着いた時には、私はもう食べ終えていました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I wish I had been born there.” does not fit because that sentence means “そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I had a car when I lived there.」（そこに住んでいた時、私は車を持っていました。）です。回想場面で、その場所に住んでいた時に車を所有していたことが分かります。 「I haven’t eaten dinner yet.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はまだ夕食を食べていません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I had already eaten when you arrived.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「あなたが着いた時には、私はもう食べ終えていました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I wish I had been born there.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I had a car when I lived there.","jp":"そこに住んでいた時、私は車を持っていました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t eaten dinner yet.","jp":"私はまだ夕食を食べていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I had already eaten when you arrived.","jp":"あなたが着いた時には、私はもう食べ終えていました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I wish I had been born there.","jp":"そこで生まれていたらよかったのに。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-30-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"A person owned a car while living in another town.","visualAssetId":"july-30-part-2-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('july-30-part-2', 'july-30-part-2-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"july-30-part-2-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"had been","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The tired state begins before the later meeting.","hintJa":"疲れた状態が、その後の会議より前に始まっていることを見ましょう。","explanation":"“She had been tired before the meeting started.” is correct. She is visibly tired before colleagues arrive and the meeting starts. “I have already eaten breakfast.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はもう朝食を食べました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I have lived here since 2016.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は2016年からここに住んでいます。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I had been there before.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は以前そこへ行ったことがありました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「She had been tired before the meeting started.」（会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。）です。同僚が来て会議が始まる前から、彼女が疲れている様子です。 「I have already eaten breakfast.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はもう朝食を食べました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I have lived here since 2016.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は2016年からここに住んでいます。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I had been there before.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は以前そこへ行ったことがありました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She had been tired before the meeting started.","jp":"会議が始まる前から彼女は疲れていました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I have already eaten breakfast.","jp":"私はもう朝食を食べました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I have lived here since 2016.","jp":"私は2016年からここに住んでいます。"},{"id":"d","en":"I had been there before.","jp":"私は以前そこへ行ったことがありました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/july-30-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A woman had already been tired before a meeting started.","visualAssetId":"july-30-part-2-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-02-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"polite questions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the polite questions meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？”.","hintJa":"個人的な質問の前に許可を求める丁寧な言い方です。","explanation":"“Do you mind if I ask how old you are?” is the sentence that means “年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Do you mind if I ask how old you are?」が「年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？","promptJa":"「年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Do you mind if I ask how old you are?","jp":"年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I’d rather not say.","jp":"できれば言いたくありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"Let’s dig into the details.","jp":"詳しい内容を掘り下げましょう。"},{"id":"d","en":"Despite the rain, we went out.","jp":"雨にもかかわらず、私たちは出かけました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-02-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"privacy","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the privacy meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “できれば言いたくありません。”.","hintJa":"答えたくない時の柔らかい断り方です。","explanation":"“I’d rather not say.” is the sentence that means “できれば言いたくありません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I’d rather not say.」が「できれば言いたくありません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: できれば言いたくありません。","promptJa":"「できれば言いたくありません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’d rather not say.","jp":"できれば言いたくありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I hope I didn’t offend you.","jp":"気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。"},{"id":"c","en":"I can’t tell the twins apart.","jp":"私はその双子を見分けられません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Although it was raining, we went out.","jp":"雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-02-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"apology","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the apology meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。”.","hintJa":"offend は「気分を害する」です。","explanation":"“I hope I didn’t offend you.” is the sentence that means “気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I hope I didn’t offend you.」が「気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。","promptJa":"「気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I hope I didn’t offend you.","jp":"気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。"},{"id":"b","en":"I don’t want to pry into your private life.","jp":"あなたの私生活に立ち入りたくありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I recognized him from behind.","jp":"私は後ろ姿で彼だと分かりました。"},{"id":"d","en":"Let me check my schedule and get back to you.","jp":"予定を確認して、またご連絡します。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
