  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-speaking-3', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-02-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"despite","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the despite meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “雨にもかかわらず、私たちは出かけました。”.","hintJa":"despite の後ろには名詞を置きます。","explanation":"Model: “Despite the rain, we went out.” (雨にもかかわらず、私たちは出かけました。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Despite the rain, we went out.」（雨にもかかわらず、私たちは出かけました。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"Despite the rain, we went out.","speakJa":"雨にもかかわらず、私たちは出かけました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-speaking-4', 23, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-02-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"although","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the although meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。”.","hintJa":"although の後ろには主語 + 動詞の節を置きます。","explanation":"Model: “Although it was raining, we went out.” (雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Although it was raining, we went out.」（雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Although it was raining, we went out.","speakJa":"雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-02-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"schedule","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the schedule meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “予定を確認して、またご連絡します。”.","hintJa":"すぐに返事できない時の自然な仕事表現です。","explanation":"Model: “Let me check my schedule and get back to you.” (予定を確認して、またご連絡します。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Let me check my schedule and get back to you.」（予定を確認して、またご連絡します。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Let me check my schedule and get back to you.","speakJa":"予定を確認して、またご連絡します。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-02-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"although","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the although meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。”.","hintJa":"although の後ろには主語 + 動詞の節を置きます。","explanation":"“Although it was raining, we went out.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「Although it was raining, we went out.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: Despite the rain, we went out.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: 雨にもかかわらず、私たちは出かけました。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Although it was raining, we went out.","jp":"雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Let me check my schedule and get back to you.","jp":"予定を確認して、またご連絡します。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’d rather not say.","jp":"できれば言いたくありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I can’t tell the twins apart.","jp":"私はその双子を見分けられません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-02-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"schedule","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the schedule meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “予定を確認して、またご連絡します。”.","hintJa":"すぐに返事できない時の自然な仕事表現です。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “Let me check my schedule and get back to you.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「Let me check my schedule and get back to you.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"Let me check my schedule and get back to you yesterday now.","accepted":["Let me check my schedule and get back to you."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-02-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"number of times","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the number of times meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もう100回も言いました。”.","hintJa":"回数は a hundred times のように表します。","explanation":"“I’ve told you a hundred times.” directly expresses “もう100回も言いました。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「I’ve told you a hundred times.」が「もう100回も言いました。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: もう100回も言いました。","promptJa":"「もう100回も言いました。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve told you a hundred times.","jp":"もう100回も言いました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Do you mind if I ask how old you are?","jp":"年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I don’t want to pry into your private life.","jp":"あなたの私生活に立ち入りたくありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Can you identify the person in this photo?","jp":"この写真の人物を特定できますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-02-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"polite questions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Look for permission before a personal age question.","hintJa":"個人的な年齢の質問をする前に、許可を求めている様子を見ましょう。","explanation":"“Do you mind if I ask how old you are?” is correct. The careful gesture and birthday cue show a polite request to ask about age. “I’d rather not say.” does not fit because that sentence means “できれば言いたくありません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I can’t tell the twins apart.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はその双子を見分けられません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Although it was raining, we went out.” does not fit because that sentence means “雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Do you mind if I ask how old you are?」（年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？）です。慎重な仕草と誕生日の手がかりが、年齢を丁寧に尋ねる場面を示しています。 「I’d rather not say.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「できれば言いたくありません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I can’t tell the twins apart.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はその双子を見分けられません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Although it was raining, we went out.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Do you mind if I ask how old you are?","jp":"年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I’d rather not say.","jp":"できれば言いたくありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I can’t tell the twins apart.","jp":"私はその双子を見分けられません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Although it was raining, we went out.","jp":"雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-02-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A person politely asks permission before asking someone’s age.","visualAssetId":"august-02-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-02-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"apology","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Notice the speaker’s concern about the other person’s feelings.","hintJa":"相手の気分を害していないか心配する話し手に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I hope I didn’t offend you.” is correct. The apology and concern follow an uncomfortable question. “Do you mind if I ask how old you are?” does not fit because that sentence means “年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I recognized him from behind.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は後ろ姿で彼だと分かりました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’ve told you a hundred times.” does not fit because that sentence means “もう100回も言いました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I hope I didn’t offend you.」（気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。）です。気まずい質問の後、話し手が謝りながら相手を気づかっています。 「Do you mind if I ask how old you are?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I recognized him from behind.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は後ろ姿で彼だと分かりました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’ve told you a hundred times.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「もう100回も言いました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I hope I didn’t offend you.","jp":"気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。"},{"id":"b","en":"Do you mind if I ask how old you are?","jp":"年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I recognized him from behind.","jp":"私は後ろ姿で彼だと分かりました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’ve told you a hundred times.","jp":"もう100回も言いました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-02-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A speaker apologetically checks that a personal question did not offend someone.","visualAssetId":"august-02-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-02-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"dig into","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The team is examining information deeply, not invading private life.","hintJa":"私生活を詮索するのではなく、情報を詳しく掘り下げている場面です。","explanation":"“Let’s dig into the details.” is correct. The group is productively studying project details together. “I hope I didn’t offend you.” does not fit because that sentence means “気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Can you identify the person in this photo?” does not fit because that sentence means “この写真の人物を特定できますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Let me check my schedule and get back to you.” does not fit because that sentence means “予定を確認して、またご連絡します。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Let’s dig into the details.」（詳しい内容を掘り下げましょう。）です。チームが協力してプロジェクトの詳細を深く調べています。 「I hope I didn’t offend you.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Can you identify the person in this photo?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「この写真の人物を特定できますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Let me check my schedule and get back to you.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「予定を確認して、またご連絡します。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Let’s dig into the details.","jp":"詳しい内容を掘り下げましょう。"},{"id":"b","en":"I hope I didn’t offend you.","jp":"気を悪くさせていなければいいのですが。"},{"id":"c","en":"Can you identify the person in this photo?","jp":"この写真の人物を特定できますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"Let me check my schedule and get back to you.","jp":"予定を確認して、またご連絡します。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-02-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"Coworkers dig into the details of a project.","visualAssetId":"august-02-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-02-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"identify","isOriginal":false,"hint":"One exact person is being identified in the photograph.","hintJa":"写真の中から一人の人物を特定していることに注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Can you identify the person in this photo?” is correct. The viewer singles out one precise person in the group photo. “I’d rather not say.” does not fit because that sentence means “できれば言いたくありません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Let’s dig into the details.” does not fit because that sentence means “詳しい内容を掘り下げましょう。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Although it was raining, we went out.” does not fit because that sentence means “雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Can you identify the person in this photo?」（この写真の人物を特定できますか？）です。見る人が集合写真の中から特定の一人を指し示しています。 「I’d rather not say.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「できれば言いたくありません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Let’s dig into the details.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「詳しい内容を掘り下げましょう。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Although it was raining, we went out.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Can you identify the person in this photo?","jp":"この写真の人物を特定できますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I’d rather not say.","jp":"できれば言いたくありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"Let’s dig into the details.","jp":"詳しい内容を掘り下げましょう。"},{"id":"d","en":"Although it was raining, we went out.","jp":"雨が降っていましたが、私たちは出かけました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-02-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"A person identifies someone in a photograph.","visualAssetId":"august-02-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-02', 'august-02-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-02-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"schedule","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The person checks availability before giving an answer later.","hintJa":"予定を確認してから後で返事をする流れを見ましょう。","explanation":"“Let me check my schedule and get back to you.” is correct. The calendar check and later-message gesture show a delayed but responsible response. “Do you mind if I ask how old you are?” does not fit because that sentence means “年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I don’t want to pry into your private life.” does not fit because that sentence means “あなたの私生活に立ち入りたくありません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Despite the rain, we went out.” does not fit because that sentence means “雨にもかかわらず、私たちは出かけました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Let me check my schedule and get back to you.」（予定を確認して、またご連絡します。）です。カレンダー確認と後で連絡する仕草が、確認後の返信を示しています。 「Do you mind if I ask how old you are?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I don’t want to pry into your private life.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「あなたの私生活に立ち入りたくありません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Despite the rain, we went out.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「雨にもかかわらず、私たちは出かけました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Let me check my schedule and get back to you.","jp":"予定を確認して、またご連絡します。"},{"id":"b","en":"Do you mind if I ask how old you are?","jp":"年齢を伺ってもよろしいですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I don’t want to pry into your private life.","jp":"あなたの私生活に立ち入りたくありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Despite the rain, we went out.","jp":"雨にもかかわらず、私たちは出かけました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-02-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A professional checks a calendar before promising to reply.","visualAssetId":"august-02-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-03-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"not yet","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the not yet meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はまだお風呂に入っていません。”.","hintJa":"今日など、まだ続いている時間には現在完了が自然です。","explanation":"“I haven’t taken a bath yet.” is the sentence that means “私はまだお風呂に入っていません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I haven’t taken a bath yet.」が「私はまだお風呂に入っていません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 私はまだお風呂に入っていません。","promptJa":"「私はまだお風呂に入っていません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","jp":"私はまだお風呂に入っていません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I didn’t take a bath last night.","jp":"私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"I tried it yesterday.","jp":"私は昨日それを試しました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I have already had lunch.","jp":"私はもう昼食を食べました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-03-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"finished past","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the finished past meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。”.","hintJa":"last night のような終わった時には過去形を使います。","explanation":"“I didn’t take a bath last night.” is the sentence that means “私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I didn’t take a bath last night.」が「私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。","promptJa":"「私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I didn’t take a bath last night.","jp":"私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"Have you taken a shower yet?","jp":"もうシャワーを浴びましたか？"},{"id":"c","en":"Coffee can be an acquired taste.","jp":"コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。"},{"id":"d","en":"I haven’t decided yet.","jp":"私はまだ決めていません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-03-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"not yet","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the not yet meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もうシャワーを浴びましたか？”.","hintJa":"今までに済んだかを確認する質問です。","explanation":"“Have you taken a shower yet?” is the sentence that means “もうシャワーを浴びましたか？”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Have you taken a shower yet?」が「もうシャワーを浴びましたか？」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: もうシャワーを浴びましたか？","promptJa":"「もうシャワーを浴びましたか？」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Have you taken a shower yet?","jp":"もうシャワーを浴びましたか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I have never tried that before.","jp":"私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。"},{"id":"c","en":"It has a sophisticated flavor.","jp":"それは洗練された味わいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"She had left before I arrived.","jp":"私が着く前に、彼女は帰っていました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-03-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"never","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the never meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。”.","hintJa":"have never + 過去分詞で経験がないことを表します。","explanation":"“I have never tried that before.” is the sentence that means “私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I have never tried that before.」が「私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。","promptJa":"「私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I have never tried that before.","jp":"私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I tried it yesterday.","jp":"私は昨日それを試しました。"},{"id":"c","en":"This flavor is more popular with adults.","jp":"この味は大人により人気があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"He plays tennis every weekend.","jp":"彼は毎週末テニスをします。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
