  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-03-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"not yet","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the not yet meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はまだ決めていません。”.","hintJa":"未決定の状態が今も続いています。","explanation":"“I haven’t decided yet.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「I haven’t decided yet.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: I have already had lunch.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: 私はもう昼食を食べました。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I haven’t decided yet.","jp":"私はまだ決めていません。"},{"id":"b","en":"She had left before I arrived.","jp":"私が着く前に、彼女は帰っていました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I didn’t take a bath last night.","jp":"私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"Coffee can be an acquired taste.","jp":"コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-03-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"past perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the past perfect meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私が着く前に、彼女は帰っていました。”.","hintJa":"先に起きた過去を過去完了で示します。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “She had left before I arrived.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「She had left before I arrived.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"She left before I arrived.","accepted":["She had left before I arrived."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-03-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"habit","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the habit meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼は毎週末テニスをします。”.","hintJa":"繰り返す習慣には現在形を使います。","explanation":"“He plays tennis every weekend.” directly expresses “彼は毎週末テニスをします。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「He plays tennis every weekend.」が「彼は毎週末テニスをします。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 彼は毎週末テニスをします。","promptJa":"「彼は毎週末テニスをします。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He plays tennis every weekend.","jp":"彼は毎週末テニスをします。"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","jp":"私はまだお風呂に入っていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I have never tried that before.","jp":"私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"This flavor is more popular with adults.","jp":"この味は大人により人気があります。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-03-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"not yet","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The day is still continuing and the bath remains unfinished.","hintJa":"今日はまだ続いており、入浴が未完了であることを見ましょう。","explanation":"“I haven’t taken a bath yet.” is correct. The ready bath and late clock show an action that has not happened yet today. “I didn’t take a bath last night.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Coffee can be an acquired taste.” does not fit because that sentence means “コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I haven’t decided yet.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はまだ決めていません。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I haven’t taken a bath yet.」（私はまだお風呂に入っていません。）です。準備された浴槽と遅い時計が、今日まだ入浴していないことを示しています。 「I didn’t take a bath last night.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Coffee can be an acquired taste.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I haven’t decided yet.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はまだ決めていません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","jp":"私はまだお風呂に入っていません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I didn’t take a bath last night.","jp":"私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"Coffee can be an acquired taste.","jp":"コーヒーは慣れると好きになる味です。"},{"id":"d","en":"I haven’t decided yet.","jp":"私はまだ決めていません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-03-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A person has not taken a bath yet today.","visualAssetId":"august-03-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-03-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"not yet","isOriginal":false,"hint":"This is a question about whether the shower is complete by now.","hintJa":"今の時点までにシャワーが済んだかを尋ねる場面です。","explanation":"“Have you taken a shower yet?” is correct. The shower cue and questioning gesture ask about completion up to the present. “I haven’t taken a bath yet.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はまだお風呂に入っていません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “It has a sophisticated flavor.” does not fit because that sentence means “それは洗練された味わいです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “He plays tennis every weekend.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼は毎週末テニスをします。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Have you taken a shower yet?」（もうシャワーを浴びましたか？）です。シャワーの手がかりと質問の仕草が、今までの完了を尋ねています。 「I haven’t taken a bath yet.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はまだお風呂に入っていません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「It has a sophisticated flavor.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「それは洗練された味わいです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「He plays tennis every weekend.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼は毎週末テニスをします。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Have you taken a shower yet?","jp":"もうシャワーを浴びましたか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","jp":"私はまだお風呂に入っていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"It has a sophisticated flavor.","jp":"それは洗練された味わいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"He plays tennis every weekend.","jp":"彼は毎週末テニスをします。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-03-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"Someone asks whether a friend has showered yet.","visualAssetId":"august-03-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-03-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"finished past","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The tasting happened on a finished day in the past.","hintJa":"試食が、すでに終わった過去の日に起きたことを見ましょう。","explanation":"“I tried it yesterday.” is correct. The completed calendar day places the food experience clearly in yesterday. “Have you taken a shower yet?” does not fit because that sentence means “もうシャワーを浴びましたか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “This flavor is more popular with adults.” does not fit because that sentence means “この味は大人により人気があります。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “She had left before I arrived.” does not fit because that sentence means “私が着く前に、彼女は帰っていました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I tried it yesterday.」（私は昨日それを試しました。）です。終わった日のカレンダーが、食べた経験を昨日の出来事として示しています。 「Have you taken a shower yet?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「もうシャワーを浴びましたか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「This flavor is more popular with adults.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「この味は大人により人気があります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「She had left before I arrived.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私が着く前に、彼女は帰っていました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I tried it yesterday.","jp":"私は昨日それを試しました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Have you taken a shower yet?","jp":"もうシャワーを浴びましたか？"},{"id":"c","en":"This flavor is more popular with adults.","jp":"この味は大人により人気があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"She had left before I arrived.","jp":"私が着く前に、彼女は帰っていました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-03-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"A person tried a new food yesterday.","visualAssetId":"august-03-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-03-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"preferences","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Compare which age group chooses the more complex flavor.","hintJa":"より複雑な味を選んでいる年齢層を比べましょう。","explanation":"“This flavor is more popular with adults.” is correct. Adults choose and enjoy the complex flavor more than the children do. “I didn’t take a bath last night.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I tried it yesterday.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は昨日それを試しました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I haven’t decided yet.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はまだ決めていません。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「This flavor is more popular with adults.」（この味は大人により人気があります。）です。子どもより大人の方が複雑な味を選び、楽しんでいます。 「I didn’t take a bath last night.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I tried it yesterday.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は昨日それを試しました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I haven’t decided yet.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はまだ決めていません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"This flavor is more popular with adults.","jp":"この味は大人により人気があります。"},{"id":"b","en":"I didn’t take a bath last night.","jp":"私は昨夜お風呂に入りませんでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"I tried it yesterday.","jp":"私は昨日それを試しました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I haven’t decided yet.","jp":"私はまだ決めていません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-03-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"A complex flavor is more popular with adults than children.","visualAssetId":"august-03-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-03', 'august-03-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-03-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"past perfect","isOriginal":false,"hint":"One past action is already complete before the later arrival.","hintJa":"後の到着より前に、別の過去の行動が完了していることを見ましょう。","explanation":"“She had left before I arrived.” is correct. She exits first, and the other person reaches the empty room afterward. “I haven’t taken a bath yet.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はまだお風呂に入っていません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I have never tried that before.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I have already had lunch.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はもう昼食を食べました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「She had left before I arrived.」（私が着く前に、彼女は帰っていました。）です。彼女が先に退出し、その後で別の人が空の部屋に到着しています。 「I haven’t taken a bath yet.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はまだお風呂に入っていません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I have never tried that before.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I have already had lunch.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はもう昼食を食べました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She had left before I arrived.","jp":"私が着く前に、彼女は帰っていました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I haven’t taken a bath yet.","jp":"私はまだお風呂に入っていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I have never tried that before.","jp":"私はそれを一度も試したことがありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I have already had lunch.","jp":"私はもう昼食を食べました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-03-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A woman had left before another person arrived.","visualAssetId":"august-03-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-09-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"shed a tear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the shed a tear meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。”.","hintJa":"shed の過去形も shed です。tear は「涙」です。","explanation":"“She shed a tear during the movie.” is the sentence that means “彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「She shed a tear during the movie.」が「彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。","promptJa":"「彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She shed a tear during the movie.","jp":"彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。"},{"id":"b","en":"He burst into tears.","jp":"彼は突然泣き出しました。"},{"id":"c","en":"Could I have two coffees, please?","jp":"コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"There’s a hair in my soup.","jp":"スープの中に髪の毛が一本あります。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-09-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"burst into tears","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the burst into tears meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼は突然泣き出しました。”.","hintJa":"急に泣き始める強い変化を表します。","explanation":"“He burst into tears.” is the sentence that means “彼は突然泣き出しました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「He burst into tears.」が「彼は突然泣き出しました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼は突然泣き出しました。","promptJa":"「彼は突然泣き出しました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He burst into tears.","jp":"彼は突然泣き出しました。"},{"id":"b","en":"The story brought tears to my eyes.","jp":"その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。"},{"id":"c","en":"We ordered a whole chicken.","jp":"私たちは丸ごとの鶏を一羽注文しました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I spilled water on the table.","jp":"私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-09-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"tears","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the tears meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。”.","hintJa":"感動などで自然に涙が出そうな時の表現です。","explanation":"“The story brought tears to my eyes.” is the sentence that means “その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「The story brought tears to my eyes.」が「その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。","promptJa":"「その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The story brought tears to my eyes.","jp":"その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I need a glass of water.","jp":"コップ一杯の水が必要です。"},{"id":"c","en":"I had some chicken for lunch.","jp":"私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。"},{"id":"d","en":"Please pour the water into the glass.","jp":"水をコップに注いでください。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-09-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"uncountable nouns","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the uncountable nouns meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “コップ一杯の水が必要です。”.","hintJa":"water は量の容器を使って数えます。","explanation":"“I need a glass of water.” is the sentence that means “コップ一杯の水が必要です。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I need a glass of water.」が「コップ一杯の水が必要です。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: コップ一杯の水が必要です。","promptJa":"「コップ一杯の水が必要です。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I need a glass of water.","jp":"コップ一杯の水が必要です。"},{"id":"b","en":"Could I have two coffees, please?","jp":"コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"Would you like a piece of cake?","jp":"ケーキを一切れいかがですか？"},{"id":"d","en":"This building has three tiers.","jp":"この建物には3つの層があります。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-09-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"countable servings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the countable servings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？”.","hintJa":"店では coffee が「一杯」の意味で数えられます。","explanation":"True. “Could I have two coffees, please?” means “コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「Could I have two coffees, please?」は「コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？」という意味です。","prompt":"“Could I have two coffees, please?” means “コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？”.","promptJa":"「Could I have two coffees, please?」は「コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-09-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"countable food","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the countable food meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私たちは丸ごとの鶏を一羽注文しました。”.","hintJa":"動物・丸ごとの料理としては chicken を数えられます。","explanation":"False. “We ordered a whole chicken.” means “私たちは丸ごとの鶏を一羽注文しました。”, not “私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「We ordered a whole chicken.」は「私たちは丸ごとの鶏を一羽注文しました。」であり、「私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。」ではありません。","prompt":"“We ordered a whole chicken.” means “私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。”.","promptJa":"「We ordered a whole chicken.」は「私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-09-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"uncountable food","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the uncountable food meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。”.","hintJa":"肉としての chicken は通常、数えません。","explanation":"A natural translation is “I had some chicken for lunch.”. It expresses “私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。” with the lesson’s uncountable food pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「I had some chicken for lunch.」です。「私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。」を今回のuncountable food表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。","accepted":["I had some chicken for lunch."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-09-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"portions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the portions meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ケーキを一切れいかがですか？”.","hintJa":"cake を切り分けた量は a piece of で表します。","explanation":"A natural translation is “Would you like a piece of cake?”. It expresses “ケーキを一切れいかがですか？” with the lesson’s portions pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「Would you like a piece of cake?」です。「ケーキを一切れいかがですか？」を今回のportions表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: ケーキを一切れいかがですか？","promptJa":"英語にしてください：ケーキを一切れいかがですか？","accepted":["Would you like a piece of cake?"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-typing', 8, 'Build It', 'typing', '{"id":"august-09-draft-typing","format":"typing","type":"typing","section":"Build It","topic":"tear vs tier","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the tear vs tier meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この建物には3つの層があります。”.","hintJa":"tier は「段・層」で、tear「涙」と発音が異なります。","explanation":"A complete model answer is “This building has three tiers.”. Check the key tear vs tier expression and every short grammar word.","explanationJa":"完全な答えは「This building has three tiers.」です。tear vs tierの中心表現と短い文法語まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete English sentence from memory: この建物には3つの層があります。","promptJa":"日本語を見て、英文を最後まで入力してください：この建物には3つの層があります。","accepted":["This building has three tiers."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-order-1', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-09-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"countable hair","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the countable hair meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “スープの中に髪の毛が一本あります。”.","hintJa":"一本の毛なら a hair と数えられます。","explanation":"Correct order: “There’s a hair in my soup.”. Build the sentence around the countable hair pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「There’s a hair in my soup.」です。countable hairの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: スープの中に髪の毛が一本あります。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：スープの中に髪の毛が一本あります。","words":["in","my","soup","There’s","a","hair"],"correctWords":["There’s","a","hair","in","my","soup"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-order-2', 10, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-09-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"spill","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the spill meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。”.","hintJa":"意図せず容器の外へ出た時は spill です。","explanation":"Correct order: “I spilled water on the table.”. Build the sentence around the spill pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I spilled water on the table.」です。spillの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。","words":["on","the","table","I","spilled","water"],"correctWords":["I","spilled","water","on","the","table"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-matching', 11, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"august-09-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"shed a tear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the shed a tear meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。”.","hintJa":"shed の過去形も shed です。tear は「涙」です。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"She shed a tear during the movie.","jp":"彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。","cat":"shed a tear"},{"en":"He burst into tears.","jp":"彼は突然泣き出しました。","cat":"burst into tears"},{"en":"The story brought tears to my eyes.","jp":"その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。","cat":"tears"},{"en":"I need a glass of water.","jp":"コップ一杯の水が必要です。","cat":"uncountable nouns"},{"en":"Could I have two coffees, please?","jp":"コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？","cat":"countable servings"},{"en":"We ordered a whole chicken.","jp":"私たちは丸ごとの鶏を一羽注文しました。","cat":"countable food"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-sorting', 12, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"august-09-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"burst into tears","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the burst into tears meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼は突然泣き出しました。”.","hintJa":"急に泣き始める強い変化を表します。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are shed a tear, burst into tears, tears.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「shed a tear・burst into tears・tears」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["shed a tear","burst into tears","tears"],"items":[["She shed a tear during the movie.","shed a tear"],["He burst into tears.","burst into tears"],["The story brought tears to my eyes.","tears"]]}'::jsonb, false, 3),
