  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-09-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"pour","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the pour meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “水をコップに注いでください。”.","hintJa":"意図的に液体を注ぐ時は pour です。","explanation":"Model: “Please pour the water into the glass.” (水をコップに注いでください。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Please pour the water into the glass.」（水をコップに注いでください。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Please pour the water into the glass.","speakJa":"水をコップに注いでください。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-09-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"spill","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the spill meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。”.","hintJa":"意図せず容器の外へ出た時は spill です。","explanation":"“I spilled water on the table.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「I spilled water on the table.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: There’s a hair in my soup.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: スープの中に髪の毛が一本あります。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I spilled water on the table.","jp":"私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Please pour the water into the glass.","jp":"水をコップに注いでください。"},{"id":"c","en":"He burst into tears.","jp":"彼は突然泣き出しました。"},{"id":"d","en":"We ordered a whole chicken.","jp":"私たちは丸ごとの鶏を一羽注文しました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-09-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"pour","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the pour meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “水をコップに注いでください。”.","hintJa":"意図的に液体を注ぐ時は pour です。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “Please pour the water into the glass.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「Please pour the water into the glass.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"Please pour water into the glass.","accepted":["Please pour the water into the glass."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-09-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"tear vs tier","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the tear vs tier meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この建物には3つの層があります。”.","hintJa":"tier は「段・層」で、tear「涙」と発音が異なります。","explanation":"“This building has three tiers.” directly expresses “この建物には3つの層があります。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「This building has three tiers.」が「この建物には3つの層があります。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: この建物には3つの層があります。","promptJa":"「この建物には3つの層があります。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"This building has three tiers.","jp":"この建物には3つの層があります。"},{"id":"b","en":"She shed a tear during the movie.","jp":"彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I need a glass of water.","jp":"コップ一杯の水が必要です。"},{"id":"d","en":"Would you like a piece of cake?","jp":"ケーキを一切れいかがですか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-09-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"shed a tear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Look for one quiet tear rather than sudden intense crying.","hintJa":"突然激しく泣くのではなく、静かに一筋の涙を流す様子を見ましょう。","explanation":"“She shed a tear during the movie.” is correct. Exactly one tear is visible during the emotional movie. “He burst into tears.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼は突然泣き出しました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “We ordered a whole chicken.” does not fit because that sentence means “私たちは丸ごとの鶏を一羽注文しました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I spilled water on the table.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「She shed a tear during the movie.」（彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。）です。感動的な映画の途中で、一筋だけ涙が見えています。 「He burst into tears.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼は突然泣き出しました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「We ordered a whole chicken.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私たちは丸ごとの鶏を一羽注文しました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I spilled water on the table.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She shed a tear during the movie.","jp":"彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。"},{"id":"b","en":"He burst into tears.","jp":"彼は突然泣き出しました。"},{"id":"c","en":"We ordered a whole chicken.","jp":"私たちは丸ごとの鶏を一羽注文しました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I spilled water on the table.","jp":"私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-09-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A moviegoer quietly sheds one tear.","visualAssetId":"august-09-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-09-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"tears","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The emotion makes tears gather in the listener’s eyes.","hintJa":"感動によって、聞き手の目に涙がこみ上げている様子です。","explanation":"“The story brought tears to my eyes.” is correct. The listener’s watery eyes and moved expression are caused by the story. “She shed a tear during the movie.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I had some chicken for lunch.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “This building has three tiers.” does not fit because that sentence means “この建物には3つの層があります。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「The story brought tears to my eyes.」（その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。）です。話を聞いた人の潤んだ目と感動した表情が見えます。 「She shed a tear during the movie.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I had some chicken for lunch.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「This building has three tiers.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「この建物には3つの層があります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The story brought tears to my eyes.","jp":"その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。"},{"id":"b","en":"She shed a tear during the movie.","jp":"彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I had some chicken for lunch.","jp":"私は昼食に鶏肉を食べました。"},{"id":"d","en":"This building has three tiers.","jp":"この建物には3つの層があります。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-09-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A moving story brings tears to a listener’s eyes.","visualAssetId":"august-09-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-09-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"countable servings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Count the individual servings being ordered.","hintJa":"注文されている飲み物の杯数を数えましょう。","explanation":"“Could I have two coffees, please?” is correct. Two fingers and two separate cups show an order for two coffees. “The story brought tears to my eyes.” does not fit because that sentence means “その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Would you like a piece of cake?” does not fit because that sentence means “ケーキを一切れいかがですか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Please pour the water into the glass.” does not fit because that sentence means “水をコップに注いでください。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Could I have two coffees, please?」（コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？）です。二本の指と二つのカップが、コーヒー2杯の注文を示しています。 「The story brought tears to my eyes.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Would you like a piece of cake?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「ケーキを一切れいかがですか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Please pour the water into the glass.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「水をコップに注いでください。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Could I have two coffees, please?","jp":"コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"The story brought tears to my eyes.","jp":"その話を聞いて涙がこみ上げました。"},{"id":"c","en":"Would you like a piece of cake?","jp":"ケーキを一切れいかがですか？"},{"id":"d","en":"Please pour the water into the glass.","jp":"水をコップに注いでください。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-09-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"A café customer orders two cups of coffee.","visualAssetId":"august-09-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-09-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"portions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Notice the portion cut from the whole cake.","hintJa":"ホールケーキから切り分けられた一切れに注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Would you like a piece of cake?” is correct. One slice is being offered as a piece of the larger cake. “He burst into tears.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼は突然泣き出しました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Could I have two coffees, please?” does not fit because that sentence means “コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I spilled water on the table.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Would you like a piece of cake?」（ケーキを一切れいかがですか？）です。大きなケーキから切った一切れを客に勧めています。 「He burst into tears.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼は突然泣き出しました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Could I have two coffees, please?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I spilled water on the table.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Would you like a piece of cake?","jp":"ケーキを一切れいかがですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"He burst into tears.","jp":"彼は突然泣き出しました。"},{"id":"c","en":"Could I have two coffees, please?","jp":"コーヒーを2杯いただけますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I spilled water on the table.","jp":"私はテーブルに水をこぼしました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-09-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"A host offers one slice of cake.","visualAssetId":"august-09-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-09', 'august-09-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-09-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"pour","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The liquid is being controlled and directed into a container.","hintJa":"液体が意図的に、容器へ狙って注がれていることを見ましょう。","explanation":"“Please pour the water into the glass.” is correct. The controlled stream goes directly from the pitcher into the glass. “She shed a tear during the movie.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I need a glass of water.” does not fit because that sentence means “コップ一杯の水が必要です。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “There’s a hair in my soup.” does not fit because that sentence means “スープの中に髪の毛が一本あります。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Please pour the water into the glass.」（水をコップに注いでください。）です。水差しからコップへ、制御された水の流れが直接注がれています。 「She shed a tear during the movie.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I need a glass of water.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「コップ一杯の水が必要です。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「There’s a hair in my soup.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「スープの中に髪の毛が一本あります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Please pour the water into the glass.","jp":"水をコップに注いでください。"},{"id":"b","en":"She shed a tear during the movie.","jp":"彼女は映画の途中で一筋の涙を流しました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I need a glass of water.","jp":"コップ一杯の水が必要です。"},{"id":"d","en":"There’s a hair in my soup.","jp":"スープの中に髪の毛が一本あります。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-09-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"Someone deliberately pours water into a glass.","visualAssetId":"august-09-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"fridge","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the fridge meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。”.","hintJa":"fridge は refrigerator の日常的な短縮形です。","explanation":"“Please put the milk in the fridge.” is the sentence that means “牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Please put the milk in the fridge.」が「牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。","promptJa":"「牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Please put the milk in the fridge.","jp":"牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。"},{"id":"b","en":"The ice cream is in the freezer.","jp":"アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。"},{"id":"c","en":"I didn’t hear the doorbell.","jp":"私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"You’re breaking up.","jp":"声が途切れ途切れです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"freezer","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the freezer meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。”.","hintJa":"freezer は食品を凍らせて保存する場所です。","explanation":"“The ice cream is in the freezer.” is the sentence that means “アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「The ice cream is in the freezer.」が「アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。","promptJa":"「アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The ice cream is in the freezer.","jp":"アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。"},{"id":"b","en":"The refrigerator isn’t working.","jp":"冷蔵庫が動いていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"I can’t hear anything.","jp":"何も聞こえません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Can you hear me now?","jp":"今は私の声が聞こえますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"appliances","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the appliances meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “冷蔵庫が動いていません。”.","hintJa":"故障や一時的な不調には isn’t working が自然です。","explanation":"“The refrigerator isn’t working.” is the sentence that means “冷蔵庫が動いていません。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「The refrigerator isn’t working.」が「冷蔵庫が動いていません。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 冷蔵庫が動いていません。","promptJa":"「冷蔵庫が動いていません。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The refrigerator isn’t working.","jp":"冷蔵庫が動いていません。"},{"id":"b","en":"I couldn’t hear you clearly.","jp":"あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"Could you say that again?","jp":"もう一度言っていただけますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"Let me reconnect and call you back.","jp":"接続し直して、かけ直します。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"couldn’t hear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the couldn’t hear meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。”.","hintJa":"一時的に聞き取れなかった時の自然な言い方です。","explanation":"“I couldn’t hear you clearly.” is the sentence that means “あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I couldn’t hear you clearly.」が「あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。","promptJa":"「あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I couldn’t hear you clearly.","jp":"あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"I didn’t hear the doorbell.","jp":"私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"The connection keeps cutting out.","jp":"回線が何度も途切れます。"},{"id":"d","en":"Could you speak a little more slowly?","jp":"もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"didn’t hear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the didn’t hear meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。”.","hintJa":"実際にその音を聞かなかった出来事を表します。","explanation":"True. “I didn’t hear the doorbell.” means “私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「I didn’t hear the doorbell.」は「私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。」という意味です。","prompt":"“I didn’t hear the doorbell.” means “私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。”.","promptJa":"「I didn’t hear the doorbell.」は「私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"anything","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the anything meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “何も聞こえません。”.","hintJa":"否定文では nothing ではなく anything が基本です。","explanation":"False. “I can’t hear anything.” means “何も聞こえません。”, not “もう一度言っていただけますか？”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「I can’t hear anything.」は「何も聞こえません。」であり、「もう一度言っていただけますか？」ではありません。","prompt":"“I can’t hear anything.” means “もう一度言っていただけますか？”.","promptJa":"「I can’t hear anything.」は「もう一度言っていただけますか？」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"clarification","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the clarification meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もう一度言っていただけますか？”.","hintJa":"丁寧で幅広く使える聞き返しです。","explanation":"A natural translation is “Could you say that again?”. It expresses “もう一度言っていただけますか？” with the lesson’s clarification pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「Could you say that again?」です。「もう一度言っていただけますか？」を今回のclarification表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: もう一度言っていただけますか？","promptJa":"英語にしてください：もう一度言っていただけますか？","accepted":["Could you say that again?"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"phone trouble","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the phone trouble meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “回線が何度も途切れます。”.","hintJa":"cut out は音や接続が突然途切れることです。","explanation":"A natural translation is “The connection keeps cutting out.”. It expresses “回線が何度も途切れます。” with the lesson’s phone trouble pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「The connection keeps cutting out.」です。「回線が何度も途切れます。」を今回のphone trouble表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 回線が何度も途切れます。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：回線が何度も途切れます。","accepted":["The connection keeps cutting out."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-typing', 8, 'Build It', 'typing', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-typing","format":"typing","type":"typing","section":"Build It","topic":"clarification","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the clarification meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？”.","hintJa":"速さが原因で聞き取れない時の丁寧な依頼です。","explanation":"A complete model answer is “Could you speak a little more slowly?”. Check the key clarification expression and every short grammar word.","explanationJa":"完全な答えは「Could you speak a little more slowly?」です。clarificationの中心表現と短い文法語まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete English sentence from memory: もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？","promptJa":"日本語を見て、英文を最後まで入力してください：もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？","accepted":["Could you speak a little more slowly?"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-order-1', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"phone trouble","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the phone trouble meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “声が途切れ途切れです。”.","hintJa":"オンライン通話で相手の声が断続的な時に使います。","explanation":"Correct order: “You’re breaking up.”. Build the sentence around the phone trouble pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「You’re breaking up.」です。phone troubleの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 声が途切れ途切れです。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：声が途切れ途切れです。","words":["You’re","breaking","up"],"correctWords":["You’re","breaking","up"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-order-2', 10, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"sound check","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the sound check meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今は私の声が聞こえますか？”.","hintJa":"接続を調整した後の確認です。","explanation":"Correct order: “Can you hear me now?”. Build the sentence around the sound check pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「Can you hear me now?」です。sound checkの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 今は私の声が聞こえますか？","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：今は私の声が聞こえますか？","words":["you","now","hear","Can","me"],"correctWords":["Can","you","hear","me","now"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-matching', 11, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"fridge","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the fridge meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。”.","hintJa":"fridge は refrigerator の日常的な短縮形です。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"Please put the milk in the fridge.","jp":"牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。","cat":"fridge"},{"en":"The ice cream is in the freezer.","jp":"アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。","cat":"freezer"},{"en":"The refrigerator isn’t working.","jp":"冷蔵庫が動いていません。","cat":"appliances"},{"en":"I couldn’t hear you clearly.","jp":"あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。","cat":"couldn’t hear"},{"en":"I didn’t hear the doorbell.","jp":"私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。","cat":"didn’t hear"},{"en":"I can’t hear anything.","jp":"何も聞こえません。","cat":"anything"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-sorting', 12, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"freezer","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the freezer meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。”.","hintJa":"freezer は食品を凍らせて保存する場所です。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are fridge, freezer, appliances.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「fridge・freezer・appliances」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["fridge","freezer","appliances"],"items":[["Please put the milk in the fridge.","fridge"],["The ice cream is in the freezer.","freezer"],["The refrigerator isn’t working.","appliances"]]}'::jsonb, false, 3),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-grid', 13, 'Build It', 'grid', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-grid","format":"grid","type":"grid","section":"Build It","topic":"didn’t hear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the didn’t hear meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。”.","hintJa":"実際にその音を聞かなかった出来事を表します。","explanation":"The center tile, “I didn’t hear the doorbell.”, means “私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。”. Read every complete phrase before choosing its position.","explanationJa":"中央の「I didn’t hear the doorbell.」が「私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。」を表します。位置だけでなく、各英文の意味を最後まで読んで選びましょう。","prompt":"Select the tile that means: 私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。","promptJa":"「私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。」を表す英文のタイルを選んでください。","correctCell":"center","gridCells":{"top-left":"Please put the milk in the fridge.","top-center":"The ice cream is in the freezer.","top-right":"The refrigerator isn’t working.","middle-left":"I couldn’t hear you clearly.","center":"I didn’t hear the doorbell.","middle-right":"I can’t hear anything.","bottom-left":"Could you say that again?","bottom-center":"The connection keeps cutting out.","bottom-right":"You’re breaking up."}}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-listen-choice-1', 14, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-listen-choice-1","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"fridge","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the fridge meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。”.","hintJa":"fridge は refrigerator の日常的な短縮形です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “Please put the milk in the fridge.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「Please put the milk in the fridge.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"Please put the milk in the fridge.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Please put the milk in the fridge.","jp":"牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。"},{"id":"b","en":"The ice cream is in the freezer.","jp":"アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。"},{"id":"c","en":"I didn’t hear the doorbell.","jp":"私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"You’re breaking up.","jp":"声が途切れ途切れです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-listen-choice-2', 15, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-listen-choice-2","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"couldn’t hear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the couldn’t hear meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。”.","hintJa":"一時的に聞き取れなかった時の自然な言い方です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “I couldn’t hear you clearly.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「I couldn’t hear you clearly.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"I couldn’t hear you clearly.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I couldn’t hear you clearly.","jp":"あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"I didn’t hear the doorbell.","jp":"私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"The connection keeps cutting out.","jp":"回線が何度も途切れます。"},{"id":"d","en":"Could you speak a little more slowly?","jp":"もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-listen-choice-3', 16, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-listen-choice-3","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"clarification","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the clarification meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もう一度言っていただけますか？”.","hintJa":"丁寧で幅広く使える聞き返しです。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “Could you say that again?”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「Could you say that again?」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"Could you say that again?","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Could you say that again?","jp":"もう一度言っていただけますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"The connection keeps cutting out.","jp":"回線が何度も途切れます。"},{"id":"c","en":"Let me reconnect and call you back.","jp":"接続し直して、かけ直します。"},{"id":"d","en":"The refrigerator isn’t working.","jp":"冷蔵庫が動いていません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
