  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-speaking-3', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"phone trouble","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the phone trouble meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “声が途切れ途切れです。”.","hintJa":"オンライン通話で相手の声が断続的な時に使います。","explanation":"Model: “You’re breaking up.” (声が途切れ途切れです。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「You’re breaking up.」（声が途切れ途切れです。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"You’re breaking up.","speakJa":"声が途切れ途切れです。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-speaking-4', 23, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"sound check","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the sound check meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今は私の声が聞こえますか？”.","hintJa":"接続を調整した後の確認です。","explanation":"Model: “Can you hear me now?” (今は私の声が聞こえますか？). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Can you hear me now?」（今は私の声が聞こえますか？）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Can you hear me now?","speakJa":"今は私の声が聞こえますか？"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"phone trouble","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the phone trouble meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “接続し直して、かけ直します。”.","hintJa":"通話を立て直す手順を自然に伝えます。","explanation":"Model: “Let me reconnect and call you back.” (接続し直して、かけ直します。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Let me reconnect and call you back.」（接続し直して、かけ直します。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Let me reconnect and call you back.","speakJa":"接続し直して、かけ直します。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"sound check","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the sound check meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今は私の声が聞こえますか？”.","hintJa":"接続を調整した後の確認です。","explanation":"“Can you hear me now?” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「Can you hear me now?」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: You’re breaking up.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: 声が途切れ途切れです。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Can you hear me now?","jp":"今は私の声が聞こえますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Let me reconnect and call you back.","jp":"接続し直して、かけ直します。"},{"id":"c","en":"The ice cream is in the freezer.","jp":"アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。"},{"id":"d","en":"I can’t hear anything.","jp":"何も聞こえません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"phone trouble","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the phone trouble meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “接続し直して、かけ直します。”.","hintJa":"通話を立て直す手順を自然に伝えます。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “Let me reconnect and call you back.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「Let me reconnect and call you back.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"Let me reconnect and call you back yesterday now.","accepted":["Let me reconnect and call you back."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"clarification","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the clarification meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？”.","hintJa":"速さが原因で聞き取れない時の丁寧な依頼です。","explanation":"“Could you speak a little more slowly?” directly expresses “もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「Could you speak a little more slowly?」が「もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？","promptJa":"「もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Could you speak a little more slowly?","jp":"もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Please put the milk in the fridge.","jp":"牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。"},{"id":"c","en":"I couldn’t hear you clearly.","jp":"あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"The connection keeps cutting out.","jp":"回線が何度も途切れます。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"fridge","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Watch which cold-storage compartment receives the milk.","hintJa":"牛乳をどちらの冷蔵設備へ入れているかを見ましょう。","explanation":"“Please put the milk in the fridge.” is correct. The milk goes onto the refrigerator shelf, not into the freezer. “The ice cream is in the freezer.” does not fit because that sentence means “アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I can’t hear anything.” does not fit because that sentence means “何も聞こえません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Can you hear me now?” does not fit because that sentence means “今は私の声が聞こえますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Please put the milk in the fridge.」（牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。）です。牛乳は冷凍庫ではなく、冷蔵庫の棚へ入れられています。 「The ice cream is in the freezer.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I can’t hear anything.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「何も聞こえません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Can you hear me now?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今は私の声が聞こえますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Please put the milk in the fridge.","jp":"牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。"},{"id":"b","en":"The ice cream is in the freezer.","jp":"アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。"},{"id":"c","en":"I can’t hear anything.","jp":"何も聞こえません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Can you hear me now?","jp":"今は私の声が聞こえますか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-10-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"Someone puts milk into a refrigerator.","visualAssetId":"august-10-part-1-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"appliances","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The appliance is malfunctioning, not simply empty.","hintJa":"冷蔵庫が空なのではなく、故障して動いていない様子を見ましょう。","explanation":"“The refrigerator isn’t working.” is correct. The dark appliance and warming food show that the refrigerator is not operating. “Please put the milk in the fridge.” does not fit because that sentence means “牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Could you say that again?” does not fit because that sentence means “もう一度言っていただけますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Could you speak a little more slowly?” does not fit because that sentence means “もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「The refrigerator isn’t working.」（冷蔵庫が動いていません。）です。暗い庫内と温まり始めた食品が、冷蔵庫の停止を示しています。 「Please put the milk in the fridge.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Could you say that again?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「もう一度言っていただけますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Could you speak a little more slowly?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The refrigerator isn’t working.","jp":"冷蔵庫が動いていません。"},{"id":"b","en":"Please put the milk in the fridge.","jp":"牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。"},{"id":"c","en":"Could you say that again?","jp":"もう一度言っていただけますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"Could you speak a little more slowly?","jp":"もう少しゆっくり話していただけますか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-10-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A refrigerator has stopped working.","visualAssetId":"august-10-part-1-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"didn’t hear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The bell rang, but the person never noticed it.","hintJa":"ベルは鳴りましたが、家の人がその音に気づかなかった場面です。","explanation":"“I didn’t hear the doorbell.” is correct. Headphones prevent the resident from hearing the visitor’s doorbell. “The refrigerator isn’t working.” does not fit because that sentence means “冷蔵庫が動いていません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “The connection keeps cutting out.” does not fit because that sentence means “回線が何度も途切れます。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Let me reconnect and call you back.” does not fit because that sentence means “接続し直して、かけ直します。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I didn’t hear the doorbell.」（私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。）です。ヘッドホンのため、住人は訪問者のドアベルを聞いていません。 「The refrigerator isn’t working.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「冷蔵庫が動いていません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「The connection keeps cutting out.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「回線が何度も途切れます。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Let me reconnect and call you back.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「接続し直して、かけ直します。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I didn’t hear the doorbell.","jp":"私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"The refrigerator isn’t working.","jp":"冷蔵庫が動いていません。"},{"id":"c","en":"The connection keeps cutting out.","jp":"回線が何度も途切れます。"},{"id":"d","en":"Let me reconnect and call you back.","jp":"接続し直して、かけ直します。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-10-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"A person misses the sound of a doorbell.","visualAssetId":"august-10-part-1-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"phone trouble","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The connection disappears and returns repeatedly.","hintJa":"接続が何度も途切れて戻る様子に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“The connection keeps cutting out.” is correct. Repeated frozen fragments show a connection that keeps cutting out. “The ice cream is in the freezer.” does not fit because that sentence means “アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I didn’t hear the doorbell.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Can you hear me now?” does not fit because that sentence means “今は私の声が聞こえますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「The connection keeps cutting out.」（回線が何度も途切れます。）です。繰り返す映像の途切れが、回線が何度も切れていることを示しています。 「The ice cream is in the freezer.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I didn’t hear the doorbell.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Can you hear me now?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今は私の声が聞こえますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The connection keeps cutting out.","jp":"回線が何度も途切れます。"},{"id":"b","en":"The ice cream is in the freezer.","jp":"アイスクリームは冷凍庫にあります。"},{"id":"c","en":"I didn’t hear the doorbell.","jp":"私はドアベルの音に気づきませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"Can you hear me now?","jp":"今は私の声が聞こえますか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-10-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"An online call repeatedly cuts out.","visualAssetId":"august-10-part-1-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-1', 'august-10-part-1-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-1-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"phone trouble","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The person fixes the connection first and will call again afterward.","hintJa":"先に接続を直し、その後でもう一度電話する流れです。","explanation":"“Let me reconnect and call you back.” is correct. Resetting the connection followed by the callback gesture shows the two-step plan. “Please put the milk in the fridge.” does not fit because that sentence means “牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I couldn’t hear you clearly.” does not fit because that sentence means “あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “You’re breaking up.” does not fit because that sentence means “声が途切れ途切れです。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Let me reconnect and call you back.」（接続し直して、かけ直します。）です。接続の再設定と折り返しの仕草が、二段階の予定を示しています。 「Please put the milk in the fridge.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I couldn’t hear you clearly.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「You’re breaking up.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「声が途切れ途切れです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Let me reconnect and call you back.","jp":"接続し直して、かけ直します。"},{"id":"b","en":"Please put the milk in the fridge.","jp":"牛乳を冷蔵庫に入れてください。"},{"id":"c","en":"I couldn’t hear you clearly.","jp":"あなたの声がはっきり聞こえませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"You’re breaking up.","jp":"声が途切れ途切れです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-10-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A caller reconnects before calling back.","visualAssetId":"august-10-part-1-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"strong coffee","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the strong coffee meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。”.","hintJa":"strong は味や刺激が強いことを表します。","explanation":"“This coffee is too strong for me.” is the sentence that means “このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「This coffee is too strong for me.」が「このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。","promptJa":"「このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"This coffee is too strong for me.","jp":"このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。"},{"id":"b","en":"I prefer mild coffee.","jp":"私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I like bold coffee in the morning.","jp":"朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’ve never been to the Philippines.","jp":"私はフィリピンへ行ったことがありません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"mild coffee","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the mild coffee meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。”.","hintJa":"mild は刺激が強すぎない味です。","explanation":"“I prefer mild coffee.” is the sentence that means “私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I prefer mild coffee.」が「私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。","promptJa":"「私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I prefer mild coffee.","jp":"私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"It tastes a little bitter.","jp":"少し苦い味がします。"},{"id":"c","en":"This roast tastes light and slightly acidic.","jp":"この焙煎は軽くて少し酸味があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’d like to visit Cebu someday.","jp":"いつかセブを訪れたいです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"bitter","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the bitter meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “少し苦い味がします。”.","hintJa":"bitter は砂糖の甘さと対照的な苦味です。","explanation":"“It tastes a little bitter.” is the sentence that means “少し苦い味がします。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「It tastes a little bitter.」が「少し苦い味がします。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 少し苦い味がします。","promptJa":"「少し苦い味がします。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"It tastes a little bitter.","jp":"少し苦い味がします。"},{"id":"b","en":"This blend is smooth and rich.","jp":"このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。"},{"id":"c","en":"I haven’t decided where to go yet.","jp":"まだどこへ行くか決めていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m still comparing the flight prices.","jp":"まだ航空券の値段を比べています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"smooth and rich","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the smooth and rich meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。”.","hintJa":"smooth は口当たり、rich は深いコクを表します。","explanation":"“This blend is smooth and rich.” is the sentence that means “このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「This blend is smooth and rich.」が「このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。","promptJa":"「このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"This blend is smooth and rich.","jp":"このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。"},{"id":"b","en":"I like bold coffee in the morning.","jp":"朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"It will be my first time in the Philippines.","jp":"フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。"},{"id":"d","en":"Once I decide, I’ll book the ticket.","jp":"決めたら、航空券を予約します。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"bold","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the bold meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。”.","hintJa":"bold ははっきりした力強い風味です。","explanation":"True. “I like bold coffee in the morning.” means “朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「I like bold coffee in the morning.」は「朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。」という意味です。","prompt":"“I like bold coffee in the morning.” means “朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。”.","promptJa":"「I like bold coffee in the morning.」は「朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"light and acidic","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the light and acidic meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この焙煎は軽くて少し酸味があります。”.","hintJa":"light は軽い風味、acidic は酸味を表します。","explanation":"False. “This roast tastes light and slightly acidic.” means “この焙煎は軽くて少し酸味があります。”, not “まだどこへ行くか決めていません。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「This roast tastes light and slightly acidic.」は「この焙煎は軽くて少し酸味があります。」であり、「まだどこへ行くか決めていません。」ではありません。","prompt":"“This roast tastes light and slightly acidic.” means “まだどこへ行くか決めていません。”.","promptJa":"「This roast tastes light and slightly acidic.」は「まだどこへ行くか決めていません。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"not decided","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the not decided meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “まだどこへ行くか決めていません。”.","hintJa":"疑問詞 + to 不定詞で選択内容を表せます。","explanation":"A natural translation is “I haven’t decided where to go yet.”. It expresses “まだどこへ行くか決めていません。” with the lesson’s not decided pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「I haven’t decided where to go yet.」です。「まだどこへ行くか決めていません。」を今回のnot decided表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: まだどこへ行くか決めていません。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：まだどこへ行くか決めていません。","accepted":["I haven’t decided where to go yet."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"first time","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the first time meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。”.","hintJa":"未来の初体験には will be my first time が自然です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “It will be my first time in the Philippines.”. It expresses “フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。” with the lesson’s first time pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「It will be my first time in the Philippines.」です。「フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。」を今回のfirst time表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。","accepted":["It will be my first time in the Philippines."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-typing', 8, 'Build It', 'typing', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-typing","format":"typing","type":"typing","section":"Build It","topic":"future plan","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the future plan meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “決めたら、航空券を予約します。”.","hintJa":"未来の条件節では once の後に現在形を使います。","explanation":"A complete model answer is “Once I decide, I’ll book the ticket.”. Check the key future plan expression and every short grammar word.","explanationJa":"完全な答えは「Once I decide, I’ll book the ticket.」です。future planの中心表現と短い文法語まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete English sentence from memory: 決めたら、航空券を予約します。","promptJa":"日本語を見て、英文を最後まで入力してください：決めたら、航空券を予約します。","accepted":["Once I decide, I’ll book the ticket."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-order-1', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"travel experience","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the travel experience meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はフィリピンへ行ったことがありません。”.","hintJa":"have been to で訪問経験を表します。","explanation":"Correct order: “I’ve never been to the Philippines.”. Build the sentence around the travel experience pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I’ve never been to the Philippines.」です。travel experienceの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 私はフィリピンへ行ったことがありません。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：私はフィリピンへ行ったことがありません。","words":["to","the","Philippines","I’ve","never","been"],"correctWords":["I’ve","never","been","to","the","Philippines"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-order-2', 10, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"travel goal","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the travel goal meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “いつかセブを訪れたいです。”.","hintJa":"現実的な希望を丁寧に表します。","explanation":"Correct order: “I’d like to visit Cebu someday.”. Build the sentence around the travel goal pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I’d like to visit Cebu someday.」です。travel goalの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: いつかセブを訪れたいです。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：いつかセブを訪れたいです。","words":["visit","Cebu","someday","I’d","like","to"],"correctWords":["I’d","like","to","visit","Cebu","someday"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-matching', 11, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"strong coffee","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the strong coffee meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。”.","hintJa":"strong は味や刺激が強いことを表します。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"This coffee is too strong for me.","jp":"このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。","cat":"strong coffee"},{"en":"I prefer mild coffee.","jp":"私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。","cat":"mild coffee"},{"en":"It tastes a little bitter.","jp":"少し苦い味がします。","cat":"bitter"},{"en":"This blend is smooth and rich.","jp":"このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。","cat":"smooth and rich"},{"en":"I like bold coffee in the morning.","jp":"朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。","cat":"bold"},{"en":"This roast tastes light and slightly acidic.","jp":"この焙煎は軽くて少し酸味があります。","cat":"light and acidic"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-sorting', 12, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"mild coffee","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the mild coffee meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。”.","hintJa":"mild は刺激が強すぎない味です。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are strong coffee, mild coffee, bitter.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「strong coffee・mild coffee・bitter」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["strong coffee","mild coffee","bitter"],"items":[["This coffee is too strong for me.","strong coffee"],["I prefer mild coffee.","mild coffee"],["It tastes a little bitter.","bitter"]]}'::jsonb, false, 3),
