  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"planning","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the planning meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “まだ航空券の値段を比べています。”.","hintJa":"still で計画途中であることを示します。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “I’m still comparing the flight prices.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「I’m still comparing the flight prices.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"I still comparing the flight prices.","accepted":["I’m still comparing the flight prices."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"future plan","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the future plan meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “決めたら、航空券を予約します。”.","hintJa":"未来の条件節では once の後に現在形を使います。","explanation":"“Once I decide, I’ll book the ticket.” directly expresses “決めたら、航空券を予約します。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「Once I decide, I’ll book the ticket.」が「決めたら、航空券を予約します。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 決めたら、航空券を予約します。","promptJa":"「決めたら、航空券を予約します。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Once I decide, I’ll book the ticket.","jp":"決めたら、航空券を予約します。"},{"id":"b","en":"This coffee is too strong for me.","jp":"このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。"},{"id":"c","en":"This blend is smooth and rich.","jp":"このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。"},{"id":"d","en":"It will be my first time in the Philippines.","jp":"フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"strong coffee","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The coffee’s intensity is stronger than the drinker prefers.","hintJa":"飲む人の好みよりコーヒーの味が強いことに注目しましょう。","explanation":"“This coffee is too strong for me.” is correct. The dark brew and intense reaction show coffee that is too strong for the customer. “I prefer mild coffee.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “This roast tastes light and slightly acidic.” does not fit because that sentence means “この焙煎は軽くて少し酸味があります。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’d like to visit Cebu someday.” does not fit because that sentence means “いつかセブを訪れたいです。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「This coffee is too strong for me.」（このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。）です。濃い色のコーヒーと強い反応が、本人には濃すぎることを示しています。 「I prefer mild coffee.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「This roast tastes light and slightly acidic.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「この焙煎は軽くて少し酸味があります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’d like to visit Cebu someday.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「いつかセブを訪れたいです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"This coffee is too strong for me.","jp":"このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。"},{"id":"b","en":"I prefer mild coffee.","jp":"私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"This roast tastes light and slightly acidic.","jp":"この焙煎は軽くて少し酸味があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’d like to visit Cebu someday.","jp":"いつかセブを訪れたいです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-10-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A customer finds a cup of coffee too strong.","visualAssetId":"august-10-part-2-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"bitter","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The reaction shows mild bitterness, not sweetness or smoothness.","hintJa":"甘さや滑らかさではなく、少しの苦味への反応を見ましょう。","explanation":"“It tastes a little bitter.” is correct. The careful tasting expression indicates a modest bitter flavor. “This coffee is too strong for me.” does not fit because that sentence means “このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I haven’t decided where to go yet.” does not fit because that sentence means “まだどこへ行くか決めていません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Once I decide, I’ll book the ticket.” does not fit because that sentence means “決めたら、航空券を予約します。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「It tastes a little bitter.」（少し苦い味がします。）です。慎重に味わう表情が、少し苦い風味を示しています。 「This coffee is too strong for me.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I haven’t decided where to go yet.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「まだどこへ行くか決めていません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Once I decide, I’ll book the ticket.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「決めたら、航空券を予約します。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"It tastes a little bitter.","jp":"少し苦い味がします。"},{"id":"b","en":"This coffee is too strong for me.","jp":"このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。"},{"id":"c","en":"I haven’t decided where to go yet.","jp":"まだどこへ行くか決めていません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Once I decide, I’ll book the ticket.","jp":"決めたら、航空券を予約します。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-10-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A coffee drinker notices a slightly bitter taste.","visualAssetId":"august-10-part-2-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"bold","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Morning energy is linked to the stronger, more assertive flavor.","hintJa":"朝の元気と、より力強い風味の選択を結びつけましょう。","explanation":"“I like bold coffee in the morning.” is correct. The person deliberately selects the robust cup in the morning. “It tastes a little bitter.” does not fit because that sentence means “少し苦い味がします。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “It will be my first time in the Philippines.” does not fit because that sentence means “フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m still comparing the flight prices.” does not fit because that sentence means “まだ航空券の値段を比べています。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I like bold coffee in the morning.」（朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。）です。本人が朝に、力強い味のカップを意図的に選んでいます。 「It tastes a little bitter.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「少し苦い味がします。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「It will be my first time in the Philippines.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m still comparing the flight prices.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「まだ航空券の値段を比べています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I like bold coffee in the morning.","jp":"朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"It tastes a little bitter.","jp":"少し苦い味がします。"},{"id":"c","en":"It will be my first time in the Philippines.","jp":"フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m still comparing the flight prices.","jp":"まだ航空券の値段を比べています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-10-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"A person chooses a bold coffee for the morning.","visualAssetId":"august-10-part-2-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"first time","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The traveler is preparing for a destination they have never visited before.","hintJa":"これまで訪れたことのない目的地へ初めて向かう準備を見ましょう。","explanation":"“It will be my first time in the Philippines.” is correct. The new-trip cues and excitement show an upcoming first visit to the Philippines. “I prefer mild coffee.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I like bold coffee in the morning.” does not fit because that sentence means “朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’d like to visit Cebu someday.” does not fit because that sentence means “いつかセブを訪れたいです。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「It will be my first time in the Philippines.」（フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。）です。新しい旅の手がかりと喜ぶ姿が、フィリピンへの初訪問を示しています。 「I prefer mild coffee.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I like bold coffee in the morning.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’d like to visit Cebu someday.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「いつかセブを訪れたいです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"It will be my first time in the Philippines.","jp":"フィリピンへ行くのは初めてになります。"},{"id":"b","en":"I prefer mild coffee.","jp":"私はまろやかなコーヒーの方が好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I like bold coffee in the morning.","jp":"朝は力強い味のコーヒーが好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’d like to visit Cebu someday.","jp":"いつかセブを訪れたいです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-10-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"A traveler prepares for a first trip to the Philippines.","visualAssetId":"august-10-part-2-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-10-part-2', 'august-10-part-2-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-10-part-2-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"planning","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The decision is not finished because several flight prices are still being compared.","hintJa":"複数の航空券価格をまだ比較しており、決定が終わっていないことを見ましょう。","explanation":"“I’m still comparing the flight prices.” is correct. Several unselected flight options remain open while the traveler compares prices. “This coffee is too strong for me.” does not fit because that sentence means “このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “This blend is smooth and rich.” does not fit because that sentence means “このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’ve never been to the Philippines.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はフィリピンへ行ったことがありません。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I’m still comparing the flight prices.」（まだ航空券の値段を比べています。）です。複数の未選択の航空便を開いたまま、旅行者が価格を比べています。 「This coffee is too strong for me.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「This blend is smooth and rich.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’ve never been to the Philippines.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はフィリピンへ行ったことがありません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m still comparing the flight prices.","jp":"まだ航空券の値段を比べています。"},{"id":"b","en":"This coffee is too strong for me.","jp":"このコーヒーは私には濃すぎます。"},{"id":"c","en":"This blend is smooth and rich.","jp":"このブレンドは口当たりがよく、コクがあります。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’ve never been to the Philippines.","jp":"私はフィリピンへ行ったことがありません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-10-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A traveler compares several flight prices.","visualAssetId":"august-10-part-2-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"without asking","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the without asking meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。”.","hintJa":"「勝手に」は場面に応じて without asking で表せます。","explanation":"“He used my computer without asking.” is the sentence that means “彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「He used my computer without asking.」が「彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。","promptJa":"「彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He used my computer without asking.","jp":"彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。"},{"id":"b","en":"She decided on her own.","jp":"彼女は自分の判断で決めました。"},{"id":"c","en":"Could you do the dishes?","jp":"食器を洗ってもらえますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I caught a cold.","jp":"私は風邪をひきました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"on your own","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the on your own meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は自分の判断で決めました。”.","hintJa":"他人に頼らず決めたことを表します。","explanation":"“She decided on her own.” is the sentence that means “彼女は自分の判断で決めました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「She decided on her own.」が「彼女は自分の判断で決めました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼女は自分の判断で決めました。","promptJa":"「彼女は自分の判断で決めました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She decided on her own.","jp":"彼女は自分の判断で決めました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Don’t just help yourself to my food.","jp":"勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。"},{"id":"c","en":"I need to do some shopping.","jp":"買い物をする必要があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"I received your email this morning.","jp":"今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"help yourself","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the help yourself meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。”.","hintJa":"許可なく取る文脈では just と否定で不満を示せます。","explanation":"“Don’t just help yourself to my food.” is the sentence that means “勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Don’t just help yourself to my food.」が「勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。","promptJa":"「勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Don’t just help yourself to my food.","jp":"勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。"},{"id":"b","en":"We’re having a barbecue this weekend.","jp":"今週末にバーベキューをします。"},{"id":"c","en":"She did a great job.","jp":"彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I got your message.","jp":"メッセージを受け取りました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"have a barbecue","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the have a barbecue meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今週末にバーベキューをします。”.","hintJa":"行事としてのBBQには have が自然です。","explanation":"“We’re having a barbecue this weekend.” is the sentence that means “今週末にバーベキューをします。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「We’re having a barbecue this weekend.」が「今週末にバーベキューをします。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 今週末にバーベキューをします。","promptJa":"「今週末にバーベキューをします。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"We’re having a barbecue this weekend.","jp":"今週末にバーベキューをします。"},{"id":"b","en":"Could you do the dishes?","jp":"食器を洗ってもらえますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I caught the last train.","jp":"私は終電に間に合いました。"},{"id":"d","en":"Did you get home safely?","jp":"無事に家に着きましたか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"do collocations","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the do collocations meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “食器を洗ってもらえますか？”.","hintJa":"家事には do the dishes を使います。","explanation":"True. “Could you do the dishes?” means “食器を洗ってもらえますか？”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「Could you do the dishes?」は「食器を洗ってもらえますか？」という意味です。","prompt":"“Could you do the dishes?” means “食器を洗ってもらえますか？”.","promptJa":"「Could you do the dishes?」は「食器を洗ってもらえますか？」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"do collocations","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the do collocations meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “買い物をする必要があります。”.","hintJa":"一般的な買い物活動には do some shopping が自然です。","explanation":"False. “I need to do some shopping.” means “買い物をする必要があります。”, not “彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「I need to do some shopping.」は「買い物をする必要があります。」であり、「彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。」ではありません。","prompt":"“I need to do some shopping.” means “彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。”.","promptJa":"「I need to do some shopping.」は「彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"do collocations","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the do collocations meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。”.","hintJa":"成果を褒める定番表現です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “She did a great job.”. It expresses “彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。” with the lesson’s do collocations pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「She did a great job.」です。「彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。」を今回のdo collocations表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。","accepted":["She did a great job."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"catch","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the catch meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は終電に間に合いました。”.","hintJa":"乗り物に間に合って乗る時は catch です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “I caught the last train.”. It expresses “私は終電に間に合いました。” with the lesson’s catch pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「I caught the last train.」です。「私は終電に間に合いました。」を今回のcatch表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 私は終電に間に合いました。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：私は終電に間に合いました。","accepted":["I caught the last train."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-typing', 8, 'Build It', 'typing', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-typing","format":"typing","type":"typing","section":"Build It","topic":"get","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the get meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “無事に家に着きましたか？”.","hintJa":"get home は「帰宅する・家に着く」です。","explanation":"A complete model answer is “Did you get home safely?”. Check the key get expression and every short grammar word.","explanationJa":"完全な答えは「Did you get home safely?」です。getの中心表現と短い文法語まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete English sentence from memory: 無事に家に着きましたか？","promptJa":"日本語を見て、英文を最後まで入力してください：無事に家に着きましたか？","accepted":["Did you get home safely?"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-order-1', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"catch","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the catch meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は風邪をひきました。”.","hintJa":"病気になることを catch a cold と言います。","explanation":"Correct order: “I caught a cold.”. Build the sentence around the catch pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I caught a cold.」です。catchの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 私は風邪をひきました。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：私は風邪をひきました。","words":["cold","a","caught","I"],"correctWords":["I","caught","a","cold"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-order-2', 10, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"receive","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the receive meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。”.","hintJa":"receive は少し改まった「受け取る」です。","explanation":"Correct order: “I received your email this morning.”. Build the sentence around the receive pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I received your email this morning.」です。receiveの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。","words":["email","this","morning","I","received","your"],"correctWords":["I","received","your","email","this","morning"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-matching', 11, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"without asking","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the without asking meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。”.","hintJa":"「勝手に」は場面に応じて without asking で表せます。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"He used my computer without asking.","jp":"彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。","cat":"without asking"},{"en":"She decided on her own.","jp":"彼女は自分の判断で決めました。","cat":"on your own"},{"en":"Don’t just help yourself to my food.","jp":"勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。","cat":"help yourself"},{"en":"We’re having a barbecue this weekend.","jp":"今週末にバーベキューをします。","cat":"have a barbecue"},{"en":"Could you do the dishes?","jp":"食器を洗ってもらえますか？","cat":"do collocations"},{"en":"I need to do some shopping.","jp":"買い物をする必要があります。","cat":"do collocations"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-sorting', 12, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"on your own","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the on your own meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は自分の判断で決めました。”.","hintJa":"他人に頼らず決めたことを表します。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are without asking, on your own, help yourself.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「without asking・on your own・help yourself」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["without asking","on your own","help yourself"],"items":[["He used my computer without asking.","without asking"],["She decided on her own.","on your own"],["Don’t just help yourself to my food.","help yourself"]]}'::jsonb, false, 3),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-grid', 13, 'Build It', 'grid', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-grid","format":"grid","type":"grid","section":"Build It","topic":"do collocations","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the do collocations meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “食器を洗ってもらえますか？”.","hintJa":"家事には do the dishes を使います。","explanation":"The center tile, “Could you do the dishes?”, means “食器を洗ってもらえますか？”. Read every complete phrase before choosing its position.","explanationJa":"中央の「Could you do the dishes?」が「食器を洗ってもらえますか？」を表します。位置だけでなく、各英文の意味を最後まで読んで選びましょう。","prompt":"Select the tile that means: 食器を洗ってもらえますか？","promptJa":"「食器を洗ってもらえますか？」を表す英文のタイルを選んでください。","correctCell":"center","gridCells":{"top-left":"He used my computer without asking.","top-center":"She decided on her own.","top-right":"Don’t just help yourself to my food.","middle-left":"We’re having a barbecue this weekend.","center":"Could you do the dishes?","middle-right":"I need to do some shopping.","bottom-left":"She did a great job.","bottom-center":"I caught the last train.","bottom-right":"I caught a cold."}}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-listen-choice-1', 14, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-listen-choice-1","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"without asking","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the without asking meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。”.","hintJa":"「勝手に」は場面に応じて without asking で表せます。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “He used my computer without asking.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「He used my computer without asking.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"He used my computer without asking.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He used my computer without asking.","jp":"彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。"},{"id":"b","en":"She decided on her own.","jp":"彼女は自分の判断で決めました。"},{"id":"c","en":"Could you do the dishes?","jp":"食器を洗ってもらえますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I caught a cold.","jp":"私は風邪をひきました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-listen-choice-2', 15, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-listen-choice-2","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"have a barbecue","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the have a barbecue meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今週末にバーベキューをします。”.","hintJa":"行事としてのBBQには have が自然です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “We’re having a barbecue this weekend.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「We’re having a barbecue this weekend.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"We’re having a barbecue this weekend.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"We’re having a barbecue this weekend.","jp":"今週末にバーベキューをします。"},{"id":"b","en":"Could you do the dishes?","jp":"食器を洗ってもらえますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I caught the last train.","jp":"私は終電に間に合いました。"},{"id":"d","en":"Did you get home safely?","jp":"無事に家に着きましたか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-listen-choice-3', 16, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-listen-choice-3","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"do collocations","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the do collocations meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。”.","hintJa":"成果を褒める定番表現です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “She did a great job.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「She did a great job.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"She did a great job.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She did a great job.","jp":"彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I caught the last train.","jp":"私は終電に間に合いました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I got your message.","jp":"メッセージを受け取りました。"},{"id":"d","en":"Don’t just help yourself to my food.","jp":"勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-dictation-1', 17, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-dictation-1","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"on your own","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the on your own meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女は自分の判断で決めました。”.","hintJa":"他人に頼らず決めたことを表します。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “She decided on her own.”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「She decided on her own.」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"She decided on her own.","accepted":["She decided on her own."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
