  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-dictation-3', 19, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-dictation-3","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"catch","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the catch meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は終電に間に合いました。”.","hintJa":"乗り物に間に合って乗る時は catch です。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “I caught the last train.”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「I caught the last train.」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"I caught the last train.","accepted":["I caught the last train."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-speaking-1', 20, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-speaking-1","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"help yourself","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the help yourself meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。”.","hintJa":"許可なく取る文脈では just と否定で不満を示せます。","explanation":"Model: “Don’t just help yourself to my food.” (勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Don’t just help yourself to my food.」（勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"Don’t just help yourself to my food.","speakJa":"勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-speaking-2', 21, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-speaking-2","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"do collocations","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the do collocations meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “買い物をする必要があります。”.","hintJa":"一般的な買い物活動には do some shopping が自然です。","explanation":"Model: “I need to do some shopping.” (買い物をする必要があります。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I need to do some shopping.」（買い物をする必要があります。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"I need to do some shopping.","speakJa":"買い物をする必要があります。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-speaking-3', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"catch","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the catch meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は風邪をひきました。”.","hintJa":"病気になることを catch a cold と言います。","explanation":"Model: “I caught a cold.” (私は風邪をひきました。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I caught a cold.」（私は風邪をひきました。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"I caught a cold.","speakJa":"私は風邪をひきました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-speaking-4', 23, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"receive","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the receive meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。”.","hintJa":"receive は少し改まった「受け取る」です。","explanation":"Model: “I received your email this morning.” (今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I received your email this morning.」（今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I received your email this morning.","speakJa":"今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"get","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the get meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “メッセージを受け取りました。”.","hintJa":"会話では get が自然で、「内容を理解した」の意味にもなります。","explanation":"Model: “I got your message.” (メッセージを受け取りました。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I got your message.」（メッセージを受け取りました。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I got your message.","speakJa":"メッセージを受け取りました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"receive","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the receive meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。”.","hintJa":"receive は少し改まった「受け取る」です。","explanation":"“I received your email this morning.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「I received your email this morning.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: I caught a cold.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: 私は風邪をひきました。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I received your email this morning.","jp":"今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I got your message.","jp":"メッセージを受け取りました。"},{"id":"c","en":"She decided on her own.","jp":"彼女は自分の判断で決めました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I need to do some shopping.","jp":"買い物をする必要があります。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"get","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the get meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “メッセージを受け取りました。”.","hintJa":"会話では get が自然で、「内容を理解した」の意味にもなります。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “I got your message.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「I got your message.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"I got your message yesterday now.","accepted":["I got your message."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"get","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the get meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “無事に家に着きましたか？”.","hintJa":"get home は「帰宅する・家に着く」です。","explanation":"“Did you get home safely?” directly expresses “無事に家に着きましたか？”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「Did you get home safely?」が「無事に家に着きましたか？」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 無事に家に着きましたか？","promptJa":"「無事に家に着きましたか？」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Did you get home safely?","jp":"無事に家に着きましたか？"},{"id":"b","en":"He used my computer without asking.","jp":"彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。"},{"id":"c","en":"We’re having a barbecue this weekend.","jp":"今週末にバーベキューをします。"},{"id":"d","en":"I caught the last train.","jp":"私は終電に間に合いました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"without asking","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The owner is surprised because permission was never requested.","hintJa":"許可を求められていなかったため、持ち主が驚いている場面です。","explanation":"“He used my computer without asking.” is correct. The colleague is already using the owner’s computer despite never asking. “She decided on her own.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼女は自分の判断で決めました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I need to do some shopping.” does not fit because that sentence means “買い物をする必要があります。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I received your email this morning.” does not fit because that sentence means “今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「He used my computer without asking.」（彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。）です。同僚は持ち主に尋ねないまま、そのパソコンを使っています。 「She decided on her own.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼女は自分の判断で決めました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I need to do some shopping.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「買い物をする必要があります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I received your email this morning.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He used my computer without asking.","jp":"彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。"},{"id":"b","en":"She decided on her own.","jp":"彼女は自分の判断で決めました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I need to do some shopping.","jp":"買い物をする必要があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"I received your email this morning.","jp":"今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-16-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"Someone uses another person’s computer without asking.","visualAssetId":"august-16-part-1-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"help yourself","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The problem is taking another person’s food as if it were freely available.","hintJa":"他人の食べ物を自由に取ってよい物のように扱っている点を見ましょう。","explanation":"“Don’t just help yourself to my food.” is correct. The guest takes food from the owner’s plate without being invited. “He used my computer without asking.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “She did a great job.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Did you get home safely?” does not fit because that sentence means “無事に家に着きましたか？,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Don’t just help yourself to my food.」（勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。）です。客が勧められていないのに、持ち主の皿から食べ物を取っています。 「He used my computer without asking.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「She did a great job.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Did you get home safely?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「無事に家に着きましたか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Don’t just help yourself to my food.","jp":"勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。"},{"id":"b","en":"He used my computer without asking.","jp":"彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。"},{"id":"c","en":"She did a great job.","jp":"彼女は素晴らしい仕事をしました。"},{"id":"d","en":"Did you get home safely?","jp":"無事に家に着きましたか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-16-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A guest takes someone else’s food without permission.","visualAssetId":"august-16-part-1-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"do collocations","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The requested household task involves the used plates in the sink.","hintJa":"頼まれている家事が、流しの使用済み食器に関係していることを見ましょう。","explanation":"“Could you do the dishes?” is correct. The speaker points directly to dishes waiting to be washed. “Don’t just help yourself to my food.” does not fit because that sentence means “勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I caught the last train.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は終電に間に合いました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I got your message.” does not fit because that sentence means “メッセージを受け取りました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Could you do the dishes?」（食器を洗ってもらえますか？）です。話し手が洗う必要のある食器を直接指しています。 「Don’t just help yourself to my food.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I caught the last train.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は終電に間に合いました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I got your message.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「メッセージを受け取りました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Could you do the dishes?","jp":"食器を洗ってもらえますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Don’t just help yourself to my food.","jp":"勝手に私の食べ物を取らないでください。"},{"id":"c","en":"I caught the last train.","jp":"私は終電に間に合いました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I got your message.","jp":"メッセージを受け取りました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-16-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"A housemate asks someone to wash the dishes.","visualAssetId":"august-16-part-1-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"catch","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The traveler reaches the final train just in time.","hintJa":"最後の電車にぎりぎり間に合って乗る様子を見ましょう。","explanation":"“I caught the last train.” is correct. The commuter boards the last train before its doors close. “She decided on her own.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼女は自分の判断で決めました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Could you do the dishes?” does not fit because that sentence means “食器を洗ってもらえますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I received your email this morning.” does not fit because that sentence means “今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I caught the last train.」（私は終電に間に合いました。）です。通勤客はドアが閉まる前に終電へ乗り込んでいます。 「She decided on her own.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼女は自分の判断で決めました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Could you do the dishes?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「食器を洗ってもらえますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I received your email this morning.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I caught the last train.","jp":"私は終電に間に合いました。"},{"id":"b","en":"She decided on her own.","jp":"彼女は自分の判断で決めました。"},{"id":"c","en":"Could you do the dishes?","jp":"食器を洗ってもらえますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I received your email this morning.","jp":"今朝あなたのメールを受け取りました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-16-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"A commuter catches the last train.","visualAssetId":"august-16-part-1-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-1', 'august-16-part-1-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-1-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"get","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The message has been received and understood.","hintJa":"メッセージを受け取り、内容も理解した反応に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I got your message.” is correct. The visible message and confirming nod show successful receipt and understanding. “He used my computer without asking.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “We’re having a barbecue this weekend.” does not fit because that sentence means “今週末にバーベキューをします。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I caught a cold.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は風邪をひきました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I got your message.」（メッセージを受け取りました。）です。表示されたメッセージと確認のうなずきが、受信と理解を示しています。 「He used my computer without asking.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「We’re having a barbecue this weekend.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今週末にバーベキューをします。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I caught a cold.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は風邪をひきました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I got your message.","jp":"メッセージを受け取りました。"},{"id":"b","en":"He used my computer without asking.","jp":"彼は私に断らず勝手にパソコンを使いました。"},{"id":"c","en":"We’re having a barbecue this weekend.","jp":"今週末にバーベキューをします。"},{"id":"d","en":"I caught a cold.","jp":"私は風邪をひきました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-16-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A person confirms receiving a message.","visualAssetId":"august-16-part-1-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"weight","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the weight meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “少し体重が増えました。”.","hintJa":"put on weight は日常会話で自然な表現です。","explanation":"“I’ve put on a little weight.” is the sentence that means “少し体重が増えました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I’ve put on a little weight.」が「少し体重が増えました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 少し体重が増えました。","promptJa":"「少し体重が増えました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve put on a little weight.","jp":"少し体重が増えました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m trying to lose weight.","jp":"体重を減らそうとしています。"},{"id":"c","en":"We need to cut the budget.","jp":"予算を削減する必要があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"I can’t hear you over the noise.","jp":"騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"weight","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the weight meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “体重を減らそうとしています。”.","hintJa":"lose weight で減量を表します。","explanation":"“I’m trying to lose weight.” is the sentence that means “体重を減らそうとしています。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I’m trying to lose weight.」が「体重を減らそうとしています。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 体重を減らそうとしています。","promptJa":"「体重を減らそうとしています。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m trying to lose weight.","jp":"体重を減らそうとしています。"},{"id":"b","en":"The company is growing quickly.","jp":"その会社は急速に成長しています。"},{"id":"c","en":"It’s hard to concentrate here.","jp":"ここでは集中するのが難しいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"It’s raining heavily.","jp":"激しく雨が降っています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"growth","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the growth meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その会社は急速に成長しています。”.","hintJa":"組織や事業の成長には grow を使えます。","explanation":"“The company is growing quickly.” is the sentence that means “その会社は急速に成長しています。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「The company is growing quickly.」が「その会社は急速に成長しています。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: その会社は急速に成長しています。","promptJa":"「その会社は急速に成長しています。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The company is growing quickly.","jp":"その会社は急速に成長しています。"},{"id":"b","en":"They increased the budget.","jp":"彼らは予算を増やしました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I received a certificate after the course.","jp":"講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。"},{"id":"d","en":"We had heavy rain last night.","jp":"昨夜は大雨でした。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"budget","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the budget meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼らは予算を増やしました。”.","hintJa":"increase は数値や量を増やすことです。","explanation":"“They increased the budget.” is the sentence that means “彼らは予算を増やしました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「They increased the budget.」が「彼らは予算を増やしました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼らは予算を増やしました。","promptJa":"「彼らは予算を増やしました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"They increased the budget.","jp":"彼らは予算を増やしました。"},{"id":"b","en":"We need to cut the budget.","jp":"予算を削減する必要があります。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m satisfied with the result.","jp":"私は結果に満足しています。"},{"id":"d","en":"I could hardly hear him.","jp":"彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"budget","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the budget meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “予算を削減する必要があります。”.","hintJa":"cut the budget は予算を減らす自然な組み合わせです。","explanation":"True. “We need to cut the budget.” means “予算を削減する必要があります。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「We need to cut the budget.」は「予算を削減する必要があります。」という意味です。","prompt":"“We need to cut the budget.” means “予算を削減する必要があります。”.","promptJa":"「We need to cut the budget.」は「予算を削減する必要があります。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"concentrate","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the concentrate meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ここでは集中するのが難しいです。”.","hintJa":"concentrate は動詞、concentration は名詞です。","explanation":"False. “It’s hard to concentrate here.” means “ここでは集中するのが難しいです。”, not “講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「It’s hard to concentrate here.」は「ここでは集中するのが難しいです。」であり、「講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。」ではありません。","prompt":"“It’s hard to concentrate here.” means “講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。”.","promptJa":"「It’s hard to concentrate here.」は「講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"certificate","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the certificate meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。”.","hintJa":"certificate は資格・修了を示す証明書です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “I received a certificate after the course.”. It expresses “講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。” with the lesson’s certificate pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「I received a certificate after the course.」です。「講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。」を今回のcertificate表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。","accepted":["I received a certificate after the course."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"satisfied","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the satisfied meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は結果に満足しています。”.","hintJa":"人の気持ちは satisfied、満足させる物は satisfying です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “I’m satisfied with the result.”. It expresses “私は結果に満足しています。” with the lesson’s satisfied pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「I’m satisfied with the result.」です。「私は結果に満足しています。」を今回のsatisfied表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 私は結果に満足しています。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：私は結果に満足しています。","accepted":["I’m satisfied with the result."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-typing', 8, 'Build It', 'typing', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-typing","format":"typing","type":"typing","section":"Build It","topic":"hardly","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the hardly meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。”.","hintJa":"hardly は「ほとんど〜ない」で、hard「一生懸命」と意味が違います。","explanation":"A complete model answer is “I could hardly hear him.”. Check the key hardly expression and every short grammar word.","explanationJa":"完全な答えは「I could hardly hear him.」です。hardlyの中心表現と短い文法語まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete English sentence from memory: 彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。","promptJa":"日本語を見て、英文を最後まで入力してください：彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。","accepted":["I could hardly hear him."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-order-1', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"can’t hear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the can’t hear meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。”.","hintJa":"今この瞬間に聞こえない状況を表します。","explanation":"Correct order: “I can’t hear you over the noise.”. Build the sentence around the can’t hear pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I can’t hear you over the noise.」です。can’t hearの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。","words":["I","can’t","hear","you","over","the","noise"],"correctWords":["I","can’t","hear","you","over","the","noise"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-order-2', 10, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"heavy rain","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the heavy rain meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “激しく雨が降っています。”.","hintJa":"動詞 rain は副詞 heavily で修飾します。","explanation":"Correct order: “It’s raining heavily.”. Build the sentence around the heavy rain pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「It’s raining heavily.」です。heavy rainの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 激しく雨が降っています。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：激しく雨が降っています。","words":["It’s","raining","heavily"],"correctWords":["It’s","raining","heavily"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-matching', 11, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"weight","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the weight meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “少し体重が増えました。”.","hintJa":"put on weight は日常会話で自然な表現です。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"I’ve put on a little weight.","jp":"少し体重が増えました。","cat":"weight"},{"en":"I’m trying to lose weight.","jp":"体重を減らそうとしています。","cat":"weight"},{"en":"The company is growing quickly.","jp":"その会社は急速に成長しています。","cat":"growth"},{"en":"They increased the budget.","jp":"彼らは予算を増やしました。","cat":"budget"},{"en":"We need to cut the budget.","jp":"予算を削減する必要があります。","cat":"budget"},{"en":"It’s hard to concentrate here.","jp":"ここでは集中するのが難しいです。","cat":"concentrate"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-sorting', 12, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"weight","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the weight meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “体重を減らそうとしています。”.","hintJa":"lose weight で減量を表します。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are weight, growth, budget.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「weight・growth・budget」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["weight","growth","budget"],"items":[["I’ve put on a little weight.","weight"],["I’m trying to lose weight.","weight"],["The company is growing quickly.","growth"],["They increased the budget.","budget"],["We need to cut the budget.","budget"]]}'::jsonb, false, 5),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-grid', 13, 'Build It', 'grid', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-grid","format":"grid","type":"grid","section":"Build It","topic":"budget","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the budget meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “予算を削減する必要があります。”.","hintJa":"cut the budget は予算を減らす自然な組み合わせです。","explanation":"The center tile, “We need to cut the budget.”, means “予算を削減する必要があります。”. Read every complete phrase before choosing its position.","explanationJa":"中央の「We need to cut the budget.」が「予算を削減する必要があります。」を表します。位置だけでなく、各英文の意味を最後まで読んで選びましょう。","prompt":"Select the tile that means: 予算を削減する必要があります。","promptJa":"「予算を削減する必要があります。」を表す英文のタイルを選んでください。","correctCell":"center","gridCells":{"top-left":"I’ve put on a little weight.","top-center":"I’m trying to lose weight.","top-right":"The company is growing quickly.","middle-left":"They increased the budget.","center":"We need to cut the budget.","middle-right":"It’s hard to concentrate here.","bottom-left":"I received a certificate after the course.","bottom-center":"I’m satisfied with the result.","bottom-right":"I can’t hear you over the noise."}}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-listen-choice-1', 14, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-listen-choice-1","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"weight","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the weight meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “少し体重が増えました。”.","hintJa":"put on weight は日常会話で自然な表現です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “I’ve put on a little weight.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「I’ve put on a little weight.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"I’ve put on a little weight.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve put on a little weight.","jp":"少し体重が増えました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m trying to lose weight.","jp":"体重を減らそうとしています。"},{"id":"c","en":"We need to cut the budget.","jp":"予算を削減する必要があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"I can’t hear you over the noise.","jp":"騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-listen-choice-2', 15, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-listen-choice-2","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"budget","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the budget meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼らは予算を増やしました。”.","hintJa":"increase は数値や量を増やすことです。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “They increased the budget.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「They increased the budget.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"They increased the budget.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"They increased the budget.","jp":"彼らは予算を増やしました。"},{"id":"b","en":"We need to cut the budget.","jp":"予算を削減する必要があります。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m satisfied with the result.","jp":"私は結果に満足しています。"},{"id":"d","en":"I could hardly hear him.","jp":"彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-listen-choice-3', 16, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-listen-choice-3","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"certificate","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the certificate meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。”.","hintJa":"certificate は資格・修了を示す証明書です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “I received a certificate after the course.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「I received a certificate after the course.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"I received a certificate after the course.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I received a certificate after the course.","jp":"講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m satisfied with the result.","jp":"私は結果に満足しています。"},{"id":"c","en":"We had heavy rain last night.","jp":"昨夜は大雨でした。"},{"id":"d","en":"The company is growing quickly.","jp":"その会社は急速に成長しています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
