  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-dictation-2', 18, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-dictation-2","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"budget","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the budget meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “予算を削減する必要があります。”.","hintJa":"cut the budget は予算を減らす自然な組み合わせです。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “We need to cut the budget.”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「We need to cut the budget.」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"We need to cut the budget.","accepted":["We need to cut the budget."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-dictation-3', 19, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-dictation-3","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"satisfied","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the satisfied meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は結果に満足しています。”.","hintJa":"人の気持ちは satisfied、満足させる物は satisfying です。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “I’m satisfied with the result.”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「I’m satisfied with the result.」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"I’m satisfied with the result.","accepted":["I’m satisfied with the result."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-speaking-1', 20, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-speaking-1","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"growth","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the growth meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その会社は急速に成長しています。”.","hintJa":"組織や事業の成長には grow を使えます。","explanation":"Model: “The company is growing quickly.” (その会社は急速に成長しています。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「The company is growing quickly.」（その会社は急速に成長しています。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"The company is growing quickly.","speakJa":"その会社は急速に成長しています。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-speaking-2', 21, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-speaking-2","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"concentrate","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the concentrate meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ここでは集中するのが難しいです。”.","hintJa":"concentrate は動詞、concentration は名詞です。","explanation":"Model: “It’s hard to concentrate here.” (ここでは集中するのが難しいです。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「It’s hard to concentrate here.」（ここでは集中するのが難しいです。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"It’s hard to concentrate here.","speakJa":"ここでは集中するのが難しいです。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-speaking-3', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"can’t hear","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the can’t hear meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。”.","hintJa":"今この瞬間に聞こえない状況を表します。","explanation":"Model: “I can’t hear you over the noise.” (騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I can’t hear you over the noise.」（騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"I can’t hear you over the noise.","speakJa":"騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-speaking-4', 23, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"heavy rain","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the heavy rain meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “激しく雨が降っています。”.","hintJa":"動詞 rain は副詞 heavily で修飾します。","explanation":"Model: “It’s raining heavily.” (激しく雨が降っています。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「It’s raining heavily.」（激しく雨が降っています。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"It’s raining heavily.","speakJa":"激しく雨が降っています。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"heavy rain","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the heavy rain meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “昨夜は大雨でした。”.","hintJa":"名詞 rain の前には形容詞 heavy を置きます。","explanation":"Model: “We had heavy rain last night.” (昨夜は大雨でした。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「We had heavy rain last night.」（昨夜は大雨でした。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"We had heavy rain last night.","speakJa":"昨夜は大雨でした。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"heavy rain","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the heavy rain meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “激しく雨が降っています。”.","hintJa":"動詞 rain は副詞 heavily で修飾します。","explanation":"“It’s raining heavily.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「It’s raining heavily.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: I can’t hear you over the noise.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: 騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"It’s raining heavily.","jp":"激しく雨が降っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"We had heavy rain last night.","jp":"昨夜は大雨でした。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m trying to lose weight.","jp":"体重を減らそうとしています。"},{"id":"d","en":"It’s hard to concentrate here.","jp":"ここでは集中するのが難しいです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"heavy rain","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the heavy rain meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “昨夜は大雨でした。”.","hintJa":"名詞 rain の前には形容詞 heavy を置きます。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “We had heavy rain last night.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「We had heavy rain last night.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"We heavy rain last night.","accepted":["We had heavy rain last night."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"hardly","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the hardly meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。”.","hintJa":"hardly は「ほとんど〜ない」で、hard「一生懸命」と意味が違います。","explanation":"“I could hardly hear him.” directly expresses “彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「I could hardly hear him.」が「彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。","promptJa":"「彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I could hardly hear him.","jp":"彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve put on a little weight.","jp":"少し体重が増えました。"},{"id":"c","en":"They increased the budget.","jp":"彼らは予算を増やしました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m satisfied with the result.","jp":"私は結果に満足しています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"weight","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The scale shows a modest increase, not an effort to reduce weight.","hintJa":"減量の努力ではなく、体重が少し増えた結果を見ましょう。","explanation":"“I’ve put on a little weight.” is correct. The scale and tighter fit show that a little weight has been gained. “I’m trying to lose weight.” does not fit because that sentence means “体重を減らそうとしています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “It’s hard to concentrate here.” does not fit because that sentence means “ここでは集中するのが難しいです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “It’s raining heavily.” does not fit because that sentence means “激しく雨が降っています。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I’ve put on a little weight.」（少し体重が増えました。）です。体重計と少しきつい服が、わずかな体重増加を示しています。 「I’m trying to lose weight.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「体重を減らそうとしています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「It’s hard to concentrate here.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「ここでは集中するのが難しいです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「It’s raining heavily.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「激しく雨が降っています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve put on a little weight.","jp":"少し体重が増えました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m trying to lose weight.","jp":"体重を減らそうとしています。"},{"id":"c","en":"It’s hard to concentrate here.","jp":"ここでは集中するのが難しいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"It’s raining heavily.","jp":"激しく雨が降っています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-16-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A person notices a small weight gain.","visualAssetId":"august-16-part-2-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"growth","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Look for expansion of the business rather than a personal weight change.","hintJa":"個人の体重変化ではなく、事業が拡大している様子を見ましょう。","explanation":"“The company is growing quickly.” is correct. More staff, customers and upward movement show rapid company growth. “I’ve put on a little weight.” does not fit because that sentence means “少し体重が増えました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I received a certificate after the course.” does not fit because that sentence means “講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I could hardly hear him.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「The company is growing quickly.」（その会社は急速に成長しています。）です。増えた従業員と顧客、上向きの動きが会社の急成長を示しています。 「I’ve put on a little weight.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「少し体重が増えました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I received a certificate after the course.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I could hardly hear him.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The company is growing quickly.","jp":"その会社は急速に成長しています。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve put on a little weight.","jp":"少し体重が増えました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I received a certificate after the course.","jp":"講座の後に修了証を受け取りました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I could hardly hear him.","jp":"彼の声がほとんど聞こえませんでした。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-16-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A small company grows quickly.","visualAssetId":"august-16-part-2-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"budget","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Expenses are being removed so the total becomes smaller.","hintJa":"支出項目を外し、合計を小さくしていることに注目しましょう。","explanation":"“We need to cut the budget.” is correct. The team cuts optional costs and visibly lowers the budget total. “The company is growing quickly.” does not fit because that sentence means “その会社は急速に成長しています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m satisfied with the result.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は結果に満足しています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “We had heavy rain last night.” does not fit because that sentence means “昨夜は大雨でした。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「We need to cut the budget.」（予算を削減する必要があります。）です。チームが不要な費用を削り、予算総額を下げています。 「The company is growing quickly.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「その会社は急速に成長しています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m satisfied with the result.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は結果に満足しています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「We had heavy rain last night.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「昨夜は大雨でした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"We need to cut the budget.","jp":"予算を削減する必要があります。"},{"id":"b","en":"The company is growing quickly.","jp":"その会社は急速に成長しています。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m satisfied with the result.","jp":"私は結果に満足しています。"},{"id":"d","en":"We had heavy rain last night.","jp":"昨夜は大雨でした。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-16-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"A team reduces its budget.","visualAssetId":"august-16-part-2-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"satisfied","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The person’s feeling comes from a result they are pleased with.","hintJa":"良い結果に対して本人が満足している気持ちを見ましょう。","explanation":"“I’m satisfied with the result.” is correct. The completed result and pleased expression show satisfaction. “I’m trying to lose weight.” does not fit because that sentence means “体重を減らそうとしています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “We need to cut the budget.” does not fit because that sentence means “予算を削減する必要があります。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “It’s raining heavily.” does not fit because that sentence means “激しく雨が降っています。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I’m satisfied with the result.」（私は結果に満足しています。）です。完成した成果と満足した表情が、結果への満足を示しています。 「I’m trying to lose weight.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「体重を減らそうとしています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「We need to cut the budget.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「予算を削減する必要があります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「It’s raining heavily.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「激しく雨が降っています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m satisfied with the result.","jp":"私は結果に満足しています。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m trying to lose weight.","jp":"体重を減らそうとしています。"},{"id":"c","en":"We need to cut the budget.","jp":"予算を削減する必要があります。"},{"id":"d","en":"It’s raining heavily.","jp":"激しく雨が降っています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-16-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"A learner is satisfied with a successful result.","visualAssetId":"august-16-part-2-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-16-part-2', 'august-16-part-2-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-16-part-2-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"heavy rain","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The image shows the noun phrase for a large amount of rain last night.","hintJa":"昨夜の大量の雨を、名詞を中心に表す場面です。","explanation":"“We had heavy rain last night.” is correct. The night setting and intense rainfall clearly show heavy rain last night. “I’ve put on a little weight.” does not fit because that sentence means “少し体重が増えました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “They increased the budget.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼らは予算を増やしました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I can’t hear you over the noise.” does not fit because that sentence means “騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「We had heavy rain last night.」（昨夜は大雨でした。）です。夜の場面と激しい降雨が、昨夜の大雨をはっきり示しています。 「I’ve put on a little weight.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「少し体重が増えました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「They increased the budget.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼らは予算を増やしました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I can’t hear you over the noise.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"We had heavy rain last night.","jp":"昨夜は大雨でした。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve put on a little weight.","jp":"少し体重が増えました。"},{"id":"c","en":"They increased the budget.","jp":"彼らは予算を増やしました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I can’t hear you over the noise.","jp":"騒音であなたの声が聞こえません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-16-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"Heavy rain falls at night.","visualAssetId":"august-16-part-2-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"since","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the since meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。”.","hintJa":"状態を表す have a headache は現在完了が自然です。","explanation":"“I’ve had a headache since this morning.” is the sentence that means “今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I’ve had a headache since this morning.」が「今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。","promptJa":"「今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve had a headache since this morning.","jp":"今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve been feeling tired all day.","jp":"一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’ve been studying for two hours.","jp":"2時間ずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m thinking of having noodles.","jp":"麺を食べようかと考えています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"present perfect continuous","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect continuous meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。”.","hintJa":"続いている一時的な状態を強調します。","explanation":"“I’ve been feeling tired all day.” is the sentence that means “一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I’ve been feeling tired all day.」が「一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。","promptJa":"「一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve been feeling tired all day.","jp":"一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。"},{"id":"b","en":"How long have you had the headache?","jp":"どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I walk to work every day.","jp":"私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。"},{"id":"d","en":"I used to skip breakfast.","jp":"以前は朝食を抜いていました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"duration","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the duration meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？”.","hintJa":"How long + 現在完了で継続期間を尋ねます。","explanation":"“How long have you had the headache?” is the sentence that means “どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「How long have you had the headache?」が「どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？","promptJa":"「どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"How long have you had the headache?","jp":"どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.","jp":"7時からずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"c","en":"This is an everyday problem.","jp":"これは日常的な問題です。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m used to waking up early.","jp":"私は早起きに慣れています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"since","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the since meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “7時からずっと勉強しています。”.","hintJa":"since の後には開始時点を置きます。","explanation":"“I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.” is the sentence that means “7時からずっと勉強しています。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.」が「7時からずっと勉強しています。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 7時からずっと勉強しています。","promptJa":"「7時からずっと勉強しています。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.","jp":"7時からずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve been studying for two hours.","jp":"2時間ずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"c","en":"What are you having for lunch?","jp":"昼食は何を食べますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m getting used to the new schedule.","jp":"新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"for","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the for meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “2時間ずっと勉強しています。”.","hintJa":"for の後には期間を置きます。","explanation":"True. “I’ve been studying for two hours.” means “2時間ずっと勉強しています。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「I’ve been studying for two hours.」は「2時間ずっと勉強しています。」という意味です。","prompt":"“I’ve been studying for two hours.” means “2時間ずっと勉強しています。”.","promptJa":"「I’ve been studying for two hours.」は「2時間ずっと勉強しています。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"every day","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the every day meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。”.","hintJa":"every day は「毎日」という副詞句です。","explanation":"False. “I walk to work every day.” means “私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。”, not “これは日常的な問題です。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「I walk to work every day.」は「私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。」であり、「これは日常的な問題です。」ではありません。","prompt":"“I walk to work every day.” means “これは日常的な問題です。”.","promptJa":"「I walk to work every day.」は「これは日常的な問題です。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"everyday","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the everyday meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “これは日常的な問題です。”.","hintJa":"everyday は名詞の前で「日常の」を表す形容詞です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “This is an everyday problem.”. It expresses “これは日常的な問題です。” with the lesson’s everyday pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「This is an everyday problem.」です。「これは日常的な問題です。」を今回のeveryday表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: これは日常的な問題です。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：これは日常的な問題です。","accepted":["This is an everyday problem."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"lunch plans","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the lunch plans meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “昼食は何を食べますか？”.","hintJa":"決まっている近い予定には現在進行形も自然です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “What are you having for lunch?”. It expresses “昼食は何を食べますか？” with the lesson’s lunch plans pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「What are you having for lunch?」です。「昼食は何を食べますか？」を今回のlunch plans表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 昼食は何を食べますか？","promptJa":"英語にしてください：昼食は何を食べますか？","accepted":["What are you having for lunch?"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-typing', 8, 'Build It', 'typing', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-typing","format":"typing","type":"typing","section":"Build It","topic":"get used to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the get used to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。”.","hintJa":"変化の途中は get used to を使います。","explanation":"A complete model answer is “I’m getting used to the new schedule.”. Check the key get used to expression and every short grammar word.","explanationJa":"完全な答えは「I’m getting used to the new schedule.」です。get used toの中心表現と短い文法語まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete English sentence from memory: 新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。","promptJa":"日本語を見て、英文を最後まで入力してください：新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。","accepted":["I’m getting used to the new schedule."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-order-1', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"lunch plans","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the lunch plans meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “麺を食べようかと考えています。”.","hintJa":"think of + 動名詞で検討中の案を表します。","explanation":"Correct order: “I’m thinking of having noodles.”. Build the sentence around the lunch plans pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I’m thinking of having noodles.」です。lunch plansの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 麺を食べようかと考えています。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：麺を食べようかと考えています。","words":["thinking","noodles","of","I’m","having"],"correctWords":["I’m","thinking","of","having","noodles"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-order-2', 10, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"used to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the used to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “以前は朝食を抜いていました。”.","hintJa":"過去の習慣で、今は違うことを示します。","explanation":"Correct order: “I used to skip breakfast.”. Build the sentence around the used to pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「I used to skip breakfast.」です。used toの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 以前は朝食を抜いていました。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：以前は朝食を抜いていました。","words":["used","breakfast","to","I","skip"],"correctWords":["I","used","to","skip","breakfast"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-matching', 11, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"since","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the since meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。”.","hintJa":"状態を表す have a headache は現在完了が自然です。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"I’ve had a headache since this morning.","jp":"今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。","cat":"since"},{"en":"I’ve been feeling tired all day.","jp":"一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。","cat":"present perfect continuous"},{"en":"How long have you had the headache?","jp":"どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？","cat":"duration"},{"en":"I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.","jp":"7時からずっと勉強しています。","cat":"since"},{"en":"I’ve been studying for two hours.","jp":"2時間ずっと勉強しています。","cat":"for"},{"en":"I walk to work every day.","jp":"私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。","cat":"every day"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-sorting', 12, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"present perfect continuous","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect continuous meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。”.","hintJa":"続いている一時的な状態を強調します。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are since, present perfect continuous, duration.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「since・present perfect continuous・duration」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["since","present perfect continuous","duration"],"items":[["I’ve had a headache since this morning.","since"],["I’ve been feeling tired all day.","present perfect continuous"],["How long have you had the headache?","duration"],["I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.","since"]]}'::jsonb, false, 4),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-grid', 13, 'Build It', 'grid', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-grid","format":"grid","type":"grid","section":"Build It","topic":"for","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the for meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “2時間ずっと勉強しています。”.","hintJa":"for の後には期間を置きます。","explanation":"The center tile, “I’ve been studying for two hours.”, means “2時間ずっと勉強しています。”. Read every complete phrase before choosing its position.","explanationJa":"中央の「I’ve been studying for two hours.」が「2時間ずっと勉強しています。」を表します。位置だけでなく、各英文の意味を最後まで読んで選びましょう。","prompt":"Select the tile that means: 2時間ずっと勉強しています。","promptJa":"「2時間ずっと勉強しています。」を表す英文のタイルを選んでください。","correctCell":"center","gridCells":{"top-left":"I’ve had a headache since this morning.","top-center":"I’ve been feeling tired all day.","top-right":"How long have you had the headache?","middle-left":"I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.","center":"I’ve been studying for two hours.","middle-right":"I walk to work every day.","bottom-left":"This is an everyday problem.","bottom-center":"What are you having for lunch?","bottom-right":"I’m thinking of having noodles."}}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-listen-choice-1', 14, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-listen-choice-1","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"since","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the since meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。”.","hintJa":"状態を表す have a headache は現在完了が自然です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “I’ve had a headache since this morning.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「I’ve had a headache since this morning.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"I’ve had a headache since this morning.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve had a headache since this morning.","jp":"今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve been feeling tired all day.","jp":"一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’ve been studying for two hours.","jp":"2時間ずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m thinking of having noodles.","jp":"麺を食べようかと考えています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-listen-choice-2', 15, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-listen-choice-2","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"since","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the since meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “7時からずっと勉強しています。”.","hintJa":"since の後には開始時点を置きます。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.","jp":"7時からずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve been studying for two hours.","jp":"2時間ずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"c","en":"What are you having for lunch?","jp":"昼食は何を食べますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m getting used to the new schedule.","jp":"新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-listen-choice-3', 16, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-listen-choice-3","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"everyday","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the everyday meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “これは日常的な問題です。”.","hintJa":"everyday は名詞の前で「日常の」を表す形容詞です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “This is an everyday problem.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「This is an everyday problem.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"This is an everyday problem.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"This is an everyday problem.","jp":"これは日常的な問題です。"},{"id":"b","en":"What are you having for lunch?","jp":"昼食は何を食べますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m used to waking up early.","jp":"私は早起きに慣れています。"},{"id":"d","en":"How long have you had the headache?","jp":"どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-dictation-1', 17, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-dictation-1","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"present perfect continuous","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the present perfect continuous meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。”.","hintJa":"続いている一時的な状態を強調します。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “I’ve been feeling tired all day.”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「I’ve been feeling tired all day.」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"I’ve been feeling tired all day.","accepted":["I’ve been feeling tired all day."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-dictation-2', 18, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-dictation-2","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"for","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the for meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “2時間ずっと勉強しています。”.","hintJa":"for の後には期間を置きます。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “I’ve been studying for two hours.”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「I’ve been studying for two hours.」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"I’ve been studying for two hours.","accepted":["I’ve been studying for two hours."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-dictation-3', 19, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-dictation-3","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"lunch plans","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the lunch plans meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “昼食は何を食べますか？”.","hintJa":"決まっている近い予定には現在進行形も自然です。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “What are you having for lunch?”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「What are you having for lunch?」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"What are you having for lunch?","accepted":["What are you having for lunch?"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-speaking-1', 20, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-speaking-1","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"duration","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the duration meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？”.","hintJa":"How long + 現在完了で継続期間を尋ねます。","explanation":"Model: “How long have you had the headache?” (どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「How long have you had the headache?」（どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"How long have you had the headache?","speakJa":"どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-speaking-2', 21, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-speaking-2","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"every day","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the every day meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。”.","hintJa":"every day は「毎日」という副詞句です。","explanation":"Model: “I walk to work every day.” (私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I walk to work every day.」（私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"I walk to work every day.","speakJa":"私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-speaking-3', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"lunch plans","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the lunch plans meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “麺を食べようかと考えています。”.","hintJa":"think of + 動名詞で検討中の案を表します。","explanation":"Model: “I’m thinking of having noodles.” (麺を食べようかと考えています。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I’m thinking of having noodles.」（麺を食べようかと考えています。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"I’m thinking of having noodles.","speakJa":"麺を食べようかと考えています。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-speaking-4', 23, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"used to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the used to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “以前は朝食を抜いていました。”.","hintJa":"過去の習慣で、今は違うことを示します。","explanation":"Model: “I used to skip breakfast.” (以前は朝食を抜いていました。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I used to skip breakfast.」（以前は朝食を抜いていました。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I used to skip breakfast.","speakJa":"以前は朝食を抜いていました。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"be used to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the be used to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は早起きに慣れています。”.","hintJa":"be used to + 名詞・動名詞は「慣れている」です。","explanation":"Model: “I’m used to waking up early.” (私は早起きに慣れています。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I’m used to waking up early.」（私は早起きに慣れています。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"I’m used to waking up early.","speakJa":"私は早起きに慣れています。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"used to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the used to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “以前は朝食を抜いていました。”.","hintJa":"過去の習慣で、今は違うことを示します。","explanation":"“I used to skip breakfast.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「I used to skip breakfast.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: I’m thinking of having noodles.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: 麺を食べようかと考えています。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I used to skip breakfast.","jp":"以前は朝食を抜いていました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m used to waking up early.","jp":"私は早起きに慣れています。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’ve been feeling tired all day.","jp":"一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。"},{"id":"d","en":"I walk to work every day.","jp":"私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"be used to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the be used to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私は早起きに慣れています。”.","hintJa":"be used to + 名詞・動名詞は「慣れている」です。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “I’m used to waking up early.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「I’m used to waking up early.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"I used to waking up early.","accepted":["I’m used to waking up early."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"get used to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the get used to meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。”.","hintJa":"変化の途中は get used to を使います。","explanation":"“I’m getting used to the new schedule.” directly expresses “新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「I’m getting used to the new schedule.」が「新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。","promptJa":"「新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m getting used to the new schedule.","jp":"新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve had a headache since this morning.","jp":"今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.","jp":"7時からずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"d","en":"What are you having for lunch?","jp":"昼食は何を食べますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"since","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The discomfort begins in the morning and continues to the present.","hintJa":"不調が朝に始まり、今まで続いていることを見ましょう。","explanation":"“I’ve had a headache since this morning.” is correct. The repeated person across the timeline shows a headache continuing since morning. “I’ve been feeling tired all day.” does not fit because that sentence means “一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I walk to work every day.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I used to skip breakfast.” does not fit because that sentence means “以前は朝食を抜いていました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I’ve had a headache since this morning.」（今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。）です。時間の流れの中で同じ人が頭を押さえ続け、朝からの継続を示しています。 「I’ve been feeling tired all day.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I walk to work every day.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I used to skip breakfast.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「以前は朝食を抜いていました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve had a headache since this morning.","jp":"今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve been feeling tired all day.","jp":"一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。"},{"id":"c","en":"I walk to work every day.","jp":"私は毎日歩いて仕事へ行きます。"},{"id":"d","en":"I used to skip breakfast.","jp":"以前は朝食を抜いていました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-17-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A person has had a headache since morning.","visualAssetId":"august-17-part-1-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"duration","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The question is about duration, not the pain’s location.","hintJa":"痛む場所ではなく、続いている時間を尋ねています。","explanation":"“How long have you had the headache?” is correct. The doctor’s timeline gesture asks how long the headache has continued. “I’ve had a headache since this morning.” does not fit because that sentence means “今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “This is an everyday problem.” does not fit because that sentence means “これは日常的な問題です。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m getting used to the new schedule.” does not fit because that sentence means “新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「How long have you had the headache?」（どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？）です。医師が時間の線を示し、頭痛の継続期間を尋ねています。 「I’ve had a headache since this morning.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「This is an everyday problem.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「これは日常的な問題です。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m getting used to the new schedule.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"How long have you had the headache?","jp":"どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve had a headache since this morning.","jp":"今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。"},{"id":"c","en":"This is an everyday problem.","jp":"これは日常的な問題です。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m getting used to the new schedule.","jp":"新しい予定にだんだん慣れてきました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-17-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A doctor asks how long a headache has lasted.","visualAssetId":"august-17-part-1-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"for","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The duration is a two-hour period, not a starting clock time.","hintJa":"開始時刻ではなく、2時間という期間に注目しましょう。","explanation":"“I’ve been studying for two hours.” is correct. The advancing clock and continuous study show a two-hour duration. “How long have you had the headache?” does not fit because that sentence means “どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “What are you having for lunch?” does not fit because that sentence means “昼食は何を食べますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m used to waking up early.” does not fit because that sentence means “私は早起きに慣れています。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I’ve been studying for two hours.」（2時間ずっと勉強しています。）です。進む時計と続く勉強が、2時間の継続を示しています。 「How long have you had the headache?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「What are you having for lunch?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「昼食は何を食べますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m used to waking up early.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私は早起きに慣れています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’ve been studying for two hours.","jp":"2時間ずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"b","en":"How long have you had the headache?","jp":"どのくらい頭痛が続いていますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"What are you having for lunch?","jp":"昼食は何を食べますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m used to waking up early.","jp":"私は早起きに慣れています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-17-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"A learner has been studying for two hours.","visualAssetId":"august-17-part-1-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"lunch plans","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The conversation is about today’s planned lunch choice.","hintJa":"今日の昼食に何を食べる予定かを尋ねる会話です。","explanation":"“What are you having for lunch?” is correct. Meal options and the questioning gesture show a lunch-plan question. “I’ve been feeling tired all day.” does not fit because that sentence means “一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’ve been studying for two hours.” does not fit because that sentence means “2時間ずっと勉強しています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I used to skip breakfast.” does not fit because that sentence means “以前は朝食を抜いていました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「What are you having for lunch?」（昼食は何を食べますか？）です。食事の選択肢と質問の仕草が、昼食予定を尋ねています。 「I’ve been feeling tired all day.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’ve been studying for two hours.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「2時間ずっと勉強しています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I used to skip breakfast.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「以前は朝食を抜いていました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"What are you having for lunch?","jp":"昼食は何を食べますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve been feeling tired all day.","jp":"一日中ずっと疲れを感じています。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’ve been studying for two hours.","jp":"2時間ずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"d","en":"I used to skip breakfast.","jp":"以前は朝食を抜いていました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-17-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"Friends discuss what to have for lunch.","visualAssetId":"august-17-part-1-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-1', 'august-17-part-1-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-1-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"be used to","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Early waking is now familiar and comfortable, not a former habit that ended.","hintJa":"早起きは今では慣れたことで、終わった昔の習慣ではありません。","explanation":"“I’m used to waking up early.” is correct. The relaxed dawn routine shows the person is accustomed to waking early. “I’ve had a headache since this morning.” does not fit because that sentence means “今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.” does not fit because that sentence means “7時からずっと勉強しています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m thinking of having noodles.” does not fit because that sentence means “麺を食べようかと考えています。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I’m used to waking up early.」（私は早起きに慣れています。）です。落ち着いた早朝の習慣が、早起きに慣れていることを示しています。 「I’ve had a headache since this morning.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「7時からずっと勉強しています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m thinking of having noodles.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「麺を食べようかと考えています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m used to waking up early.","jp":"私は早起きに慣れています。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’ve had a headache since this morning.","jp":"今朝からずっと頭が痛いです。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’ve been studying since seven o’clock.","jp":"7時からずっと勉強しています。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m thinking of having noodles.","jp":"麺を食べようかと考えています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-17-part-1-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A person is comfortable waking up early.","visualAssetId":"august-17-part-1-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"clothing","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the clothing meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。”.","hintJa":"sleeveless は袖のない服を表します。","explanation":"“She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.” is the sentence that means “彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.」が「彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。","promptJa":"「彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.","jp":"彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。"},{"id":"b","en":"Whose bag is this?","jp":"これは誰の鞄ですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"The entire room was silent.","jp":"部屋全体が静かでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"The performance bombed.","jp":"その公演は大失敗でした。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"whose","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the whose meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “これは誰の鞄ですか？”.","hintJa":"whose は持ち主を尋ねる疑問詞です。","explanation":"“Whose bag is this?” is the sentence that means “これは誰の鞄ですか？”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Whose bag is this?」が「これは誰の鞄ですか？」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: これは誰の鞄ですか？","promptJa":"「これは誰の鞄ですか？」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Whose bag is this?","jp":"これは誰の鞄ですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Whose is this?","jp":"これは誰のものですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I entirely agree with you.","jp":"私はあなたに全面的に同意します。"},{"id":"d","en":"He’s starting to go bald.","jp":"彼ははげ始めています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"whose","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the whose meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “これは誰のものですか？”.","hintJa":"名詞が明らかな時は whose だけでも使えます。","explanation":"“Whose is this?” is the sentence that means “これは誰のものですか？”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Whose is this?」が「これは誰のものですか？」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: これは誰のものですか？","promptJa":"「これは誰のものですか？」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Whose is this?","jp":"これは誰のものですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"The book was written in English.","jp":"その本は英語で書かれました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I read the report in its entirety.","jp":"私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。"},{"id":"d","en":"It may rain later.","jp":"あとで雨が降るかもしれません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"passive voice","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the passive voice meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その本は英語で書かれました。”.","hintJa":"was written は write の受動態です。","explanation":"“The book was written in English.” is the sentence that means “その本は英語で書かれました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「The book was written in English.」が「その本は英語で書かれました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: その本は英語で書かれました。","promptJa":"「その本は英語で書かれました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The book was written in English.","jp":"その本は英語で書かれました。"},{"id":"b","en":"The entire room was silent.","jp":"部屋全体が静かでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"My joke fell flat.","jp":"私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"That word can sound too strong.","jp":"その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"entire","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the entire meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “部屋全体が静かでした。”.","hintJa":"entire は名詞を修飾する形容詞です。","explanation":"True. “The entire room was silent.” means “部屋全体が静かでした。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「The entire room was silent.」は「部屋全体が静かでした。」という意味です。","prompt":"“The entire room was silent.” means “部屋全体が静かでした。”.","promptJa":"「The entire room was silent.」は「部屋全体が静かでした。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"entirely","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the entirely meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はあなたに全面的に同意します。”.","hintJa":"entirely は動詞や形容詞を修飾する副詞です。","explanation":"False. “I entirely agree with you.” means “私はあなたに全面的に同意します。”, not “私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「I entirely agree with you.」は「私はあなたに全面的に同意します。」であり、「私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。」ではありません。","prompt":"“I entirely agree with you.” means “私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。”.","promptJa":"「I entirely agree with you.」は「私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"entirety","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the entirety meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。”.","hintJa":"in its entirety は「全体を残さず」です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “I read the report in its entirety.”. It expresses “私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。” with the lesson’s entirety pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「I read the report in its entirety.」です。「私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。」を今回のentirety表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。","accepted":["I read the report in its entirety."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"fall flat","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the fall flat meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。”.","hintJa":"期待した反応が得られない時の自然な表現です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “My joke fell flat.”. It expresses “私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。” with the lesson’s fall flat pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「My joke fell flat.」です。「私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。」を今回のfall flat表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。","accepted":["My joke fell flat."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-typing', 8, 'Build It', 'typing', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-typing","format":"typing","type":"typing","section":"Build It","topic":"word choice","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the word choice meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。”.","hintJa":"意味だけでなく、相手への響きも考えて語を選びます。","explanation":"A complete model answer is “That word can sound too strong.”. Check the key word choice expression and every short grammar word.","explanationJa":"完全な答えは「That word can sound too strong.」です。word choiceの中心表現と短い文法語まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete English sentence from memory: その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。","promptJa":"日本語を見て、英文を最後まで入力してください：その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。","accepted":["That word can sound too strong."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-order-1', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"bomb","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the bomb meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その公演は大失敗でした。”.","hintJa":"informal な強い表現なので使う場面に注意します。","explanation":"Correct order: “The performance bombed.”. Build the sentence around the bomb pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「The performance bombed.」です。bombの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: その公演は大失敗でした。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：その公演は大失敗でした。","words":["The","performance","bombed"],"correctWords":["The","performance","bombed"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-order-2', 10, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"go bald","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the go bald meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼ははげ始めています。”.","hintJa":"状態の変化は go + 形容詞で表せます。","explanation":"Correct order: “He’s starting to go bald.”. Build the sentence around the go bald pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「He’s starting to go bald.」です。go baldの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 彼ははげ始めています。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：彼ははげ始めています。","words":["starting","bald","to","He’s","go"],"correctWords":["He’s","starting","to","go","bald"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-matching', 11, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"clothing","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the clothing meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。”.","hintJa":"sleeveless は袖のない服を表します。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.","jp":"彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。","cat":"clothing"},{"en":"Whose bag is this?","jp":"これは誰の鞄ですか？","cat":"whose"},{"en":"Whose is this?","jp":"これは誰のものですか？","cat":"whose"},{"en":"The book was written in English.","jp":"その本は英語で書かれました。","cat":"passive voice"},{"en":"The entire room was silent.","jp":"部屋全体が静かでした。","cat":"entire"},{"en":"I entirely agree with you.","jp":"私はあなたに全面的に同意します。","cat":"entirely"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-sorting', 12, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"whose","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the whose meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “これは誰の鞄ですか？”.","hintJa":"whose は持ち主を尋ねる疑問詞です。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are clothing, whose, passive voice.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「clothing・whose・passive voice」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["clothing","whose","passive voice"],"items":[["She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.","clothing"],["Whose bag is this?","whose"],["Whose is this?","whose"],["The book was written in English.","passive voice"]]}'::jsonb, false, 4),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-grid', 13, 'Build It', 'grid', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-grid","format":"grid","type":"grid","section":"Build It","topic":"entire","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the entire meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “部屋全体が静かでした。”.","hintJa":"entire は名詞を修飾する形容詞です。","explanation":"The center tile, “The entire room was silent.”, means “部屋全体が静かでした。”. Read every complete phrase before choosing its position.","explanationJa":"中央の「The entire room was silent.」が「部屋全体が静かでした。」を表します。位置だけでなく、各英文の意味を最後まで読んで選びましょう。","prompt":"Select the tile that means: 部屋全体が静かでした。","promptJa":"「部屋全体が静かでした。」を表す英文のタイルを選んでください。","correctCell":"center","gridCells":{"top-left":"She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.","top-center":"Whose bag is this?","top-right":"Whose is this?","middle-left":"The book was written in English.","center":"The entire room was silent.","middle-right":"I entirely agree with you.","bottom-left":"I read the report in its entirety.","bottom-center":"My joke fell flat.","bottom-right":"The performance bombed."}}'::jsonb, false, 1),
