  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-speaking-3', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"bomb","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the bomb meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その公演は大失敗でした。”.","hintJa":"informal な強い表現なので使う場面に注意します。","explanation":"Model: “The performance bombed.” (その公演は大失敗でした。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「The performance bombed.」（その公演は大失敗でした。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"The performance bombed.","speakJa":"その公演は大失敗でした。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-speaking-4', 23, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"go bald","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the go bald meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼ははげ始めています。”.","hintJa":"状態の変化は go + 形容詞で表せます。","explanation":"Model: “He’s starting to go bald.” (彼ははげ始めています。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「He’s starting to go bald.」（彼ははげ始めています。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"He’s starting to go bald.","speakJa":"彼ははげ始めています。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"may","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the may meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “あとで雨が降るかもしれません。”.","hintJa":"may の後は動詞の原形です。","explanation":"Model: “It may rain later.” (あとで雨が降るかもしれません。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「It may rain later.」（あとで雨が降るかもしれません。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"It may rain later.","speakJa":"あとで雨が降るかもしれません。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"go bald","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the go bald meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼ははげ始めています。”.","hintJa":"状態の変化は go + 形容詞で表せます。","explanation":"“He’s starting to go bald.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「He’s starting to go bald.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: The performance bombed.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: その公演は大失敗でした。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He’s starting to go bald.","jp":"彼ははげ始めています。"},{"id":"b","en":"It may rain later.","jp":"あとで雨が降るかもしれません。"},{"id":"c","en":"Whose bag is this?","jp":"これは誰の鞄ですか？"},{"id":"d","en":"I entirely agree with you.","jp":"私はあなたに全面的に同意します。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"may","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the may meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “あとで雨が降るかもしれません。”.","hintJa":"may の後は動詞の原形です。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “It may rain later.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「It may rain later.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"It may rain later yesterday now.","accepted":["It may rain later."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"word choice","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the word choice meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。”.","hintJa":"意味だけでなく、相手への響きも考えて語を選びます。","explanation":"“That word can sound too strong.” directly expresses “その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「That word can sound too strong.」が「その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。","promptJa":"「その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"That word can sound too strong.","jp":"その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。"},{"id":"b","en":"She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.","jp":"彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。"},{"id":"c","en":"The book was written in English.","jp":"その本は英語で書かれました。"},{"id":"d","en":"My joke fell flat.","jp":"私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"clothing","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the garment’s missing sleeves.","hintJa":"服に袖がないことに注目しましょう。","explanation":"“She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.” is correct. The shirt leaves both shoulders and arms uncovered because it has no sleeves. “Whose bag is this?” does not fit because that sentence means “これは誰の鞄ですか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I entirely agree with you.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はあなたに全面的に同意します。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “He’s starting to go bald.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼ははげ始めています。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.」（彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。）です。シャツに袖がなく、肩と腕が出ています。 「Whose bag is this?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「これは誰の鞄ですか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I entirely agree with you.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はあなたに全面的に同意します。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「He’s starting to go bald.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼ははげ始めています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.","jp":"彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。"},{"id":"b","en":"Whose bag is this?","jp":"これは誰の鞄ですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"I entirely agree with you.","jp":"私はあなたに全面的に同意します。"},{"id":"d","en":"He’s starting to go bald.","jp":"彼ははげ始めています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-17-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A woman wears a sleeveless shirt.","visualAssetId":"august-17-part-2-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"whose","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The object is visible, so the speaker asks only about its owner.","hintJa":"物は見えているので、その持ち主だけを尋ねています。","explanation":"“Whose is this?” is correct. The person displays the unclaimed item and asks the group who it belongs to. “She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I read the report in its entirety.” does not fit because that sentence means “私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “That word can sound too strong.” does not fit because that sentence means “その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Whose is this?」（これは誰のものですか？）です。持ち主不明の物を掲げ、誰のものか皆に尋ねています。 「She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I read the report in its entirety.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「That word can sound too strong.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Whose is this?","jp":"これは誰のものですか？"},{"id":"b","en":"She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.","jp":"彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。"},{"id":"c","en":"I read the report in its entirety.","jp":"私はレポートを最初から最後まで読みました。"},{"id":"d","en":"That word can sound too strong.","jp":"その言葉は強すぎる印象になることがあります。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-17-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"Someone asks who owns an unidentified item.","visualAssetId":"august-17-part-2-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"entire","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The silence covers the whole room and everyone in it.","hintJa":"静けさが部屋全体と全員に広がっていることを見ましょう。","explanation":"“The entire room was silent.” is correct. No one anywhere in the room is speaking, so the whole room is silent. “Whose is this?” does not fit because that sentence means “これは誰のものですか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “My joke fell flat.” does not fit because that sentence means “私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “It may rain later.” does not fit because that sentence means “あとで雨が降るかもしれません。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「The entire room was silent.」（部屋全体が静かでした。）です。部屋のどこでも誰も話しておらず、空間全体が静かです。 「Whose is this?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「これは誰のものですか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「My joke fell flat.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「It may rain later.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「あとで雨が降るかもしれません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The entire room was silent.","jp":"部屋全体が静かでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"Whose is this?","jp":"これは誰のものですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"My joke fell flat.","jp":"私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"It may rain later.","jp":"あとで雨が降るかもしれません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-17-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"An entire room becomes silent.","visualAssetId":"august-17-part-2-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"fall flat","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The attempted joke gets no laugh or positive response.","hintJa":"冗談を言ったのに、笑いや良い反応が全くないことを見ましょう。","explanation":"“My joke fell flat.” is correct. The silent audience and awkward speaker show that the joke failed to land. “Whose bag is this?” does not fit because that sentence means “これは誰の鞄ですか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “The entire room was silent.” does not fit because that sentence means “部屋全体が静かでした。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “He’s starting to go bald.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼ははげ始めています。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「My joke fell flat.」（私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。）です。無反応の観客と気まずい話し手が、冗談が受けなかったことを示しています。 「Whose bag is this?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「これは誰の鞄ですか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「The entire room was silent.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「部屋全体が静かでした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「He’s starting to go bald.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼ははげ始めています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"My joke fell flat.","jp":"私の冗談は全く受けませんでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"Whose bag is this?","jp":"これは誰の鞄ですか？"},{"id":"c","en":"The entire room was silent.","jp":"部屋全体が静かでした。"},{"id":"d","en":"He’s starting to go bald.","jp":"彼ははげ始めています。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-17-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"A joke receives no reaction from an audience.","visualAssetId":"august-17-part-2-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-17-part-2', 'august-17-part-2-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-17-part-2-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"may","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Rain is only a future possibility; it has not started yet.","hintJa":"雨はまだ始まっておらず、これからの可能性だけが示されています。","explanation":"“It may rain later.” is correct. Dry ground and approaching clouds show possible rain later. “She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “The book was written in English.” does not fit because that sentence means “その本は英語で書かれました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “The performance bombed.” does not fit because that sentence means “その公演は大失敗でした。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「It may rain later.」（あとで雨が降るかもしれません。）です。乾いた地面と近づく雲が、後で雨になる可能性を示しています。 「She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「The book was written in English.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「その本は英語で書かれました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「The performance bombed.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「その公演は大失敗でした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"It may rain later.","jp":"あとで雨が降るかもしれません。"},{"id":"b","en":"She’s wearing a sleeveless shirt.","jp":"彼女はノースリーブのシャツを着ています。"},{"id":"c","en":"The book was written in English.","jp":"その本は英語で書かれました。"},{"id":"d","en":"The performance bombed.","jp":"その公演は大失敗でした。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-17-part-2-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"Dark clouds suggest that it may rain later.","visualAssetId":"august-17-part-2-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-23-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"work greeting","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the work greeting meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今日はお疲れさまでした。”.","hintJa":"一日の仕事をねぎらう自然な英語です。","explanation":"“Thanks for your hard work today.” is the sentence that means “今日はお疲れさまでした。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Thanks for your hard work today.」が「今日はお疲れさまでした。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 今日はお疲れさまでした。","promptJa":"「今日はお疲れさまでした。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Thanks for your hard work today.","jp":"今日はお疲れさまでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"Thanks for taking care of that.","jp":"対応してくれてありがとうございます。"},{"id":"c","en":"What time will the event start?","jp":"そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"That message looks suspicious.","jp":"そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-23-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"work greeting","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the work greeting meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “対応してくれてありがとうございます。”.","hintJa":"具体的な仕事への感謝を伝えます。","explanation":"“Thanks for taking care of that.” is the sentence that means “対応してくれてありがとうございます。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Thanks for taking care of that.」が「対応してくれてありがとうございます。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 対応してくれてありがとうございます。","promptJa":"「対応してくれてありがとうございます。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Thanks for taking care of that.","jp":"対応してくれてありがとうございます。"},{"id":"b","en":"Have a good evening.","jp":"よい夜をお過ごしください。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m confused by these instructions.","jp":"この説明が分からなくて混乱しています。"},{"id":"d","en":"Something feels off.","jp":"何か違和感があります。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-23-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"leaving work","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the leaving work meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “よい夜をお過ごしください。”.","hintJa":"退勤時の自然で簡潔な挨拶です。","explanation":"“Have a good evening.” is the sentence that means “よい夜をお過ごしください。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Have a good evening.」が「よい夜をお過ごしください。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: よい夜をお過ごしください。","promptJa":"「よい夜をお過ごしください。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Have a good evening.","jp":"よい夜をお過ごしください。"},{"id":"b","en":"What time does the store open?","jp":"その店は何時に開店しますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"These instructions are confusing.","jp":"この説明は分かりにくいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"This deal sounds fishy.","jp":"この取引は何か怪しいです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-23-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"schedules","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the schedules meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その店は何時に開店しますか？”.","hintJa":"決まった営業時間には現在形 does ... open を使います。","explanation":"“What time does the store open?” is the sentence that means “その店は何時に開店しますか？”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「What time does the store open?」が「その店は何時に開店しますか？」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: その店は何時に開店しますか？","promptJa":"「その店は何時に開店しますか？」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"What time does the store open?","jp":"その店は何時に開店しますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"What time will the event start?","jp":"そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"There seems to be some confusion.","jp":"少し行き違いがあるようです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much.","jp":"お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-23-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"future event","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the future event meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？”.","hintJa":"未来の一回の出来事には will も使えます。","explanation":"True. “What time will the event start?” means “そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「What time will the event start?」は「そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？」という意味です。","prompt":"“What time will the event start?” means “そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？”.","promptJa":"「What time will the event start?」は「そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-23-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"confused","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the confused meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この説明が分からなくて混乱しています。”.","hintJa":"人の気持ちは confused です。","explanation":"False. “I’m confused by these instructions.” means “この説明が分からなくて混乱しています。”, not “この説明は分かりにくいです。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「I’m confused by these instructions.」は「この説明が分からなくて混乱しています。」であり、「この説明は分かりにくいです。」ではありません。","prompt":"“I’m confused by these instructions.” means “この説明は分かりにくいです。”.","promptJa":"「I’m confused by these instructions.」は「この説明は分かりにくいです。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-23-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"confusing","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the confusing meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この説明は分かりにくいです。”.","hintJa":"混乱させる原因は confusing です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “These instructions are confusing.”. It expresses “この説明は分かりにくいです。” with the lesson’s confusing pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「These instructions are confusing.」です。「この説明は分かりにくいです。」を今回のconfusing表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: この説明は分かりにくいです。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：この説明は分かりにくいです。","accepted":["These instructions are confusing."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-23-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"confusion","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the confusion meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “少し行き違いがあるようです。”.","hintJa":"confusion は名詞で、仕事の場でも柔らかく使えます。","explanation":"A natural translation is “There seems to be some confusion.”. It expresses “少し行き違いがあるようです。” with the lesson’s confusion pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「There seems to be some confusion.」です。「少し行き違いがあるようです。」を今回のconfusion表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 少し行き違いがあるようです。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：少し行き違いがあるようです。","accepted":["There seems to be some confusion."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-typing', 8, 'Build It', 'typing', '{"id":"august-23-draft-typing","format":"typing","type":"typing","section":"Build It","topic":"alcohol","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the alcohol meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。”.","hintJa":"lightweight はカジュアル。丁寧には I can’t handle much alcohol も使えます。","explanation":"A complete model answer is “I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much.”. Check the key alcohol expression and every short grammar word.","explanationJa":"完全な答えは「I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much.」です。alcoholの中心表現と短い文法語まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete English sentence from memory: お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。","promptJa":"日本語を見て、英文を最後まで入力してください：お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。","accepted":["I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-order-1', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-23-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"suspicious","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the suspicious meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。”.","hintJa":"人・物・状況を怪しいと判断する表現です。","explanation":"Correct order: “That message looks suspicious.”. Build the sentence around the suspicious pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「That message looks suspicious.」です。suspiciousの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。","words":["suspicious","looks","message","That"],"correctWords":["That","message","looks","suspicious"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-order-2', 10, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-23-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"feels off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the feels off meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “何か違和感があります。”.","hintJa":"断定を避けて違和感を伝える自然な表現です。","explanation":"Correct order: “Something feels off.”. Build the sentence around the feels off pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「Something feels off.」です。feels offの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 何か違和感があります。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：何か違和感があります。","words":["Something","feels","off"],"correctWords":["Something","feels","off"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-matching', 11, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"august-23-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"work greeting","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the work greeting meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今日はお疲れさまでした。”.","hintJa":"一日の仕事をねぎらう自然な英語です。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"Thanks for your hard work today.","jp":"今日はお疲れさまでした。","cat":"work greeting"},{"en":"Thanks for taking care of that.","jp":"対応してくれてありがとうございます。","cat":"work greeting"},{"en":"Have a good evening.","jp":"よい夜をお過ごしください。","cat":"leaving work"},{"en":"What time does the store open?","jp":"その店は何時に開店しますか？","cat":"schedules"},{"en":"What time will the event start?","jp":"そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？","cat":"future event"},{"en":"I’m confused by these instructions.","jp":"この説明が分からなくて混乱しています。","cat":"confused"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-sorting', 12, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"august-23-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"work greeting","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the work greeting meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “対応してくれてありがとうございます。”.","hintJa":"具体的な仕事への感謝を伝えます。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are work greeting, leaving work, schedules.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「work greeting・leaving work・schedules」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["work greeting","leaving work","schedules"],"items":[["Thanks for your hard work today.","work greeting"],["Thanks for taking care of that.","work greeting"],["Have a good evening.","leaving work"],["What time does the store open?","schedules"]]}'::jsonb, false, 4),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-grid', 13, 'Build It', 'grid', '{"id":"august-23-draft-grid","format":"grid","type":"grid","section":"Build It","topic":"future event","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the future event meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？”.","hintJa":"未来の一回の出来事には will も使えます。","explanation":"The center tile, “What time will the event start?”, means “そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？”. Read every complete phrase before choosing its position.","explanationJa":"中央の「What time will the event start?」が「そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？」を表します。位置だけでなく、各英文の意味を最後まで読んで選びましょう。","prompt":"Select the tile that means: そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？","promptJa":"「そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？」を表す英文のタイルを選んでください。","correctCell":"center","gridCells":{"top-left":"Thanks for your hard work today.","top-center":"Thanks for taking care of that.","top-right":"Have a good evening.","middle-left":"What time does the store open?","center":"What time will the event start?","middle-right":"I’m confused by these instructions.","bottom-left":"These instructions are confusing.","bottom-center":"There seems to be some confusion.","bottom-right":"That message looks suspicious."}}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-listen-choice-1', 14, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-23-draft-listen-choice-1","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"work greeting","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the work greeting meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今日はお疲れさまでした。”.","hintJa":"一日の仕事をねぎらう自然な英語です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “Thanks for your hard work today.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「Thanks for your hard work today.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"Thanks for your hard work today.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Thanks for your hard work today.","jp":"今日はお疲れさまでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"Thanks for taking care of that.","jp":"対応してくれてありがとうございます。"},{"id":"c","en":"What time will the event start?","jp":"そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"That message looks suspicious.","jp":"そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-listen-choice-2', 15, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-23-draft-listen-choice-2","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"schedules","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the schedules meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “その店は何時に開店しますか？”.","hintJa":"決まった営業時間には現在形 does ... open を使います。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “What time does the store open?”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「What time does the store open?」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"What time does the store open?","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"What time does the store open?","jp":"その店は何時に開店しますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"What time will the event start?","jp":"そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"There seems to be some confusion.","jp":"少し行き違いがあるようです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much.","jp":"お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-listen-choice-3', 16, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-23-draft-listen-choice-3","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"confusing","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the confusing meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この説明は分かりにくいです。”.","hintJa":"混乱させる原因は confusing です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “These instructions are confusing.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「These instructions are confusing.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"These instructions are confusing.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"These instructions are confusing.","jp":"この説明は分かりにくいです。"},{"id":"b","en":"There seems to be some confusion.","jp":"少し行き違いがあるようです。"},{"id":"c","en":"This deal sounds fishy.","jp":"この取引は何か怪しいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"Have a good evening.","jp":"よい夜をお過ごしください。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-dictation-1', 17, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-23-draft-dictation-1","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"work greeting","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the work greeting meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “対応してくれてありがとうございます。”.","hintJa":"具体的な仕事への感謝を伝えます。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “Thanks for taking care of that.”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「Thanks for taking care of that.」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"Thanks for taking care of that.","accepted":["Thanks for taking care of that."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
