  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-speaking-3', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-23-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"suspicious","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the suspicious meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。”.","hintJa":"人・物・状況を怪しいと判断する表現です。","explanation":"Model: “That message looks suspicious.” (そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「That message looks suspicious.」（そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"That message looks suspicious.","speakJa":"そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-speaking-4', 23, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-23-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"feels off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the feels off meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “何か違和感があります。”.","hintJa":"断定を避けて違和感を伝える自然な表現です。","explanation":"Model: “Something feels off.” (何か違和感があります。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Something feels off.」（何か違和感があります。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Something feels off.","speakJa":"何か違和感があります。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-23-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"fishy","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the fishy meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この取引は何か怪しいです。”.","hintJa":"fishy はカジュアルな「うさんくさい」です。","explanation":"Model: “This deal sounds fishy.” (この取引は何か怪しいです。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「This deal sounds fishy.」（この取引は何か怪しいです。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"This deal sounds fishy.","speakJa":"この取引は何か怪しいです。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-23-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"feels off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the feels off meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “何か違和感があります。”.","hintJa":"断定を避けて違和感を伝える自然な表現です。","explanation":"“Something feels off.” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「Something feels off.」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: That message looks suspicious.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Something feels off.","jp":"何か違和感があります。"},{"id":"b","en":"This deal sounds fishy.","jp":"この取引は何か怪しいです。"},{"id":"c","en":"Thanks for taking care of that.","jp":"対応してくれてありがとうございます。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m confused by these instructions.","jp":"この説明が分からなくて混乱しています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-23-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"fishy","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the fishy meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “この取引は何か怪しいです。”.","hintJa":"fishy はカジュアルな「うさんくさい」です。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “This deal sounds fishy.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「This deal sounds fishy.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"This deal sounds fishy yesterday now.","accepted":["This deal sounds fishy."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-23-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"alcohol","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the alcohol meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。”.","hintJa":"lightweight はカジュアル。丁寧には I can’t handle much alcohol も使えます。","explanation":"“I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much.” directly expresses “お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much.」が「お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。","promptJa":"「お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much.","jp":"お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。"},{"id":"b","en":"Thanks for your hard work today.","jp":"今日はお疲れさまでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"What time does the store open?","jp":"その店は何時に開店しますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"There seems to be some confusion.","jp":"少し行き違いがあるようです。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-23-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"work greeting","isOriginal":false,"hint":"This is broad appreciation at the end of today’s work.","hintJa":"今日一日の仕事を終えた時の、全体的なねぎらいに注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Thanks for your hard work today.” is correct. The completed work and end-of-day farewell show appreciation for today’s effort. “Thanks for taking care of that.” does not fit because that sentence means “対応してくれてありがとうございます。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m confused by these instructions.” does not fit because that sentence means “この説明が分からなくて混乱しています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Something feels off.” does not fit because that sentence means “何か違和感があります。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Thanks for your hard work today.」（今日はお疲れさまでした。）です。完了した仕事と退勤前の挨拶が、今日の努力へのねぎらいを示しています。 「Thanks for taking care of that.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「対応してくれてありがとうございます。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m confused by these instructions.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「この説明が分からなくて混乱しています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Something feels off.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「何か違和感があります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Thanks for your hard work today.","jp":"今日はお疲れさまでした。"},{"id":"b","en":"Thanks for taking care of that.","jp":"対応してくれてありがとうございます。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m confused by these instructions.","jp":"この説明が分からなくて混乱しています。"},{"id":"d","en":"Something feels off.","jp":"何か違和感があります。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-23-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"Coworkers thank each other after a full day of work.","visualAssetId":"august-23-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-23-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"leaving work","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The farewell happens in the evening after work.","hintJa":"仕事の後、夕方に交わす別れの挨拶を見ましょう。","explanation":"“Have a good evening.” is correct. Sunset and the friendly goodbye indicate a wish for a good evening. “Thanks for your hard work today.” does not fit because that sentence means “今日はお疲れさまでした。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “These instructions are confusing.” does not fit because that sentence means “この説明は分かりにくいです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much.” does not fit because that sentence means “お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Have a good evening.」（よい夜をお過ごしください。）です。夕日と親しい別れの仕草が、よい夜を願う挨拶を示しています。 「Thanks for your hard work today.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今日はお疲れさまでした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「These instructions are confusing.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「この説明は分かりにくいです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Have a good evening.","jp":"よい夜をお過ごしください。"},{"id":"b","en":"Thanks for your hard work today.","jp":"今日はお疲れさまでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"These instructions are confusing.","jp":"この説明は分かりにくいです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m a lightweight, so I don’t drink much.","jp":"お酒に弱いので、あまり飲みません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-23-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A coworker wishes another person a good evening when leaving.","visualAssetId":"august-23-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-23-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"future event","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The question concerns the start time of one future event.","hintJa":"未来に一度行われるイベントの開始時刻を尋ねています。","explanation":"“What time will the event start?” is correct. The upcoming event and clock gesture ask when it will begin. “Have a good evening.” does not fit because that sentence means “よい夜をお過ごしください。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “There seems to be some confusion.” does not fit because that sentence means “少し行き違いがあるようです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “This deal sounds fishy.” does not fit because that sentence means “この取引は何か怪しいです。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「What time will the event start?」（そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？）です。これからのイベントと時計の仕草が、開始時刻を尋ねています。 「Have a good evening.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「よい夜をお過ごしください。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「There seems to be some confusion.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「少し行き違いがあるようです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「This deal sounds fishy.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「この取引は何か怪しいです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"What time will the event start?","jp":"そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Have a good evening.","jp":"よい夜をお過ごしください。"},{"id":"c","en":"There seems to be some confusion.","jp":"少し行き違いがあるようです。"},{"id":"d","en":"This deal sounds fishy.","jp":"この取引は何か怪しいです。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-23-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"Someone asks when a future event will start.","visualAssetId":"august-23-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-23-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"confusion","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The problem is a shared misunderstanding, expressed as a noun.","hintJa":"問題は共有された行き違いで、名詞として表されています。","explanation":"“There seems to be some confusion.” is correct. The mismatched plans show confusion between the coworkers. “Thanks for taking care of that.” does not fit because that sentence means “対応してくれてありがとうございます。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “What time will the event start?” does not fit because that sentence means “そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Something feels off.” does not fit because that sentence means “何か違和感があります。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「There seems to be some confusion.」（少し行き違いがあるようです。）です。食い違う計画書が、同僚の間の混乱・行き違いを示しています。 「Thanks for taking care of that.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「対応してくれてありがとうございます。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「What time will the event start?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Something feels off.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「何か違和感があります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"There seems to be some confusion.","jp":"少し行き違いがあるようです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Thanks for taking care of that.","jp":"対応してくれてありがとうございます。"},{"id":"c","en":"What time will the event start?","jp":"そのイベントは何時に始まりますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"Something feels off.","jp":"何か違和感があります。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-23-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"Coworkers realize there has been a misunderstanding.","visualAssetId":"august-23-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-23', 'august-23-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-23-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"fishy","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The informal reaction is that the deal seems untrustworthy.","hintJa":"その取引が信用できず、うさんくさく感じられる反応です。","explanation":"“This deal sounds fishy.” is correct. Contradictory warning signs make the deal look clearly untrustworthy. “Thanks for your hard work today.” does not fit because that sentence means “今日はお疲れさまでした。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “What time does the store open?” does not fit because that sentence means “その店は何時に開店しますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context. “That message looks suspicious.” does not fit because that sentence means “そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「This deal sounds fishy.」（この取引は何か怪しいです。）です。矛盾する警告の手がかりが、取引のうさんくささを示しています。 「Thanks for your hard work today.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今日はお疲れさまでした。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「What time does the store open?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「その店は何時に開店しますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「That message looks suspicious.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"This deal sounds fishy.","jp":"この取引は何か怪しいです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Thanks for your hard work today.","jp":"今日はお疲れさまでした。"},{"id":"c","en":"What time does the store open?","jp":"その店は何時に開店しますか？"},{"id":"d","en":"That message looks suspicious.","jp":"そのメッセージは怪しく見えます。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-23-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A business deal feels suspicious.","visualAssetId":"august-23-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-24-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"dumplings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the dumplings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。”.","hintJa":"dumpling は皮で具を包む料理の広い呼び名です。","explanation":"“Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.” is the sentence that means “餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.」が「餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。","promptJa":"「餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.","jp":"餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Shumai are usually steamed.","jp":"焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。"},{"id":"c","en":"We both like gyoza.","jp":"私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"You must not touch this.","jp":"これに触れてはいけません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-24-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"cooking","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the cooking meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。”.","hintJa":"be steamed は「蒸される」という調理法です。","explanation":"“Shumai are usually steamed.” is the sentence that means “焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Shumai are usually steamed.」が「焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。","promptJa":"「焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Shumai are usually steamed.","jp":"焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。"},{"id":"b","en":"These dumplings are filled with pork.","jp":"このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。"},{"id":"c","en":"We are both hungry.","jp":"私たちは二人ともお腹が空いています。"},{"id":"d","en":"Do you know what I ate?","jp":"私が何を食べたか知っていますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-24-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"fillings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the fillings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。”.","hintJa":"be filled with で中身を説明します。","explanation":"“These dumplings are filled with pork.” is the sentence that means “このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「These dumplings are filled with pork.」が「このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。","promptJa":"「このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"These dumplings are filled with pork.","jp":"このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"We fried the gyoza until they were crispy.","jp":"餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。"},{"id":"c","en":"Both dishes look delicious.","jp":"どちらの料理もおいしそうです。"},{"id":"d","en":"Can you tell me where the restaurant is?","jp":"そのレストランがどこにあるか教えてもらえますか？"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-24-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"cooking","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the cooking meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。”.","hintJa":"until で仕上がりの状態を示します。","explanation":"“We fried the gyoza until they were crispy.” is the sentence that means “餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「We fried the gyoza until they were crispy.」が「餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。","promptJa":"「餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"We fried the gyoza until they were crispy.","jp":"餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。"},{"id":"b","en":"We both like gyoza.","jp":"私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。"},{"id":"c","en":"He must not be at home.","jp":"彼は家にいないに違いありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m feeling under the weather today.","jp":"今日は少し体調がよくありません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-24-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"both placement","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the both placement meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。”.","hintJa":"一般動詞の前に both を置きます。","explanation":"True. “We both like gyoza.” means “私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「We both like gyoza.」は「私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。」という意味です。","prompt":"“We both like gyoza.” means “私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。”.","promptJa":"「We both like gyoza.」は「私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-24-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"both placement","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the both placement meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私たちは二人ともお腹が空いています。”.","hintJa":"be動詞の後ろに both を置きます。","explanation":"False. “We are both hungry.” means “私たちは二人ともお腹が空いています。”, not “どちらの料理もおいしそうです。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「We are both hungry.」は「私たちは二人ともお腹が空いています。」であり、「どちらの料理もおいしそうです。」ではありません。","prompt":"“We are both hungry.” means “どちらの料理もおいしそうです。”.","promptJa":"「We are both hungry.」は「どちらの料理もおいしそうです。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-24-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"both placement","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the both placement meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “どちらの料理もおいしそうです。”.","hintJa":"名詞の前で both + 複数名詞を使えます。","explanation":"A natural translation is “Both dishes look delicious.”. It expresses “どちらの料理もおいしそうです。” with the lesson’s both placement pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「Both dishes look delicious.」です。「どちらの料理もおいしそうです。」を今回のboth placement表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: どちらの料理もおいしそうです。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：どちらの料理もおいしそうです。","accepted":["Both dishes look delicious."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-24-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"negative deduction","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the negative deduction meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “彼は家にいないに違いありません。”.","hintJa":"文脈によって must not が否定の推量を表します。","explanation":"A natural translation is “He must not be at home.”. It expresses “彼は家にいないに違いありません。” with the lesson’s negative deduction pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「He must not be at home.」です。「彼は家にいないに違いありません。」を今回のnegative deduction表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 彼は家にいないに違いありません。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：彼は家にいないに違いありません。","accepted":["He must not be at home."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-typing', 8, 'Build It', 'typing', '{"id":"august-24-draft-typing","format":"typing","type":"typing","section":"Build It","topic":"health","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the health meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今日は少し体調がよくありません。”.","hintJa":"under the weather は軽い体調不良を柔らかく表します。","explanation":"A complete model answer is “I’m feeling under the weather today.”. Check the key health expression and every short grammar word.","explanationJa":"完全な答えは「I’m feeling under the weather today.」です。healthの中心表現と短い文法語まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete English sentence from memory: 今日は少し体調がよくありません。","promptJa":"日本語を見て、英文を最後まで入力してください：今日は少し体調がよくありません。","accepted":["I’m feeling under the weather today."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-order-1', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-24-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"prohibition","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the prohibition meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “これに触れてはいけません。”.","hintJa":"人への指示では must not が強い禁止になります。","explanation":"Correct order: “You must not touch this.”. Build the sentence around the prohibition pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「You must not touch this.」です。prohibitionの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: これに触れてはいけません。","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：これに触れてはいけません。","words":["must","this","not","You","touch"],"correctWords":["You","must","not","touch","this"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-order-2', 10, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-24-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"indirect questions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the indirect questions meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私が何を食べたか知っていますか？”.","hintJa":"間接疑問では what の後を主語 + 動詞の語順にします。","explanation":"Correct order: “Do you know what I ate?”. Build the sentence around the indirect questions pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「Do you know what I ate?」です。indirect questionsの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 私が何を食べたか知っていますか？","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：私が何を食べたか知っていますか？","words":["what","I","ate","Do","you","know"],"correctWords":["Do","you","know","what","I","ate"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-matching', 11, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"august-24-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"dumplings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the dumplings meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。”.","hintJa":"dumpling は皮で具を包む料理の広い呼び名です。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.","jp":"餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。","cat":"dumplings"},{"en":"Shumai are usually steamed.","jp":"焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。","cat":"cooking"},{"en":"These dumplings are filled with pork.","jp":"このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。","cat":"fillings"},{"en":"We fried the gyoza until they were crispy.","jp":"餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。","cat":"cooking"},{"en":"We both like gyoza.","jp":"私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。","cat":"both placement"},{"en":"We are both hungry.","jp":"私たちは二人ともお腹が空いています。","cat":"both placement"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
