  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-24-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"indirect questions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the indirect questions meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “私が何を食べたか知っていますか？”.","hintJa":"間接疑問では what の後を主語 + 動詞の語順にします。","explanation":"“Do you know what I ate?” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「Do you know what I ate?」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: You must not touch this.\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: これに触れてはいけません。\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Do you know what I ate?","jp":"私が何を食べたか知っていますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Can you tell me where the restaurant is?","jp":"そのレストランがどこにあるか教えてもらえますか？"},{"id":"c","en":"Shumai are usually steamed.","jp":"焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。"},{"id":"d","en":"We are both hungry.","jp":"私たちは二人ともお腹が空いています。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
