  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-24-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"health","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the health meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今日は少し体調がよくありません。”.","hintJa":"under the weather は軽い体調不良を柔らかく表します。","explanation":"“I’m feeling under the weather today.” directly expresses “今日は少し体調がよくありません。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「I’m feeling under the weather today.」が「今日は少し体調がよくありません。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: 今日は少し体調がよくありません。","promptJa":"「今日は少し体調がよくありません。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m feeling under the weather today.","jp":"今日は少し体調がよくありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.","jp":"餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。"},{"id":"c","en":"We fried the gyoza until they were crispy.","jp":"餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。"},{"id":"d","en":"He must not be at home.","jp":"彼は家にいないに違いありません。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-24-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"dumplings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Identify the pleated Japanese dumplings with crisp browned bottoms.","hintJa":"ひだのある皮と香ばしく焼けた底を持つ日本式ダンプリングを見つけましょう。","explanation":"“Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.” is correct. The pleated, pan-fried dumplings are recognizable as Japanese-style gyoza. “Shumai are usually steamed.” does not fit because that sentence means “焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “We are both hungry.” does not fit because that sentence means “私たちは二人ともお腹が空いています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Do you know what I ate?” does not fit because that sentence means “私が何を食べたか知っていますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.」（餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。）です。ひだがあり焼かれたダンプリングが、日本式の餃子として分かります。 「Shumai are usually steamed.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「We are both hungry.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私たちは二人ともお腹が空いています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Do you know what I ate?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私が何を食べたか知っていますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.","jp":"餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。"},{"id":"b","en":"Shumai are usually steamed.","jp":"焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。"},{"id":"c","en":"We are both hungry.","jp":"私たちは二人ともお腹が空いています。"},{"id":"d","en":"Do you know what I ate?","jp":"私が何を食べたか知っていますか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-24-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A plate of Japanese-style gyoza dumplings.","visualAssetId":"august-24-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-24-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"fillings","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Look inside the dumpling to identify its filling.","hintJa":"ダンプリングの中を見て、何が詰められているか確認しましょう。","explanation":"“These dumplings are filled with pork.” is correct. The cut-open dumpling and preparation bowl clearly show pork filling. “Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.” does not fit because that sentence means “餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Both dishes look delicious.” does not fit because that sentence means “どちらの料理もおいしそうです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m feeling under the weather today.” does not fit because that sentence means “今日は少し体調がよくありません。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「These dumplings are filled with pork.」（このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。）です。切ったダンプリングと調理中のボウルが、豚肉の具をはっきり示しています。 「Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Both dishes look delicious.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「どちらの料理もおいしそうです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m feeling under the weather today.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今日は少し体調がよくありません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"These dumplings are filled with pork.","jp":"このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。"},{"id":"b","en":"Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.","jp":"餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。"},{"id":"c","en":"Both dishes look delicious.","jp":"どちらの料理もおいしそうです。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m feeling under the weather today.","jp":"今日は少し体調がよくありません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-24-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"Dumplings are filled with pork.","visualAssetId":"august-24-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-24-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"both placement","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Both members of the pair share the same preference.","hintJa":"二人とも同じ食べ物を好きだと示していることを見ましょう。","explanation":"“We both like gyoza.” is correct. Each of the two people chooses gyoza and reacts positively. “These dumplings are filled with pork.” does not fit because that sentence means “このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “He must not be at home.” does not fit because that sentence means “彼は家にいないに違いありません。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Can you tell me where the restaurant is?” does not fit because that sentence means “そのレストランがどこにあるか教えてもらえますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「We both like gyoza.」（私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。）です。二人がそれぞれ餃子を選び、好意的に反応しています。 「These dumplings are filled with pork.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「He must not be at home.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「彼は家にいないに違いありません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Can you tell me where the restaurant is?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「そのレストランがどこにあるか教えてもらえますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"We both like gyoza.","jp":"私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。"},{"id":"b","en":"These dumplings are filled with pork.","jp":"このダンプリングには豚肉が入っています。"},{"id":"c","en":"He must not be at home.","jp":"彼は家にいないに違いありません。"},{"id":"d","en":"Can you tell me where the restaurant is?","jp":"そのレストランがどこにあるか教えてもらえますか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-24-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"Two people both enjoy gyoza.","visualAssetId":"august-24-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-24-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"negative deduction","isOriginal":false,"hint":"This is a logical conclusion about absence, not a rule forbidding an action.","hintJa":"行動を禁止する規則ではなく、不在だという論理的な推測です。","explanation":"“He must not be at home.” is correct. The empty dark house and absent car support the conclusion that he is not home. “Shumai are usually steamed.” does not fit because that sentence means “焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “We both like gyoza.” does not fit because that sentence means “私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Do you know what I ate?” does not fit because that sentence means “私が何を食べたか知っていますか？,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「He must not be at home.」（彼は家にいないに違いありません。）です。暗く空の家と車がないことから、彼は家にいないと推測できます。 「Shumai are usually steamed.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「We both like gyoza.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Do you know what I ate?」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「私が何を食べたか知っていますか？」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"He must not be at home.","jp":"彼は家にいないに違いありません。"},{"id":"b","en":"Shumai are usually steamed.","jp":"焼売は通常、蒸して作ります。"},{"id":"c","en":"We both like gyoza.","jp":"私たちは二人とも餃子が好きです。"},{"id":"d","en":"Do you know what I ate?","jp":"私が何を食べたか知っていますか？"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-24-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"Clues show that a man must not be at home.","visualAssetId":"august-24-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-24', 'august-24-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-24-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"indirect questions","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The speaker uses a polite indirect question to ask for the restaurant’s location.","hintJa":"レストランの場所を、丁寧な間接疑問で尋ねる場面です。","explanation":"“Can you tell me where the restaurant is?” is correct. The restaurant picture, map and polite request show a question about where it is. “Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.” does not fit because that sentence means “餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “We fried the gyoza until they were crispy.” does not fit because that sentence means “餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “You must not touch this.” does not fit because that sentence means “これに触れてはいけません。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Can you tell me where the restaurant is?」（そのレストランがどこにあるか教えてもらえますか？）です。レストラン写真、地図、丁寧な依頼が、その場所を尋ねていることを示しています。 「Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「We fried the gyoza until they were crispy.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「You must not touch this.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「これに触れてはいけません。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Can you tell me where the restaurant is?","jp":"そのレストランがどこにあるか教えてもらえますか？"},{"id":"b","en":"Gyoza are Japanese-style dumplings.","jp":"餃子は日本式のダンプリングです。"},{"id":"c","en":"We fried the gyoza until they were crispy.","jp":"餃子をカリッとするまで焼きました。"},{"id":"d","en":"You must not touch this.","jp":"これに触れてはいけません。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-24-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A customer politely asks where a restaurant is.","visualAssetId":"august-24-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-choice-1', 0, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-25-draft-choice-1","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"coming home","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the coming home meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ただいま！”.","hintJa":"自宅に帰った時の自然な一言です。","explanation":"“I’m home!” is the sentence that means “ただいま！”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I’m home!」が「ただいま！」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: ただいま！","promptJa":"「ただいま！」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m home!","jp":"ただいま！"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m back.","jp":"戻りました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m off.","jp":"行ってきます。"},{"id":"d","en":"Take care!","jp":"気をつけてね！"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-choice-2', 1, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-25-draft-choice-2","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"coming back","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the coming back meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “戻りました。”.","hintJa":"家以外でも、元いた場所に戻った時に使えます。","explanation":"“I’m back.” is the sentence that means “戻りました。”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「I’m back.」が「戻りました。」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: 戻りました。","promptJa":"「戻りました。」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m back.","jp":"戻りました。"},{"id":"b","en":"Welcome home!","jp":"おかえりなさい！"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m heading out now.","jp":"今から出かけます。"},{"id":"d","en":"Have fun!","jp":"楽しんできてね！"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-choice-3', 2, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-25-draft-choice-3","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"welcome home","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the welcome home meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “おかえりなさい！”.","hintJa":"自宅へ帰ってきた人を迎える表現です。","explanation":"“Welcome home!” is the sentence that means “おかえりなさい！”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Welcome home!」が「おかえりなさい！」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: おかえりなさい！","promptJa":"「おかえりなさい！」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Welcome home!","jp":"おかえりなさい！"},{"id":"b","en":"Welcome back!","jp":"お戻りなさい！"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m heading to work.","jp":"仕事へ向かっています。"},{"id":"d","en":"Please pour the tea slowly.","jp":"お茶をゆっくり注いでください。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-choice-4', 3, 'Understand', 'mcq', '{"id":"august-25-draft-choice-4","format":"mcq","type":"mcq","section":"Understand","topic":"welcome back","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the welcome back meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “お戻りなさい！”.","hintJa":"職場や授業など、戻ってきた人にも使えます。","explanation":"“Welcome back!” is the sentence that means “お戻りなさい！”. Check the complete meaning before choosing.","explanationJa":"「Welcome back!」が「お戻りなさい！」を表す英文です。単語一つではなく文全体の意味で選びましょう。","prompt":"Choose the English sentence that means: お戻りなさい！","promptJa":"「お戻りなさい！」に合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Welcome back!","jp":"お戻りなさい！"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m off.","jp":"行ってきます。"},{"id":"c","en":"Have a good day!","jp":"よい一日を！"},{"id":"d","en":"The poor dog was left outside.","jp":"かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-true-false-1', 4, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-25-draft-true-false-1","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"heading out","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the heading out meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “行ってきます。”.","hintJa":"出発する時の短く自然な表現です。","explanation":"True. “I’m off.” means “行ってきます。”.","explanationJa":"正解はTrueです。「I’m off.」は「行ってきます。」という意味です。","prompt":"“I’m off.” means “行ってきます。”.","promptJa":"「I’m off.」は「行ってきます。」という意味です。","correct":true}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-true-false-2', 5, 'Understand', 'truefalse', '{"id":"august-25-draft-true-false-2","format":"truefalse","type":"truefalse","section":"Understand","topic":"heading out","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the heading out meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今から出かけます。”.","hintJa":"今まさに外出することを伝えます。","explanation":"False. “I’m heading out now.” means “今から出かけます。”, not “仕事へ向かっています。”.","explanationJa":"正解はFalseです。「I’m heading out now.」は「今から出かけます。」であり、「仕事へ向かっています。」ではありません。","prompt":"“I’m heading out now.” means “仕事へ向かっています。”.","promptJa":"「I’m heading out now.」は「仕事へ向かっています。」という意味です。","correct":false}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-typed-1', 6, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-25-draft-typed-1","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"destination","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the destination meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “仕事へ向かっています。”.","hintJa":"heading to + 場所で行き先を表します。","explanation":"A natural translation is “I’m heading to work.”. It expresses “仕事へ向かっています。” with the lesson’s destination pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「I’m heading to work.」です。「仕事へ向かっています。」を今回のdestination表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: 仕事へ向かっています。","promptJa":"英語にしてください：仕事へ向かっています。","accepted":["I’m heading to work."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-typed-2', 7, 'Build It', 'translation', '{"id":"august-25-draft-typed-2","format":"translation","type":"translation","section":"Build It","topic":"send-off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the send-off meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “よい一日を！”.","hintJa":"日中に相手を送り出す定番の挨拶です。","explanation":"A natural translation is “Have a good day!”. It expresses “よい一日を！” with the lesson’s send-off pattern.","explanationJa":"自然な英訳は「Have a good day!」です。「よい一日を！」を今回のsend-off表現で伝えています。","prompt":"Translate into English: よい一日を！","promptJa":"英語にしてください：よい一日を！","accepted":["Have a good day!"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-typing', 8, 'Build It', 'typing', '{"id":"august-25-draft-typing","format":"typing","type":"typing","section":"Build It","topic":"poor","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the poor meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。”.","hintJa":"poor /pʊr/ または /pɔːr/ は「貧しい・かわいそうな」です。文脈で区別します。","explanation":"A complete model answer is “The poor dog was left outside.”. Check the key poor expression and every short grammar word.","explanationJa":"完全な答えは「The poor dog was left outside.」です。poorの中心表現と短い文法語まで確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete English sentence from memory: かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。","promptJa":"日本語を見て、英文を最後まで入力してください：かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。","accepted":["The poor dog was left outside."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-order-1', 9, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-25-draft-order-1","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"send-off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the send-off meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “気をつけてね！”.","hintJa":"安全や体調を気づかう幅広い別れの言葉です。","explanation":"Correct order: “Take care!”. Build the sentence around the send-off pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「Take care!」です。send-offの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 気をつけてね！","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：気をつけてね！","words":["care","Take"],"correctWords":["Take","care"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-order-2', 10, 'Build It', 'order', '{"id":"august-25-draft-order-2","format":"order","type":"order","section":"Build It","topic":"send-off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the send-off meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “楽しんできてね！”.","hintJa":"楽しい予定へ出かける人に使います。","explanation":"Correct order: “Have fun!”. Build the sentence around the send-off pattern.","explanationJa":"正しい語順は「Have fun!」です。send-offの形を中心に文を組み立てます。","prompt":"Put the words in order: 楽しんできてね！","promptJa":"語順を並べましょう：楽しんできてね！","words":["fun","Have"],"correctWords":["Have","fun"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-matching', 11, 'Build It', 'matching', '{"id":"august-25-draft-matching","format":"matching","type":"matching","section":"Build It","topic":"coming home","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the coming home meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ただいま！”.","hintJa":"自宅に帰った時の自然な一言です。","explanation":"Each English phrase has exactly one Japanese meaning. Match the whole message rather than isolated words.","explanationJa":"各英文に対応する日本語は一つです。単語だけではなく、表現全体の意味で組み合わせましょう。","prompt":"Match the English and Japanese.","promptJa":"英語と日本語を組み合わせてください。","pairs":[{"en":"I’m home!","jp":"ただいま！","cat":"coming home"},{"en":"I’m back.","jp":"戻りました。","cat":"coming back"},{"en":"Welcome home!","jp":"おかえりなさい！","cat":"welcome home"},{"en":"Welcome back!","jp":"お戻りなさい！","cat":"welcome back"},{"en":"I’m off.","jp":"行ってきます。","cat":"heading out"},{"en":"I’m heading out now.","jp":"今から出かけます。","cat":"heading out"}]}'::jsonb, false, 6),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-sorting', 12, 'Build It', 'sorting', '{"id":"august-25-draft-sorting","format":"sorting","type":"sorting","section":"Build It","topic":"coming back","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the coming back meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “戻りました。”.","hintJa":"家以外でも、元いた場所に戻った時に使えます。","explanation":"Sort by the purpose of the complete phrase. The available topics are coming home, coming back, welcome home.","explanationJa":"英文全体の目的で分類します。今回の分類は「coming home・coming back・welcome home」です。","prompt":"Sort the phrases by topic.","promptJa":"表現をトピック別に分類してください。","categories":["coming home","coming back","welcome home"],"items":[["I’m home!","coming home"],["I’m back.","coming back"],["Welcome home!","welcome home"]]}'::jsonb, false, 3),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-grid', 13, 'Build It', 'grid', '{"id":"august-25-draft-grid","format":"grid","type":"grid","section":"Build It","topic":"heading out","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the heading out meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “行ってきます。”.","hintJa":"出発する時の短く自然な表現です。","explanation":"The center tile, “I’m off.”, means “行ってきます。”. Read every complete phrase before choosing its position.","explanationJa":"中央の「I’m off.」が「行ってきます。」を表します。位置だけでなく、各英文の意味を最後まで読んで選びましょう。","prompt":"Select the tile that means: 行ってきます。","promptJa":"「行ってきます。」を表す英文のタイルを選んでください。","correctCell":"center","gridCells":{"top-left":"I’m home!","top-center":"I’m back.","top-right":"Welcome home!","middle-left":"Welcome back!","center":"I’m off.","middle-right":"I’m heading out now.","bottom-left":"I’m heading to work.","bottom-center":"Have a good day!","bottom-right":"Take care!"}}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-listen-choice-1', 14, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-25-draft-listen-choice-1","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"coming home","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the coming home meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “ただいま！”.","hintJa":"自宅に帰った時の自然な一言です。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “I’m home!”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「I’m home!」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"I’m home!","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m home!","jp":"ただいま！"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m back.","jp":"戻りました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m off.","jp":"行ってきます。"},{"id":"d","en":"Take care!","jp":"気をつけてね！"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-listen-choice-2', 15, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-25-draft-listen-choice-2","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"welcome back","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the welcome back meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “お戻りなさい！”.","hintJa":"職場や授業など、戻ってきた人にも使えます。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “Welcome back!”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「Welcome back!」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"Welcome back!","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Welcome back!","jp":"お戻りなさい！"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m off.","jp":"行ってきます。"},{"id":"c","en":"Have a good day!","jp":"よい一日を！"},{"id":"d","en":"The poor dog was left outside.","jp":"かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-listen-choice-3', 16, 'Listen', 'listenChoice', '{"id":"august-25-draft-listen-choice-3","format":"listenChoice","type":"listenChoice","section":"Listen","topic":"destination","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the destination meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “仕事へ向かっています。”.","hintJa":"heading to + 場所で行き先を表します。","explanation":"The sentence in the audio is “I’m heading to work.”. Listen through to the end before choosing.","explanationJa":"音声の英文は「I’m heading to work.」です。最後まで聞いてから選びましょう。","prompt":"Listen and choose the sentence.","promptJa":"音声を聞いて英文を選んでください。","audioText":"I’m heading to work.","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m heading to work.","jp":"仕事へ向かっています。"},{"id":"b","en":"Have a good day!","jp":"よい一日を！"},{"id":"c","en":"Please pour the tea slowly.","jp":"お茶をゆっくり注いでください。"},{"id":"d","en":"Welcome home!","jp":"おかえりなさい！"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-dictation-1', 17, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-25-draft-dictation-1","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"coming back","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the coming back meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “戻りました。”.","hintJa":"家以外でも、元いた場所に戻った時に使えます。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “I’m back.”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「I’m back.」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"I’m back.","accepted":["I’m back."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-dictation-2', 18, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-25-draft-dictation-2","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"heading out","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the heading out meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “行ってきます。”.","hintJa":"出発する時の短く自然な表現です。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “I’m off.”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「I’m off.」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"I’m off.","accepted":["I’m off."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-dictation-3', 19, 'Listen', 'listenType', '{"id":"august-25-draft-dictation-3","format":"listenType","type":"listenType","section":"Listen","topic":"send-off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the send-off meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “よい一日を！”.","hintJa":"日中に相手を送り出す定番の挨拶です。","explanation":"The complete sentence is “Have a good day!”. Check every small word as well as the main vocabulary.","explanationJa":"全文は「Have a good day!」です。中心の単語だけでなく、短い機能語も確認しましょう。","prompt":"Type the complete sentence you hear.","promptJa":"聞こえた英文を入力してください。","audioText":"Have a good day!","accepted":["Have a good day!"]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-speaking-1', 20, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-25-draft-speaking-1","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"welcome home","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the welcome home meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “おかえりなさい！”.","hintJa":"自宅へ帰ってきた人を迎える表現です。","explanation":"Model: “Welcome home!” (おかえりなさい！). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Welcome home!」（おかえりなさい！）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"Welcome home!","speakJa":"おかえりなさい！"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-speaking-2', 21, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-25-draft-speaking-2","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"heading out","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the heading out meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “今から出かけます。”.","hintJa":"今まさに外出することを伝えます。","explanation":"Model: “I’m heading out now.” (今から出かけます。). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「I’m heading out now.」（今から出かけます。）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"I’m heading out now.","speakJa":"今から出かけます。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-speaking-3', 22, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-25-draft-speaking-3","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"send-off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the send-off meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “気をつけてね！”.","hintJa":"安全や体調を気づかう幅広い別れの言葉です。","explanation":"Model: “Take care!” (気をつけてね！). Say it as one connected message, then compare with the model.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Take care!」（気をつけてね！）です。一つの意味のまとまりとして話し、お手本と比べましょう。","prompt":"Listen, then speak.","promptJa":"聞いてから話してみましょう。","speakText":"Take care!","speakJa":"気をつけてね！"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-speaking-4', 23, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-25-draft-speaking-4","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"send-off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the send-off meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “楽しんできてね！”.","hintJa":"楽しい予定へ出かける人に使います。","explanation":"Model: “Have fun!” (楽しんできてね！). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Have fun!」（楽しんできてね！）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Have fun!","speakJa":"楽しんできてね！"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-speaking-5', 24, 'Speak', 'speaking', '{"id":"august-25-draft-speaking-5","format":"speaking","type":"speaking","section":"Speak","topic":"pour","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the pour meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “お茶をゆっくり注いでください。”.","hintJa":"pour /pɔːr/ は液体を注ぐ動詞です。","explanation":"Model: “Please pour the tea slowly.” (お茶をゆっくり注いでください。). The second attempt checks whether you can recall the whole phrase independently.","explanationJa":"お手本は「Please pour the tea slowly.」（お茶をゆっくり注いでください。）です。2回目は英文を見ずに、表現全体を思い出せるか確認します。","prompt":"Say the sentence naturally, then try it once without looking.","promptJa":"自然に言ってから、英文を見ずにもう一度話してみましょう。","speakText":"Please pour the tea slowly.","speakJa":"お茶をゆっくり注いでください。"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-dialogue', 25, 'Use It', 'dialogue', '{"id":"august-25-draft-dialogue","format":"dialogue","type":"dialogue","section":"Use It","topic":"send-off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the send-off meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “楽しんできてね！”.","hintJa":"楽しい予定へ出かける人に使います。","explanation":"“Have fun!” answers the previous speaker directly and keeps the conversation coherent.","explanationJa":"「Have fun!」は直前の発言に直接答え、会話の流れが自然につながります。","prompt":"Choose the most natural next line.","promptJa":"会話の次の一文を選んでください。","context":"A: Take care!\nB: ...","contextJa":"A: 気をつけてね！\nB: …","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Have fun!","jp":"楽しんできてね！"},{"id":"b","en":"Please pour the tea slowly.","jp":"お茶をゆっくり注いでください。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m back.","jp":"戻りました。"},{"id":"d","en":"I’m heading out now.","jp":"今から出かけます。"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-mistake', 26, 'Use It', 'mistake', '{"id":"august-25-draft-mistake","format":"mistake","type":"mistake","section":"Use It","topic":"pour","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the pour meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “お茶をゆっくり注いでください。”.","hintJa":"pour /pɔːr/ は液体を注ぐ動詞です。","explanation":"Correct sentence: “Please pour the tea slowly.”. Compare it with the incorrect version and restore the missing or incorrect grammar word.","explanationJa":"正しい英文は「Please pour the tea slowly.」です。誤文と比べ、抜けた語や誤った文法部分を直しましょう。","prompt":"Correct the sentence.","promptJa":"英文を自然な形に直してください。","wrongSentence":"Please pour tea slowly.","accepted":["Please pour the tea slowly."]}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-situation', 27, 'Use It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-25-draft-situation","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"Use It","topic":"poor","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the poor meaning. Look for the sentence that expresses “かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。”.","hintJa":"poor /pʊr/ または /pɔːr/ は「貧しい・かわいそうな」です。文脈で区別します。","explanation":"“The poor dog was left outside.” directly expresses “かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。”. The other choices answer different situations.","explanationJa":"「The poor dog was left outside.」が「かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。」を直接表します。他の選択肢は別の場面に使う表現です。","prompt":"Which sentence would you use when you want to say: かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。","promptJa":"「かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。」と言いたい時、どの英文を使いますか？","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"The poor dog was left outside.","jp":"かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m home!","jp":"ただいま！"},{"id":"c","en":"Welcome back!","jp":"お戻りなさい！"},{"id":"d","en":"Have a good day!","jp":"よい一日を！"}],"correct":"a"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-visual-1', 28, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-25-draft-visual-1","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"coming home","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The speaker has arrived at their own home.","hintJa":"話し手が自分の家に到着して、中へ声をかけています。","explanation":"“I’m home!” is correct. The person enters their home and announces the arrival to family. “I’m back.” does not fit because that sentence means “戻りました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m heading out now.” does not fit because that sentence means “今から出かけます。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Have fun!” does not fit because that sentence means “楽しんできてね！,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I’m home!」（ただいま！）です。本人が自宅へ入り、家族に帰宅を知らせています。 「I’m back.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「戻りました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m heading out now.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「今から出かけます。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Have fun!」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「楽しんできてね！」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m home!","jp":"ただいま！"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m back.","jp":"戻りました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m heading out now.","jp":"今から出かけます。"},{"id":"d","en":"Have fun!","jp":"楽しんできてね！"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-25-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":1,"imageAlt":"A family member announces that they are home.","visualAssetId":"august-25-01"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-visual-2', 29, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-25-draft-visual-2","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"welcome home","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The people inside are greeting someone who has returned home.","hintJa":"家の中の人が、帰宅した人を迎えている場面です。","explanation":"“Welcome home!” is correct. The family welcomes the returning person at the home doorway. “I’m home!” does not fit because that sentence means “ただいま！,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m heading to work.” does not fit because that sentence means “仕事へ向かっています。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “The poor dog was left outside.” does not fit because that sentence means “かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Welcome home!」（おかえりなさい！）です。家族が玄関で、帰ってきた人を温かく迎えています。 「I’m home!」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「ただいま！」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m heading to work.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「仕事へ向かっています。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「The poor dog was left outside.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Welcome home!","jp":"おかえりなさい！"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m home!","jp":"ただいま！"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m heading to work.","jp":"仕事へ向かっています。"},{"id":"d","en":"The poor dog was left outside.","jp":"かわいそうな犬が外に置き去りにされました。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-25-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":2,"imageAlt":"A family warmly welcomes someone home.","visualAssetId":"august-25-02"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-visual-3', 30, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-25-draft-visual-3","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"heading out","isOriginal":false,"hint":"The speaker is leaving now, not arriving or already traveling.","hintJa":"到着ではなく、今まさに出発する人の一言を考えましょう。","explanation":"“I’m off.” is correct. Shoes, bag and the wave at the door show immediate departure. “Welcome home!” does not fit because that sentence means “おかえりなさい！,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Have a good day!” does not fit because that sentence means “よい一日を！,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Please pour the tea slowly.” does not fit because that sentence means “お茶をゆっくり注いでください。,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「I’m off.」（行ってきます。）です。靴、鞄、玄関での手振りが、今からの出発を示しています。 「Welcome home!」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「おかえりなさい！」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Have a good day!」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「よい一日を！」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Please pour the tea slowly.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「お茶をゆっくり注いでください。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"I’m off.","jp":"行ってきます。"},{"id":"b","en":"Welcome home!","jp":"おかえりなさい！"},{"id":"c","en":"Have a good day!","jp":"よい一日を！"},{"id":"d","en":"Please pour the tea slowly.","jp":"お茶をゆっくり注いでください。"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-25-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":3,"imageAlt":"A person announces that they are leaving.","visualAssetId":"august-25-03"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-visual-4', 31, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-25-draft-visual-4","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"send-off","isOriginal":false,"hint":"This is a friendly daytime send-off.","hintJa":"日中に出かける人へ送る、親しい挨拶です。","explanation":"“Have a good day!” is correct. Morning light and the warm farewell show a wish for a good day. “I’m back.” does not fit because that sentence means “戻りました。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “I’m off.” does not fit because that sentence means “行ってきます。,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Have fun!” does not fit because that sentence means “楽しんできてね！,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Have a good day!」（よい一日を！）です。朝の光と温かい見送りが、よい一日を願う挨拶を示しています。 「I’m back.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「戻りました。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「I’m off.」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「行ってきます。」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Have fun!」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「楽しんできてね！」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Have a good day!","jp":"よい一日を！"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m back.","jp":"戻りました。"},{"id":"c","en":"I’m off.","jp":"行ってきます。"},{"id":"d","en":"Have fun!","jp":"楽しんできてね！"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-25-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":4,"imageAlt":"Someone wishes a departing person a good day.","visualAssetId":"august-25-04"}'::jsonb, false, 1),
  ('august-25', 'august-25-draft-visual-5', 32, 'See It', 'situation', '{"id":"august-25-draft-visual-5","format":"situation","type":"situation","section":"See It","topic":"pour","isOriginal":false,"hint":"Focus on the controlled liquid action and its slow speed.","hintJa":"液体を意図的に注ぐ動作と、ゆっくりした速さに注目しましょう。","explanation":"“Please pour the tea slowly.” is correct. The teapot sends a slow controlled stream directly into the cup. “I’m home!” does not fit because that sentence means “ただいま！,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Welcome back!” does not fit because that sentence means “お戻りなさい！,” which is different from the visible action and context. “Take care!” does not fit because that sentence means “気をつけてね！,” which is different from the visible action and context.","explanationJa":"正解は「Please pour the tea slowly.」（お茶をゆっくり注いでください。）です。ティーポットからカップへ、ゆっくり制御された流れでお茶を注いでいます。 「I’m home!」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「ただいま！」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Welcome back!」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「お戻りなさい！」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。 「Take care!」はこの場面とは一致しません。その英文は「気をつけてね！」という意味で、絵に見える動作・状況とは異なります。","prompt":"Which sentence best matches the illustration?","promptJa":"イラストの場面に最も合う英文を選んでください。","choices":[{"id":"a","en":"Please pour the tea slowly.","jp":"お茶をゆっくり注いでください。"},{"id":"b","en":"I’m home!","jp":"ただいま！"},{"id":"c","en":"Welcome back!","jp":"お戻りなさい！"},{"id":"d","en":"Take care!","jp":"気をつけてね！"}],"correct":"a","image":"/assets/questions/visual/august-25-storyboard.webp","imagePanel":5,"imageAlt":"A person slowly pours tea into a cup.","visualAssetId":"august-25-05"}'::jsonb, false, 1);
